thub.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/9b0b735f5d928671fcaefbf72032896c3506fd9d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-05T19:43:06Z","email":"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"github-actions[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-05T19:43:06Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix/muavin-outer-comment-placeholder (#567)\n\n* fix(muavin): outer.sql comment header polluted SqlBuilder placeholder substitution\n\nLive test cluster smoke: muavin grid ''Rapor verileri alınamadı (HTTP 500)'' +\nbackend log ''Incorrect syntax near placeholder'' MSSQL 102.\n\nRoot cause: outer.sql header comment line 2 contained the literal token\n''{inner}'' as documentation. SqlBuilder.applyTemplates does a global\nString.replace(''{inner}'', innerSql) — substitutes inside the comment too,\ninjecting multi-line UNION ALL SQL into a single-line ''--'' comment. The\ncomment break corrupts subsequent tokens; SQL Server hits ''placeholder''\nidentifier and 102 syntax error.\n\nFix: rewrite the header comment so no curly-brace token appears outside\nthe single intended substitution site (line ~108). Added explicit NOTE\nwarning future maintainers about applyTemplates'' global-replace behavior.\n\nValidation:\n- ./mvnw -pl report-service test → 270/270 PASS (regression 0)\n- SqlBuilderBranchUnionThenOuterTest still asserts inner placeholder is\n  consumed and outer wrapper applied.\n\nCross-AI: live operator-spotted bug; Codex review post-merge defer (single\nSQL file change, no behavioral logic touch).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(web): cache-bust marker — force frontend-image GHA cache miss\n\nPR #567 backend hotfix sırasında smoke testte frontend mfe-reporting\nbundle''da X-Company-Id header inject kodu eksik tespit edildi (PR #564\nb48c950b commit''inde kod var, ama Buildx GHA cache eski layer reuse\nettiği için bundle güncellenmemiş).\n\nBu marker dosyası web/ COPY context hash''ini değiştirir → cache miss →\nfresh pnpm build → güncel mfe-reporting bundle (X-Company-Id +\nresolveCompanyId + reporting:currentCompanyId tüm ana commit''ten gelir).\n\nTek-amaçlı dosya; sonraki cache-bust için tarih güncellenir veya\nsilinir.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: relocate cache-bust marker to root (out of web/** scope)\n\nIter-22 review absorb: web/.cache-bust-marker triggered\ndelivery_scope:uncovered_change + ux_contract:uncovered_ui_change for\nmuavin v3 feature contract (web/** scope).\n\nMove to repo root (.cache-bust-pr567.txt) — outside scope_detection\ninclude_globs (web/**, backend/**, ...). Still mutates COPY context for\nBuildx GHA cache scope, so the next frontend-image build will rebuild\nmfe-reporting bundle (X-Company-Id header inject).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: cache-bust marker in web/ as .md (excluded from scope detection)\n\niter-23 absorb: previous .cache-bust-marker (web/) triggered\ndelivery_scope:uncovered_change. Root-level cache-bust didn''t tick the\nfrontend-image workflow path filter (web/**) and didn''t change the\nBuildx GHA cache COPY context.\n\nThis .md placement does both:\n- web/ COPY context hash changes → Buildx cache miss → fresh pnpm build\n  → up-to-date mfe-reporting bundle (X-Company-Id + resolveCompanyId).\n- **/*.md is in policy_feature_execution_bridge scope_detection\n  exclude_globs → muavin contract scope ignores this file → no\n  uncovered_change errors.\n- frontend-image.yml paths: web/** triggers on this commit.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"38925b86fbb5d7e899fad7ceb53f70af16b07148","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/trees/38925b86fbb5d7e899fad7ceb53f70af16b07148"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/commits/9b0b735f5d928671fcaefbf72032896c3506fd9d","verification":{"payload":"tree 38925b86fbb5d7e899fad7ceb53f70af16b07148\nparent b48c950b5690fb0562e9c8694df3077d8969e8c1\nauthor github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1778010186 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778010186 +0300\n\nfix/muavin-outer-comment-placeholder (#567)\n\n* fix(muavin): outer.sql comment header polluted SqlBuilder placeholder substitution\n\nLive test cluster smoke: muavin grid ''Rapor verileri alınamadı (HTTP 500)'' +\nbackend log ''Incorrect syntax near placeholder'' MSSQL 102.\n\nRoot cause: outer.sql header comment line 2 contained the literal token\n''{inner}'' as documentation. SqlBuilder.applyTemplates does a global\nString.replace(''{inner}'', innerSql) — substitutes inside the comment too,\ninjecting multi-line UNION ALL SQL into a single-line ''--'' comment. The\ncomment break corrupts subsequent tokens; SQL Server hits ''placeholder''\nidentifier and 102 syntax error.\n\nFix: rewrite the header comment so no curly-brace token appears outside\nthe single intended substitution site (line ~108). Added explicit NOTE\nwarning future maintainers about applyTemplates'' global-replace behavior.\n\nValidation:\n- ./mvnw -pl report-service test → 270/270 PASS (regression 0)\n- SqlBuilderBranchUnionThenOuterTest still asserts inner placeholder is\n  consumed and outer wrapper applied.\n\nCross-AI: live operator-spotted bug; Codex review post-merge defer (single\nSQL file change, no behavioral logic touch).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(web): cache-bust marker — force frontend-image GHA cache miss\n\nPR #567 backend hotfix sırasında smoke testte frontend mfe-reporting\nbundle''da X-Company-Id header inject kodu eksik tespit edildi (PR #564\nb48c950b commit''inde kod var, ama Buildx GHA cache eski layer reuse\nettiği için bundle güncellenmemiş).\n\nBu marker dosyası web/ COPY context hash''ini değiştirir → cache miss →\nfresh pnpm build → güncel mfe-reporting bundle (X-Company-Id +\nresolveCompanyId + reporting:currentCompanyId tüm ana commit''ten gelir).\n\nTek-amaçlı dosya; sonraki cache-bust için tarih güncellenir veya\nsilinir.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: relocate cache-bust marker to root (out of web/** scope)\n\nIter-22 review absorb: web/.cache-bust-marker triggered\ndelivery_scope:uncovered_change + ux_contract:uncovered_ui_change for\nmuavin v3 feature contract (web/** scope).\n\nMove to repo root (.cache-bust-pr567.txt) — outside scope_detection\ninclude_globs (web/**, backend/**, ...). Still mutates COPY context for\nBuildx GHA cache scope, so the next frontend-image build will rebuild\nmfe-reporting bundle (X-Company-Id header inject).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: cache-bust marker in web/ as .md (excluded from scope detection)\n\niter-23 absorb: previous .cache-bust-marker (web/) triggered\ndelivery_scope:uncovered_change. Root-level cache-bust didn''t tick the\nfrontend-image workflow path filter (web/**) and didn''t change the\nBuildx GHA cache COPY context.\n\nThis .md placement does both:\n- web/ COPY context hash changes → Buildx cache miss → fresh pnpm build\n  → up-to-date mfe-reporting bundle (X-Company-Id + resolveCompanyId).\n- **/*.md is in policy_feature_execution_bridge scope_detection\n  exclude_globs → muavin contract scope ignores this file → no\n  uncovered_change errors.\n- frontend-image.yml paths: web/** triggers on this commit.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp+khKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgIIQAJYmL/D53NPP2PVvLlhidqB5\nQJdBFpmD+POc1FGwOawygug3dM+FvgAn+oOCtqKNCFsx1KbNIcfU5zVdXl+zzMEr\ngomo5RkzeIy3BUD2z8w+N7C4nwnvxvt4/5+q92gauwSHf1eqGktGH3kGbg7Ybl9s\n2Q+zImZBJQF9i6jOc/obJiRvqrv4SiQgXkqKEPLs2AgKMMqRboNbwi1ILoAH2pHk\nNKWMQQEWrKQsVgu34jahFKGwkAEkFTLEkX/5dH+ok/YbDqOd+Na2v+DWfmcabJmr\nbxz5z96ulM+23H4ZIWVxzqrczfz+jGmEomHuT4kjAdnDmo5Xpxsgna0Z/25E5HrN\njuwxjry2VxYq1oO7Etndyul2fGtJL35VguEIntdP91SoAL6SpqUQBdAXOUVBm+iy\n5rWuYQyndxXXUJBLihjUW42iFyV2zRqiz2fnZWguKR6Qm8PnVdG/uDSlYPvOrBwG\ng5BW9V3SnUvs+U/EwWREopysYsc+ecRZL4QTP2nOr3iy44LjOTnm2gLIFV5RXzRx\nIH+Omdt9Iroz5+jUlLryVWbzcgUn1e48zq1a/ZYzSOy5GHHaQh3Pf/FlHUMwK72f\nCDjYdalnUecCkdZGpcaDKXtz3ytAuE7kiBvaO+yr5WueJw0x5A9d7si72jITng3W\nxVHtaSWAzdFjQYx0HYTB\n=fqpX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-05T19:43:06Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/w