ttps://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/8b9eea01c495d8f9b3e9b2d188fda4d16ebcb977"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186576227?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/b445ba961c0f889b80d46599f2535412fe8a724c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-05T09:05:31Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"Halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-05T09:05:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(report-service): muavin v3 — file-based SQL + 8-katman EUR fallback (Codex 019df4ed AGREE) (#561)\n\n* feat(report-service): foundation — file-based SQL + hidden/exportOnly columns\n\nCodex thread 019df4ed iter-4 absorb (AGREE + 3 revizyon).\n\nColumnDefinition:\n- hidden(boolean default false) — UI grid''de görünmez\n- exportOnly(boolean default false) — sadece CSV/Excel export''a girer\n- 5-arg backward-compat constructor (eski JSON''lar etkilenmez)\n\nReportDefinition:\n- sourceQueryFile (opsiyonel) — classpath:reports/sql/<file>.sql ref\n  Avoid 6000+ char escaped string in JSON\n- outerQueryFile (opsiyonel) — post-union projection/window wrapper\n- queryShape (enum-like string) — \"BRANCH_UNION_THEN_OUTER\" multi-year global\n  running balance (muavin) için\n\nReportRegistry:\n- hydrateSqlFiles() — SQL files classpath''ten yüklenir, UNSAFE_SQL filter\n  uygulanır\n- validateSqlFilePath() — path traversal reject (no .., absolute, or scheme;\n  must match ^sql/<filename>.sql$)\n- getEffectiveSourceQuery() / getEffectiveOuterQuery() — hydrated content\n  cache''lenmiş döner\n\nRefs:\n- Codex thread 019df4ed-615c-73d1-b67a-7d0b61cc94df (AGREE iter-4)\n- Spec: ~/Documents/platform-k8s-gitops/.../docs/reports/muavin-grid-spec.md\n- gitops PR #360 e5efda3\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(report-service): schema resolver + SqlBuilder — companySchema + BRANCH_UNION_THEN_OUTER\n\nCodex thread 019df4ed iter-4 absorb (AGREE).\n\nYearlySchemaResolver:\n- ResolvedSchemas record extended: schemas + companySchema (nullable)\n- Backward-compat 1-arg constructor preserved\n- resolve() now also resolves company-only schema\n  \"workcube_mikrolink_{companyId}\" when single COMPANY scope\n- Multi-company scope → companySchema null (ambiguous; reports requiring\n  company schema must restrict scope further)\n\nSqlBuilder:\n- New hydrated overloads: buildDataQuery/buildCountQuery/buildExportQuery\n  with effectiveSourceQuery + effectiveOuterQuery params (caller passes\n  hydrated SQL from ReportRegistry)\n- {schema} + {companySchema} placeholder replacement (applyTemplates helper)\n- BRANCH_UNION_THEN_OUTER queryShape: raw multi-year UNION ALL inside outer\n  wrapper with {inner} placeholder; filter pushdown DISABLED so window\n  function sees full row set; AG Grid filters applied at outer wrapper\n  WHERE clause\n- Backward-compat 8-arg + 10-arg overloads preserved (no caller break)\n\nReportDefinition:\n- Backward-compat 14-arg constructor for programmatic callers\n  (DashboardQueryEngine etc.) — defaults sourceQueryFile/outerQueryFile/\n  queryShape to null\n\nRefs:\n- Codex thread 019df4ed-615c-73d1-b67a-7d0b61cc94df (AGREE iter-4)\n- Spec: ~/Documents/platform-k8s-gitops/.../docs/reports/muavin-grid-spec.md\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(report-service): muavin v3 — fin-muhasebe-detay JSON + branch.sql + outer.sql\n\nCodex thread 019df4ed iter-4 absorb (AGREE).\n\nfin-muhasebe-detay.json (v3.0):\n- sourceQueryFile + outerQueryFile + queryShape: BRANCH_UNION_THEN_OUTER\n- 32 columns: 26 visible (12 boyut + 4 TL + 4 USD + 5 EUR + 1 audit)\n  + 6 hidden audit (kur_tarihi/kur_id/kur_yas_gun/is_opening_document\n  exportOnly + card_row_id/action_id debug-only)\n- access.rowFilter REMOVED — Codex iter-4 önerisi: ACC_COMPANY_ID\n  cari boyutudur, OUR_COMPANY schema selection authz scope üzerinden\n  resolver''da yapılır\n\nsql/fin-muhasebe-detay.branch.sql (per-yıl branch, 247 satır):\n- {schema} + {companySchema} + {companyId} placeholder\n- 8-katman EUR fallback OUTER APPLY:\n  L1 ACM by CARD_ID (RATE2 — RATE1 dummy=1.0!)\n  L2 ACM by ACTION_ID cascade\n  L3 POOL: 13 *_MONEY (yıl×şirket + 2 şirket-only) inline UNION ALL\n     dispatched via MONEY_TABLES.ACTION_TYPE → ACTION_TABLE\n  L5 MH same-day company (RATE2)\n  L6 MH same-day GLOBAL (Codex order: same-day-global > prev-day-company)\n  L7 MH ≤7d prev company\n  L8 MH ≤7d prev GLOBAL\n- Pipe-delimited audit string (ACM/POOL/MH/MISSING)\n- Decimal cast SQL-side (float aggregation artefact engelleme)\n- IS_CANCEL=0 filter (iptal fişler dışlanır)\n- ACCOUNT_CARD_DOCUMENT_TYPES + OUR_COMPANY_ID = {companyId} match (canonical\n  şirket-bazlı lookup; SETUP_DOCUMENT_TYPE açılış için primary değil)\n\nsql/fin-muhasebe-detay.outer.sql (window wrapper, 106 satır):\n- {inner} placeholder (SqlBuilder branch UNION ALL''la doldurur)\n- Window functions: SUM(signed_*) OVER (PARTITION BY account_code\n  ORDER BY action_date, card_id, card_row_id ROWS UNBOUNDED PRECEDING)\n- TL/USD/EUR ayrı: borc/alacak/net/bakiye\n- COALESCE kur_kaynagi → MISSING|EUR_RATE_NOT_FOUND\n- Multi-year global running balance (Codex tezi: filter pushdown YOK,\n  outer WHERE''de uygulanır; bakiye filtreden önce hesaplanır)\n\nSqlBuilder.applyTemplates: {companyId} support eklendi\n- companySchema''dan numeric id parse (\"workcube_mikrolink_35\" → \"35\")\n- Yoksa \"0\" (no-match, fallback path''a düşer)\n\nTest: ReportRegistryTest 31 reports (fin-muhasebe-detay v3 dahil) load PASS\n\nRefs:\n- Codex thread 019df4ed-615c-73d1-b67a-7d0b61cc94df (AGREE iter-4)\n- gitops PR #360 e5efda3 spec doc\n- Live validation 5 kategori production MSSQL workcube_mikrolink\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(gitignore): anchor reports/ to root + add muavin SQL files\n\nCodex iter-4 absorb follow-up. Previous Commit 0d814a3e shipped\nfin-muhasebe-detay.json v3.0 referencing sourceQueryFile/outerQueryFile,\nbut the SQL files (sql/fin-muhasebe-detay.branch.sql,\nsql/fin-muhasebe-detay.outer.sql) were silently blocked by the root-level\n.gitignore \"reports/\" pattern (intended for observability artifacts).\n\nFix: anchor pattern to \"/reports/\" so it matches only repo-root, leaving\nnested checked-in reports/ directories (notably\nbackend/report-service/src/main/resources/reports/) untouched.\n\nPlus: add the two SQL files (247 + 106 lines) — branch + outer wrapper for\nmuavin v3 multi-year global running balance.\n\nWithout this commit ReportRegistry would NPE on hydrateSqlFiles for\nfin-muhasebe-detay (file missing on classpath).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(report-service): muavin v3 unit/snapshot tests (28 new tests, all PASS)\n\nColumnDefinitionTest (8 tests):\n- canonical 7-arg constructor defaults\n- backward-compat 5-arg constructor (hidden=false, exportOnly=false)\n- type/width defaults\n- blank field rejection\n- JSON parse: legacy v2 (no hidden/exportOnly) → defaults false\n- JSON parse: v3 with hidden=true + exportOnly=true\n- JSON parse: hidden-only (exportOnly omitted)\n\nReportDefinitionTest (7 tests):\n- hasSourceQueryFile / hasOuterQueryFile / isBranchUnionThenOuter\n- validation: must have one of source/sourceQuery/sourceQueryFile\n- 14-arg backward-compat constructor (new fields default null)\n- JSON parse v3 with file-based SQL refs\n- JSON parse legacy v2 still works\n\nYearlySchemaResolverCompanySchemaTest (6 tests):\n- Single COMPANY scope → companySchema = \"workcube_mikrolink_{id}\"\n- Multiple COMPANY scope → companySchema null (ambiguous)\n- No COMPANY scope → fallback to base sourceSchema\n- Backward-compat 1-arg ResolvedSchemas constructor\n- Record helpers: isSingle + hasCompanySchema\n- Missing company-only schema in DB → null\n\nSqlBuilderBranchUnionThenOuterTest (7 snapshot tests):\n- BRANCH_UNION_THEN_OUTER: outer wraps {inner} placeholder\n- {schema} placeholder per-branch (workcube_mikrolink_2024_35 vs _2025_35)\n- {companySchema} placeholder uniform across branches\n- {companyId} extracted from companySchema (numeric)\n- Missing companySchema → companyId fallback to \"0\"\n- BRANCH_UNION_THEN_OUTER: no filter pushdown into branches\n  (filter applied in outer WHERE for window correctness)\n- Legacy multi-schema fallback path preserved\n\nTotal: 28 new tests, all PASS. Existing 216 tests untouched.\n\nRefs:\n- Codex thread 019df4ed-615c-73d1-b67a-7d0b61cc94df (AGREE iter-4)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(governance): seed fin-muhasebe-detay-muavin-v3 feature contract\n\nCodex thread 019df4ed iter-7 önerdiği seed komutuyla muavin v3 için\nper-feature contract dosyası ve active_features index güncellemesi.\n\n- features/fin-muhasebe-detay-muavin-v3.v1.json: yeni entry (ACTIVE)\n- active_features.v1.json: append-safe update (STORY-0319 dokunulmadı)\n\nBackend report-service muavin v3 implementation''ını governance\ngates ile uyumlu hale getirir. PR #562 (multi-file contract pattern)\nmerge sonrası bu PR (#561) governance check''leri geçecek.\n\nRefs:\n- platform-k8s-gitops#360 (spec doc, e5efda3 merged)\n- platform-ssot#562 (governance migration, 7375f1ab merged)\n- Codex thread 019df4ed-615c-73d1-b67a-7d0b61cc94df iter-7 AGREE\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(report-service): Codex iter-8 REVISE absorb — QueryEngine wiring + L3 fallback + hidden enforcement\n\nThree blocking issues fixed:\n\nIssue #1 — QueryEngine wired to hydrated SQL (CRITICAL runtime bug).\nReportRegistry was hydrating sourceQueryFile/outerQueryFile content but\nQueryEngine still called the legacy 8-arg SqlBuilder overloads, so\ndef.sourceQuery() returned null and applyTemplates() produced \"(null)\" SQL.\nQueryEngine now injects ReportRegistry, resolves effective source/outer\nSQL, and calls the 10/11-arg hydrated overloads. New regression test in\nQueryEngineTest captures the wiring with ArgumentCaptor.\n\nIssue #2 — branch.sql now has all 8 fallback layers per spec §5.\nPrevious SQL collapsed L3 (POOL direct AC.ACTION_TABLE) and L4 (POOL via\nMONEY_TABLES dispatch) into a single MONEY_TABLES-joined branch. New\nstructure: L3 (priority 30) does direct equality on ac.ACTION_TABLE for\nthe ~1% populated rows, L4 (priority 40) keeps the deterministic 60-row\nMONEY_TABLES dispatch. ORDER BY tie-break also adds IS_SELECTED so\nmanually-marked ACM/POOL rows win when multiple rows share the same\npriority. MoneyHistory layers (L5-L8) emit NULL is_selected so they fall\nback to date+id ordering.\n\nIssue #3 — ColumnFilter enforces hidden/exportOnly.\nPreviously hidden=true and exportOnly=true were declared in JSON but\nignored at runtime. New visibility matrix:\n\n  hidden=false                  → grid YES, export YES\n  hidden=true,  exportOnly=true → grid NO,  export YES (audit-only)\n  hidden=true,  exportOnly=false→ grid NO,  export NO  (debug-only)\n\nRBAC restrictions still take precedence over the static flags. Added\ngetExportColumns() that the export controller now uses, so audit fields\n(kur_tarihi, kur_id, kur_yas_gun, is_opening_document) reach CSV/XLSX\nwithout leaking into the grid. ReportExportController switched from\nqueryEngine.getVisibleColumns to queryEngine.getExportColumns.\n\nTests: 16 new (9 ColumnFilter, 6 branch.sql snapshot, 1 QueryEngine\nhydrated-SQL flow); 260 total PASS (was 244 pre-fix). All 28 prior\nmuavin v3 tests intact.\n\nCodex thread 019df4ed-615c-73d1-b67a-7d0b61cc94df iter-8 REVISE absorb.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"36375f533c3ad6b7f9af918d24c389a818b84299","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/trees/36375f533c3ad6b7f9af918d24c389a818b84299"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/commits/b445ba961c0f889b80d46599f2535412fe8a724c","verification":{"payload":"tree 36375f533c3ad6b7f9af918d24c389a818b84299\nparent 7375f1abb1c118fec8c185ecff104ea51369a197\nauthor Halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1777971931 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777971931 +0300\n\nfeat(report-service): muavin v3 — file-based SQL + 8-katman EUR fallback (Codex 019df4ed AGREE) (#561)\n\n* feat(report-service): foundation — file-based SQL + hidden/exportOnly columns\n\nCodex thread 019df4ed iter-4 absorb (AGREE + 3 revizyon).\n\nColumnDefinition:\n- hidden(boolean default false) — UI grid''de görünmez\n- exportOnly(boolean default false) — sadece CSV/Excel export''a girer\n- 5-arg backward-compat constructor (eski JSON''lar etkilenmez)\n\nReportDefinition:\n- sourceQueryFile (opsiyonel) — classpath:reports/sql/<file>.sql ref\n  Avoid 6000+ char escaped string in JSON\n- outerQueryFile (opsiyonel) — post-union projection/window wrapper\n- queryShape (enum-like string) — \"BRANCH_UNION_THEN_OUTER\" multi-year global\n  running balance (muavin) için\n\nReportRegistry:\n- hydrateSqlFiles() — SQL files classpath''ten yüklenir, UNSAFE_SQL filter\n  uygulanır\n- validateSqlFilePath() — path traversal reject (no .., absolute, or scheme;\n  must match ^sql/<filename>.sql$)\n- getEffectiveSourceQuery() / getEffectiveOuterQuery() — hydrated content\n  cache''lenmiş döner\n\nRefs:\n- Codex thread 019df4ed-615c-73d1-b67a-7d0b61cc94df (AGREE iter-4)\n- Spec: ~/Documents/platform-k8s-gitops/.../docs/reports/muavin-grid-spec.md\n- gitops PR #360 e5efda3\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(report-service): schema resolver + SqlBuilder — companySchema + BRANCH_UNION_THEN_OUTER\n\nCodex thread 019df4ed iter-4 absorb (AGREE).\n\nYearlySchemaResolver:\n- ResolvedSchemas record extended: schemas + companySchema (nullable)\n- Backward-compat 1-arg constructor preserved\n- resolve() now also resolves company-only schema\n  \"workcube_mikrolink_{companyId}\" when single COMPANY scope\n- Multi-company scope → companySchema null (ambiguous; reports requiring\n  company schema must restrict scope further)\n\nSqlBuilder:\n- New hydrated overloads: buildDataQuery/buildCountQuery/buildExportQuery\n  with effectiveSourceQuery + effectiveOuterQuery params (caller passes\n  hydrated SQL from ReportRegistry)\n- {schema} + {companySchema} placeholder replacement (applyTemplates helper)\n- BRANCH_UNION_THEN_OUTER queryShape: raw multi-year UNION ALL inside outer\n  wrapper with {inner} placeholder; filter pushdown DISABLED so window\n  function sees full row set; AG Grid filters applied at outer wrapper\n  WHERE clause\n- Backward-compat 8-arg + 10-arg overloads preserved (no caller break)\n\nReportDefinition:\n- Backward-compat 14-arg constructor for programmatic callers\n  (DashboardQueryEngine etc.) — defaults sourceQueryFile/outerQueryFile/\n  queryShape to null\n\nRefs:\n- Codex thread 019df4ed-615c-73d1-b67a-7d0b61cc94df (AGREE iter-4)\n- Spec: ~/Documents/platform-k8s-gitops/.../docs/reports/muavin-grid-spec.md\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(report-service): muavin v3 — fin-muhasebe-detay JSON + branch.sql + outer.sql\n\nCodex thread 019df4ed iter-4 absorb (AGREE).\n\nfin-muhasebe-detay.json (v3.0):\n- sourceQueryFile + outerQueryFile + queryShape: BRANCH_UNION_THEN_OUTER\n- 32 columns: 26 visible (12 boyut + 4 TL + 4 USD + 5 EUR + 1 audit)\n  + 6 hidden audit (kur_tarihi/kur_id/kur_yas_gun/is_opening_document\n  exportOnly + card_row_id/action_id debug-only)\n- access.rowFilter REMOVED — Codex iter-4 önerisi: ACC_COMPANY_ID\n  cari boyutudur, OUR_COMPANY schema selection authz scope üzerinden\n  resolver''da yapılır\n\nsql/fin-muhasebe-detay.branch.sql (per-yıl branch, 247 satır):\n- {schema} + {companySchema} + {companyId} placeholder\n- 8-katman EUR fallback OUTER APPLY:\n  L1 ACM by CARD_ID (RATE2 — RATE1 dummy=1.0!)\n  L2 ACM by ACTION_ID cascade\n  L3 POOL: 13 *_MONEY (yıl×şirket + 2 şirket-only) inline UNION ALL\n     dispatched via MONEY_TABLES.ACTION_TYPE → ACTION_TABLE\n  L5 MH same-day company (RATE2)\n  L6 MH same-day GLOBAL (Codex order: same-day-global > prev-day-company)\n  L7 MH ≤7d prev company\n  L8 MH ≤7d prev GLOBAL\n- Pipe-delimited audit string (ACM/POOL/MH/MISSING)\n- Decimal cast SQL-side (float aggregation artefact engelleme)\n- IS_CANCEL=0 filter (iptal fişler dışlanır)\n- ACCOUNT_CARD_DOCUMENT_TYPES + OUR_COMPANY_ID = {companyId} match (canonical\n  şirket-bazlı lookup; SETUP_DOCUMENT_TYPE açılış için primary değil)\n\nsql/fin-muhasebe-detay.outer.sql (window wrapper, 106 satır):\n- {inner} placeholder (SqlBuilder branch UNION ALL''la doldurur)\n- Window functions: SUM(signed_*) OVER (PARTITION BY account_code\n  ORDER BY action_date, card_id, card_row_id ROWS UNBOUNDED PRECEDING)\n- TL/USD/EUR ayrı: borc/alacak/net/bakiye\n- COALESCE kur_kaynagi → MISSING|EUR_RATE_NOT_FOUND\n- Multi-year global running balance (Codex tezi: filter pushdown YOK,\n  outer WHERE''de uygulanır; bakiye filtreden önce hesaplanır)\n\nSqlBuilder.applyTemplates: {companyId} support eklendi\n- companySchema''dan numeric id parse (\"workcube_mikrolink_35\" → \"35\")\n- Yoksa \"0\" (no-match, fallback path''a düşer)\n\nTest: ReportRegistryTest 31 reports (fin-muhasebe-detay v3 dahil) load PASS\n\nRefs:\n- Codex thread 019df4ed-615c-73d1-b67a-7d0b61cc94df (AGREE iter-4)\n- gitops PR #360 e5efda3 spec doc\n- Live validation 5 kategori production MSSQL workcube_mikrolink\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(gitignore): anchor reports/ to root + add muavin SQL files\n\nCodex iter-4 absorb follow-up. Previous Commit 0d814a3e shipped\nfin-muhasebe-detay.json v3.0 referencing sourceQueryFile/outerQueryFile,\nbut the SQL files (sql/fin-muhasebe-detay.branch.sql,\nsql/fin-muhasebe-detay.outer.sql) were silently blocked by the root-level\n.gitignore \"reports/\" pattern (intended for observability artifacts).\n\nFix: anchor pattern to \"/reports/\" so it matches only repo-root, leaving\nnested checked-in reports/ directories (notably\nbackend/report-service/src/main/resources/reports/) untouched.\n\nPlus: add the two SQL files (247 + 106 lines) — branch + outer wrapper for\nmuavin v3 multi-year global running balance.\n\nWithout this commit ReportRegistry would NPE on hydrateSqlFiles for\nfin-muhasebe-detay (file missing on classpath).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(report-service): muavin v3 unit/snapshot tests (28 new tests, all PASS)\n\nColumnDefinitionTest (8 tests):\n- canonical 7-arg constructor defaults\n- backward-compat 5-arg constructor (hidden=false, exportOnly=false)\n- type/width defaults\n- blank field rejection\n- JSON parse: legacy v2 (no hidden/exportOnly) → defaults false\n- JSON parse: v3 with hidden=true + exportOnly=true\n- JSON parse: hidden-only (exportOnly omitted)\n\nReportDefinitionTest (7 tests):\n- hasSourceQueryFile / hasOuterQueryFile / isBranchUnionThenOuter\n- validation: must have one of source/sourceQuery/sourceQueryFile\n- 14-arg backward-compat constructor (new fields default null)\n- JSON parse v3 with file-based SQL refs\n- JSON parse legacy v2 still works\n\nYearlySchemaResolverCompanySchemaTest (6 tests):\n- Single COMPANY scope → companySchema = \"workcube_mikrolink_{id}\"\n- Multiple COMPANY scope → companySchema null (ambiguous)\n- No COMPANY scope → fallback to base sourceSchema\n- Backward-compat 1-arg ResolvedSchemas constructor\n- Record helpers: isSingle + hasCompanySchema\n- Missing company-only schema in DB → null\n\nSqlBuilderBranchUnionThenOuterTest (7 snapshot tests):\n- BRANCH_UNION_THEN_OUTER: outer wraps {inner} placeholder\n- {schema} placeholder per-branch (workcube_mikrolink_2024_35 vs _2025_35)\n- {companySchema} placeholder uniform across branches\n- {companyId} extracted from companySchema (numeric)\n- Missing companySchema → companyId fallback to \"0\"\n- BRANCH_UNION_THEN_OUTER: no filter pushdown into branches\n  (filter applied in outer WHERE for window correctness)\n- Legacy multi-schema fallback path preserved\n\nTotal: 28 new tests, all PASS. Existing 216 tests untouched.\n\nRefs:\n- Codex thread 019df4ed-615c-73d1-b67a-7d0b61cc94df (AGREE iter-4)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(governance): seed fin-muhasebe-detay-muavin-v3 feature contract\n\nCodex thread 019df4ed iter-7 önerdiği seed komutuyla muavin v3 için\nper-feature contract dosyası ve active_features index güncellemesi.\n\n- features/fin-muhasebe-detay-muavin-v3.v1.json: yeni entry (ACTIVE)\n- active_features.v1.json: append-safe update (STORY-0319 dokunulmadı)\n\nBackend report-service muavin v3 implementation''ını governance\ngates ile uyumlu hale getirir. PR #562 (multi-file contract pattern)\nmerge sonrası bu PR (#561) governance check''leri geçecek.\n\nRefs:\n- platform-k8s-gitops#360 (spec doc, e5efda3 merged)\n- platform-ssot#562 (governance migration, 7375f1ab merged)\n- Codex thread 019df4ed-615c-73d1-b67a-7d0b61cc94df iter-7 AGREE\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(report-service): Codex iter-8 REVISE absorb — QueryEngine wiring + L3 fallback + hidden enforcement\n\nThree blocking issues fixed:\n\nIssue #1 — QueryEngine wired to hydrated SQL (CRITICAL runtime bug).\nReportRegistry was hydrating sourceQueryFile/outerQueryFile content but\nQueryEngine still called the legacy 8-arg SqlBuilder overloads, so\ndef.sourceQuery() returned null and applyTemplates() produced \"(null)\" SQL.\nQueryEngine now injects ReportRegistry, resolves effective source/outer\nSQL, and calls the 10/11-arg hydrated overloads. New regression test in\nQueryEngineTest captures the wiring with ArgumentCaptor.\n\nIssue #2 — branch.sql now has all 8 fallback layers per spec §5.\nPrevious SQL collapsed L3 (POOL direct AC.ACTION_TABLE) and L4 (POOL via\nMONEY_TABLES dispatch) into a single MONEY_TABLES-joined branch. New\nstructure: L3 (priority 30) does direct equality on ac.ACTION_TABLE for\nthe ~1% populated rows, L4 (priority 40) keeps the deterministic 60-row\nMONEY_TABLES dispatch. ORDER BY tie-break also adds IS_SELECTED so\nmanually-marked ACM/POOL rows win when multiple rows share the same\npriority. MoneyHistory layers (L5-L8) emit NULL is_selected so they fall\nback to date+id ordering.\n\nIssue #3 — ColumnFilter enforces hidden/exportOnly.\nPreviously hidden=true and exportOnly=true were declared in JSON but\nignored at runtime. New visibility matrix:\n\n  hidden=false                  → grid YES, export YES\n  hidden=true,  exportOnly=true → grid NO,  export YES (audit-only)\n  hidden=true,  exportOnly=false→ grid NO,  export NO  (debug-only)\n\nRBAC restrictions still take precedence over the static flags. Added\ngetExportColumns() that the export controller now uses, so audit fields\n(kur_tarihi, kur_id, kur_yas_gun, is_opening_document) reach CSV/XLSX\nwithout leaking into the grid. ReportExportController switched from\nqueryEngine.getVisibleColumns to queryEngine.getExportColumns.\n\nTests: 16 new (9 ColumnFilter, 6 branch.sql snapshot, 1 QueryEngine\nhydrated-SQL flow); 260 total PASS (was 244 pre-fix). All 28 prior\nmuavin v3 tests intact.\n\nCodex thread 019df4ed-615c-73d1-b67a-7d0b61cc94df iter-8 REVISE absorb.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp+bLbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0uoQAEVD7sRnVvRkylAPYtsPBvYG\nFP4N7AScSSq0tADrNE8C2j54KJCgbEH3iHXlEJR3c1sV0sdiBuCoDFeTWwwSKC5s\njD/WdY6+2L2OmGm2nTKV3/KdbjEtwuG3/ioKcPDpbLW9pmhwlbL+dRAo9Xzkaldi\n1DDOUXUT7T5SDVuZCyloX2KRY1Dm+YTm2aO61+0h8K404DIvh/GJdtR1fUxXSVEj\nmPIInvJlWo/7izW4PQt4pFtW/ZNMZuYJdBff/2d7jxbLkDv7uGv+gKJnzhBPndhI\nMBLRcIKaYJfz3lpccupzj297su99jSUFISmMEC89UqDjmeHe7YHxfPi1qkEFNADa\ndrQCkvQ2HdtdODgHcVSkBHBi4be+5se9SSNGyNAtOXZGsDhUK4xrYISNgJV3RP8e\nfHH1ZE6cGJ2a0Q91rZge4T6wkiwITgQ7f+U0IZPmHX0xWf4AByOorZUXGtJiDIwR\n+1ay9iRxiyXJYeV85K7e08rFuA5X+CnYcdZMUFVgpANo5ufttkaqbZCBXxKCNlrv\nXbpV5/6YapfaPqKvLq3KnKU9xMQJxZGSbqQxBnCTlscDumRDB4G3H/3A73IMMf5E\njLOOIpsu9BNioC7KT9fiHRZzQEpNtMN01rnbacgGpt8To9H9VNwq3zdhGK1pNtV2\njw1BniogtyXaBm9qYqbX\n=BT9x\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-05T09:05:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commit/b445ba961c0f889b80d46599f2535412fe8a724c","node_id":"C_kwDOQooUwNoAKGI0NDViYTk2MWMwZjg4OWI4MGQ0NjU5OWYyNTM1NDEyZmU4YTcyNGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commit/7375f1abb1c118fec8c185ecff104ea51369a197","sha":"7375f1abb1c118fec8c185ecff104ea51369a197","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/7375f1abb1c118fec8c185ecff104ea51369a197"}],"sha":"b445ba961c0f889b80d46599f2535412fe8a724c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/b445ba961c0f889b80d46599f2535412fe8a724c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186576227?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/7375f1abb1c118fec8c185ecff104ea51369a197/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-05T08:37:09Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"Halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-05T08:37:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(governance): multi-file feature execution contract pattern (Codex 019df4ed iter-5) (#562)\n\n* feat(governance): multi-file feature execution contract foundation\n\nIntroduce per-feature contract files under extensions/PRJ-PM-SUITE/contract/features/\nplus an active_features.v1.json index, and extend the bridge policy with multi-source\nresolution (contract_paths > contract_glob > contract_path).\n\nThe legacy single-file contract (feature_execution_contract.v1.json) is preserved\nfor backward-compat audit; its content is migrated byte-identical into\nfeatures/staging-prod-profile-migration.v1.json so STORY-0319 contract is\nunchanged.\n\nCodex 019df4ed iter-5 verdict: C-prime multi-file contract pattern.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(governance): multi-contract loader for feature execution checker\n\ncheck_feature_execution_contract.py now resolves contract path candidates\nwith the priority chain contract_paths > contract_glob > contract_path,\nloads each contract independently, and validates them with feature-id\nprefixed errors so multi-contract failure mode is observable.\n\nCoverage is union-semantic: every scoped change must be covered by at\nleast one ACTIVE contract; service_scopes detection uses the union of\nall active contracts; UX REQUIRED-mode is asserted at union level.\n\nBackward-compat: legacy reporter shape preserved (top-level contract_path\n+ contract_summary union fields); new fields contract_paths,\ncontract_resolution_source, active_contracts[] are additive.\n\nCodex 019df4ed iter-5 verdict.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(governance): multi-active-contracts delivery session packet + guard\n\nbuild_delivery_session_packet.py:\n- Mirror the bridge policy resolution chain (contract_paths > contract_glob >\n  contract_path) and accept --contract-paths CLI override.\n- Build a per-contract sub-packet (lane_plan + write_plan + ux_context) for\n  every ACTIVE contract.\n- Emit union active_scopes / change_path_globs / lane commands /\n  allowed_write_paths so existing single-feature consumers (delivery session\n  guard, gates) keep working.\n- New active_contracts[] array exposes per-feature breakdown for observability.\n\ncheck_delivery_session_guard.py:\n- Read the union packet fields exactly as before; the union-by-construction\n  invariant from the builder makes the guard multi-contract-safe.\n- Report active_contract_count and feature_ids so multi-feature drift is\n  visible in CI artefacts.\n\nCodex 019df4ed iter-5 verdict.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(governance): seed feature contract with overwrite + traversal guards\n\nseed_feature_execution_contract.py adds three layered safety guards so two\nparallel PRs can no longer silently overwrite each other''s contract:\n\n1. --target-file is mandatory and must match an allow-list regex confined\n   to extensions/PRJ-PM-SUITE/contract/(features/<id>.v1.json |\n   feature_execution_contract.v1.json). Absolute paths, .., and arbitrary\n   directories are rejected before any file write.\n2. If the target already exists with a different feature_id, the script\n   refuses to overwrite (concurrent-PR collision protection). Same-id\n   overwrite still requires an explicit --allow-overwrite flag.\n3. New per-feature contracts are appended into active_features.v1.json\n   atomically (load-modify-write) so duplicates are not introduced; legacy\n   single-file target skips the index update.\n\nThe seeder no longer reads contract_path from the policy as the implicit\nwrite target -- callers must declare --target-file explicitly.\n\nCodex 019df4ed iter-5 verdict.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(governance): multi-contract loader + seed safety unittest suite\n\nTwo unittest files exercising the C-prime multi-file pattern end-to-end via\nisolated tmpdir-based fake repos:\n\nextensions/PRJ-PM-SUITE/tests/test_check_feature_execution_contract.py\n- contract_glob expands and loads multiple per-feature files (5 tests).\n- explicit contract_paths takes priority over the glob fallback.\n- legacy contract_path keeps working when contract_paths/contract_glob are\n  empty (backward-compat).\n- Coverage union: scoped change uncovered by any active contract emits the\n  expected delivery_scope:uncovered_change error at union level.\n- Per-contract validation errors carry the contract_<feature_id>: prefix.\n\nextensions/PRJ-PM-SUITE/tests/test_seed_feature_execution_contract_safe.py\n- --target-file traversal/absolute path/glob-mismatch all rejected (6 tests).\n- Legacy single-file path is allowed (in the regex) but never updates the\n  active_features.v1.json index.\n- Overwrite with a different feature_id is refused unconditionally (the\n  STORY-0319 protection PR #561 originally hit).\n- Same-id overwrite requires --allow-overwrite even with the flag.\n- active_features.v1.json appends new entries; re-seeding the same id keeps\n  exactly one entry instead of duplicating.\n\nLocal run: 11/11 PASS (python3 -m unittest extensions.PRJ-PM-SUITE.tests.*).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(governance): allow multi-source resolution fields in bridge policy schema\n\nThe bridge policy schema enforces additionalProperties=false. The new\ncontract_paths / contract_glob / active_features_path /\ncontract_resolution_notes fields introduced for the C-prime multi-file\ncontract pattern need to be declared optional properties so the\nvalidate-schemas CI gate accepts the extended policy.\n\nThis is the missing schema half of the previous foundation commit; all\nfields are additive and optional, so existing single-contract policies\ncontinue to validate unchanged.\n\nCodex 019df4ed iter-5 verdict.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(governance): active_features.v1.json source-of-truth resolver (Codex iter-6 REVISE absorb)\n\nCodex iter-6 REVISE blocker fix: `active_features.v1.json` was a dead\ncontrol-plane artefact - the seed script updated it but neither the\nchecker nor the packet builder read it back. DRAFT / INACTIVE contracts\nunder contract/features/ could leak through the glob fallback and trip\nunrelated PRs, while the active/deactive lifecycle index had no effect.\n\nChanges:\n- Extract shared resolver into extensions/PRJ-PM-SUITE/contract/contract_resolution.py\n  (DRY - both gates import the same resolve_active_contracts()).\n- New priority ladder: contract_paths -> active_features_path ->\n  contract_glob -> contract_path. The active_features index is now the\n  governance source-of-truth; ACTIVE-only entries are returned and\n  DRAFT / INACTIVE / ARCHIVED are filtered out.\n- Fail-closed validation of active_features.v1.json: missing index file,\n  malformed JSON, duplicate feature_id, unknown status, contract_path\n  traversal, or an ACTIVE entry pointing at a missing contract are all\n  hard GovernanceError; checker surfaces the error token in its JSON\n  report and the packet builder aborts with a SystemExit.\n- DRAFT entries pointing to a not-yet-existent contract are tolerated\n  (transient lifecycle), but never returned as active.\n- Policy notes spell out the priority order + fail-closed semantics so\n  future operators know contract_glob is migration fallback only.\n- 12 new tests in tests/test_active_features_resolver.py covering: ACTIVE\n  filtering, explicit-paths override, glob-fallback (only when index\n  absent), invalid-json, duplicate feature_id, invalid status, path\n  traversal, missing-active-contract, missing-DRAFT-contract OK, plus\n  end-to-end checks that DRAFT contracts NEVER leak into the gate scope\n  and that the checker + packet builder resolve to the same contracts.\n\nTest count: 23 PASS (11 existing + 12 new). Local CI dry-run on the real\nrepo: checker `contract_resolution_source=active_features_path`, 1\nactive contract, status=OK; packet builder same source, same contract.\n\nCodex thread: 019df4ed-615c-73d1-b67a-7d0b61cc94df iter-6.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"54849552f4620802bca8490849bc7ecd125abd3c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/trees/54849552f4620802bca8490849bc7ecd125abd3c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/commits/7375f1abb1c118fec8c185ecff104ea51369a197","verification":{"payload":"tree 54849552f4620802bca8490849bc7ecd125abd3c\nparent 84ba0a83958d5bb2279c4fbe919e703ce4d195e7\nauthor Halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1777970229 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777970229 +0300\n\nfeat(governance): multi-file feature execution contract pattern (Codex 019df4ed iter-5) (#562)\n\n* feat(governance): multi-file feature execution contract foundation\n\nIntroduce per-feature contract files under extensions/PRJ-PM-SUITE/contract/features/\nplus an active_features.v1.json index, and extend the bridge policy with multi-source\nresolution (contract_paths > contract_glob > contract_path).\n\nThe legacy single-file contract (feature_execution_contract.v1.json) is preserved\nfor backward-compat audit; its content is migrated byte-identical into\nfeatures/staging-prod-profile-migration.v1.json so STORY-0319 contract is\nunchanged.\n\nCodex 019df4ed iter-5 verdict: C-prime multi-file contract pattern.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(governance): multi-contract loader for feature execution checker\n\ncheck_feature_execution_contract.py now resolves contract path candidates\nwith the priority chain contract_paths > contract_glob > contract_path,\nloads each contract independently, and validates them with feature-id\nprefixed errors so multi-contract failure mode is observable.\n\nCoverage is union-semantic: every scoped change must be covered by at\nleast one ACTIVE contract; service_scopes detection uses the union of\nall active contracts; UX REQUIRED-mode is asserted at union level.\n\nBackward-compat: legacy reporter shape preserved (top-level contract_path\n+ contract_summary union fields); new fields contract_paths,\ncontract_resolution_source, active_contracts[] are additive.\n\nCodex 019df4ed iter-5 verdict.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(governance): multi-active-contracts delivery session packet + guard\n\nbuild_delivery_session_packet.py:\n- Mirror the bridge policy resolution chain (contract_paths > contract_glob >\n  contract_path) and accept --contract-paths CLI override.\n- Build a per-contract sub-packet (lane_plan + write_plan + ux_context) for\n  every ACTIVE contract.\n- Emit union active_scopes / change_path_globs / lane commands /\n  allowed_write_paths so existing single-feature consumers (delivery session\n  guard, gates) keep working.\n- New active_contracts[] array exposes per-feature breakdown for observability.\n\ncheck_delivery_session_guard.py:\n- Read the union packet fields exactly as before; the union-by-construction\n  invariant from the builder makes the guard multi-contract-safe.\n- Report active_contract_count and feature_ids so multi-feature drift is\n  visible in CI artefacts.\n\nCodex 019df4ed iter-5 verdict.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(governance): seed feature contract with overwrite + traversal guards\n\nseed_feature_execution_contract.py adds three layered safety guards so two\nparallel PRs can no longer silently overwrite each other''s contract:\n\n1. --target-file is mandatory and must match an allow-list regex confined\n   to extensions/PRJ-PM-SUITE/contract/(features/<id>.v1.json |\n   feature_execution_contract.v1.json). Absolute paths, .., and arbitrary\n   directories are rejected before any file write.\n2. If the target already exists with a different feature_id, the script\n   refuses to overwrite (concurrent-PR collision protection). Same-id\n   overwrite still requires an explicit --allow-overwrite flag.\n3. New per-feature contracts are appended into active_features.v1.json\n   atomically (load-modify-write) so duplicates are not introduced; legacy\n   single-file target skips the index update.\n\nThe seeder no longer reads contract_path from the policy as the implicit\nwrite target -- callers must declare --target-file explicitly.\n\nCodex 019df4ed iter-5 verdict.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(governance): multi-contract loader + seed safety unittest suite\n\nTwo unittest files exercising the C-prime multi-file pattern end-to-end via\nisolated tmpdir-based fake repos:\n\nextensions/PRJ-PM-SUITE/tests/test_check_feature_execution_contract.py\n- contract_glob expands and loads multiple per-feature files (5 tests).\n- explicit contract_paths takes priority over the glob fallback.\n- legacy contract_path keeps working when contract_paths/contract_glob are\n  empty (backward-compat).\n- Coverage union: scoped change uncovered by any active contract emits the\n  expected delivery_scope:uncovered_change error at union level.\n- Per-contract validation errors carry the contract_<feature_id>: prefix.\n\nextensions/PRJ-PM-SUITE/tests/test_seed_feature_execution_contract_safe.py\n- --target-file traversal/absolute path/glob-mismatch all rejected (6 tests).\n- Legacy single-file path is allowed (in the regex) but never updates the\n  active_features.v1.json index.\n- Overwrite with a different feature_id is refused unconditionally (the\n  STORY-0319 protection PR #561 originally hit).\n- Same-id overwrite requires --allow-overwrite even with the flag.\n- active_features.v1.json appends new entries; re-seeding the same id keeps\n  exactly one entry instead of duplicating.\n\nLocal run: 11/11 PASS (python3 -m unittest extensions.PRJ-PM-SUITE.tests.*).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(governance): allow multi-source resolution fields in bridge policy schema\n\nThe bridge policy schema enforces additionalProperties=false. The new\ncontract_paths / contract_glob / active_features_path /\ncontract_resolution_notes fields introduced for the C-prime multi-file\ncontract pattern need to be declared optional properties so the\nvalidate-schemas CI gate accepts the extended policy.\n\nThis is the missing schema half of the previous foundation commit; all\nfields are additive and optional, so existing single-contract policies\ncontinue to validate unchanged.\n\nCodex 019df4ed iter-5 verdict.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(governance): active_features.v1.json source-of-truth resolver (Codex iter-6 REVISE absorb)\n\nCodex iter-6 REVISE blocker fix: `active_features.v1.json` was a dead\ncontrol-plane artefact - the seed script updated it but neither the\nchecker nor the packet builder read it back. DRAFT / INACTIVE contracts\nunder contract/features/ could leak through the glob fallback and trip\nunrelated PRs, while the active/deactive lifecycle index had no effect.\n\nChanges:\n- Extract shared resolver into extensions/PRJ-PM-SUITE/contract/contract_resolution.py\n  (DRY - both gates import the same resolve_active_contracts()).\n- New priority ladder: contract_paths -> active_features_path ->\n  contract_glob -> contract_path. The active_features index is now the\n  governance source-of-truth; ACTIVE-only entries are returned and\n  DRAFT / INACTIVE / ARCHIVED are filtered out.\n- Fail-closed validation of active_features.v1.json: missing index file,\n  malformed JSON, duplicate feature_id, unknown status, contract_path\n  traversal, or an ACTIVE entry pointing at a missing contract are all\n  hard GovernanceError; checker surfaces the error token in its JSON\n  report and the packet builder aborts with a SystemExit.\n- DRAFT entries pointing to a not-yet-existent contract are tolerated\n  (transient lifecycle), but never returned as active.\n- Policy notes spell out the priority order + fail-closed semantics so\n  future operators know contract_glob is migration fallback only.\n- 12 new tests in tests/test_active_features_resolver.py covering: ACTIVE\n  filtering, explicit-paths override, glob-fallback (only when index\n  absent), invalid-json, duplicate feature_id, invalid status, path\n  traversal, missing-active-contract, missing-DRAFT-contract OK, plus\n  end-to-end checks that DRAFT contracts NEVER leak into the gate scope\n  and that the checker + packet builder resolve to the same contracts.\n\nTest count: 23 PASS (11 existing + 12 new). Local CI dry-run on the real\nrepo: checker `contract_resolution_source=active_features_path`, 1\nactive contract, status=OK; packet builder same source, same contract.\n\nCodex thread: 019df4ed-615c-73d1-b67a-7d0b61cc94df iter-6.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp+aw1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuOIQAAPPn8O94eehKK0/jXh6Q/xV\nHuv3DpnyM+WqakUTU+SYtZmi5YzlQMSCFWGIM8esWMHlwH0wAEnAXlH8XQrULXa2\nTN/7v1YVF4lYOs7rbBgDOxpVTAaaeA3Nhodi38GY5jLOqvmCsmgfvtVV2yZeyoTO\nZeoSDq/eYNVabQvyZPxlJ85IgTYVr5V7mTC6JVxFAGIiBZaFuz8t9ew/fcbDJaby\nktFWe6oxhBZ4xhPeIbjPKMVYeOYdFHulPdu+tYG2oJZpGpLGuDkUvCHsHWq6ecUX\nTTx2kRCqVVSvK4H9SpYcseTmz1Ozxdmn5Se7fDHgtw5WkzcE0Li8ahtQKE2cpxaV\nq0pvpLrwQRVA4ttDFJ7gynExE2WDV3p8kpw9fASWwrvNsQbJfJWm1C2kf+3I+ZX4\n2ebcxRk7SxFMs87qi4F2u3ihrFe7n5M05mFVn5y5xTkjzpz+PDM3e/2crO6aLb5T\nfdOS3sRgiqnZIjYdgI66oXqXCuEc