): AUDIT_BACKEND_URI feature-flag for gateway route[5] (QLTY-PROACTIVE-06 Faz 1) (#520)\n\nPart of the A → C gradual audit consolidation roadmap. Option A\n(feature-flag) lets operators flip the base GET /api/audit/events\nendpoint owner between user-service (legacy) and permission-service\n(consolidation target) via a single canonical env var. Reversible,\nno code change on rollback.\n\nScope:\n- Gateway property routes[5].uri now reads ${AUDIT_BACKEND_URI:lb://USER-SERVICE}\n- Compose default: AUDIT_BACKEND_URI=${AUDIT_BACKEND_URI:-lb://USER-SERVICE}\n- Stage rollout: set AUDIT_BACKEND_URI=lb://PERMISSION-SERVICE in\n  /home/halil/platform/env/backend.env + recreate api-gateway\n- Rollback: reset env + recreate (3 minutes)\n\nDoes NOT change:\n- routes[16] /api/audit/events/live → PERMISSION-SERVICE (always — PR #514)\n- routes[17] /api/audit/events/export* → PERMISSION-SERVICE (always — PR #514)\n- Only governs the base list endpoint\n\nGuard (next PR in Faz 2):\n- /api/audit/events/compare shadow endpoint to collect parity evidence\n  before full cutover\n\nFollow-up (Faz 3-5, separate PRs):\n- Mirror durability upgrade (HTTP fire-and-forget → outbox poller)\n- Controller cleanup (delete user-service/AuditEventController.java after\n  parity proven)\n- Schema unwinding (retention + user_audit_events table drop)\n\nPer Codex adversarial thread 019da7f1 (verdict: RED on direct flip;\nPARTIAL on feature-flag; this PR addresses the PARTIAL path).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"05adc55939454b7d85465834f7d88627703efead","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/trees/05adc55939454b7d85465834f7d88627703efead"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/commits/6bddaf5ac791a5d4f4e02a7364e66970a37285eb","verification":{"payload":"tree 05adc55939454b7d85465834f7d88627703efead\nparent f036c4e7253311728aef31cf1eccbf64ecde6fda\nauthor Halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1776641533 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1776641533 +0300\n\nfeat(audit): AUDIT_BACKEND_URI feature-flag for gateway route[5] (QLTY-PROACTIVE-06 Faz 1) (#520)\n\nPart of the A → C gradual audit consolidation roadmap. Option A\n(feature-flag) lets operators flip the base GET /api/audit/events\nendpoint owner between user-service (legacy) and permission-service\n(consolidation target) via a single canonical env var. Reversible,\nno code change on rollback.\n\nScope:\n- Gateway property routes[5].uri now reads ${AUDIT_BACKEND_URI:lb://USER-SERVICE}\n- Compose default: AUDIT_BACKEND_URI=${AUDIT_BACKEND_URI:-lb://USER-SERVICE}\n- Stage rollout: set AUDIT_BACKEND_URI=lb://PERMISSION-SERVICE in\n  /home/halil/platform/env/backend.env + recreate api-gateway\n- Rollback: reset env + recreate (3 minutes)\n\nDoes NOT change:\n- routes[16] /api/audit/events/live → PERMISSION-SERVICE (always — PR #514)\n- routes[17] /api/audit/events/export* → PERMISSION-SERVICE (always — PR #514)\n- Only governs the base list endpoint\n\nGuard (next PR in Faz 2):\n- /api/audit/events/compare shadow endpoint to collect parity evidence\n  before full cutover\n\nFollow-up (Faz 3-5, separate PRs):\n- Mirror durability upgrade (HTTP fire-and-forget → outbox poller)\n- Controller cleanup (delete user-service/AuditEventController.java after\n  parity proven)\n- Schema unwinding (retention + user_audit_events table drop)\n\nPer Codex adversarial thread 019da7f1 (verdict: RED on direct flip;\nPARTIAL on feature-flag; this PR addresses the PARTIAL path).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp5WX9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAddwQAGdcJVBVB5f16T1ZpZPbtDvr\n8H7iJKbgGcVjlK7F4vkQFe4T2+fDAte7GThEWizdmpycmS9qf4YY4DyoX1dggYbi\nVre4kWhmowe6jQQQYmK+s+k4UpwO1J51fxwc5HRB6W/8DsrVRFwUnuoQk5T8eOFj\n7k0i1X6+P4HUS2yaZwdJUwJRUROhCodtVUWSYCnQMiOfXKTWje9nVolM30sZRGic\nI7xMvdXKnCysH59Suo14OjYQ1LusuT2mBei43mhx5LNLtIDJFTmAY4+xL