.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/6bddaf5ac791a5d4f4e02a7364e66970a37285eb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186576227?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/f036c4e7253311728aef31cf1eccbf64ecde6fda/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-19T23:15:59Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"Halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-19T23:15:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(ops): crawler multi-strategy token + KC sweeper provisioner (QLTY-PROACTIVE-05) (#519)\n\n* feat(ops): staging crawler multi-strategy token + KC sweeper client provisioner (QLTY-PROACTIVE-05)\n\nRework of `web/scripts/ops/staging-console-crawler.mjs` that was added\nduring QLTY-PROACTIVE-01 investigation. v1 minted tokens via canary-load\nwhose client in serban realm does NOT carry audience mappers for\nvariant-service/user-service/permission-service/report-service — so every\nsecured API returned 401 and the crawler reported ~3,700 false positives\n(see Codex thread 019da771 analysis during theme-registry incident).\n\n## crawler.mjs changes\nNew TOKEN_STRATEGY env var with 4 modes:\n- `canary-load`  (legacy, default — preserved for back-compat; emits warn)\n- `password-grant`  (new: KC_CLIENT_ID + KC_CLIENT_SECRET; recommended\n                    with a purpose-built sweeper client)\n- `env-token`    (new: KC_TOKEN is already-minted bearer; skip KC mint)\n- `anonymous`    (new: no Authorization header; useful to verify public\n                    endpoints after a __skipAuth style fix)\n\nToken diagnostic: password-grant strategy decodes and logs `sub/email/aud`\nso operators can confirm the aud list matches the tested backends.\n\nAdded browser-extension CONSOLE_ALLOW pattern for `webpage_content_reporter.js`\n— this was the ONE remaining console error observed in live staging after\nQLTY-PROACTIVE-01/02/03 fixes landed (extension-side noise, not our code).\n\n## kc-provision-staging-sweeper.sh (new)\nIdempotent KC admin-API script that creates/updates a `staging-sweeper`\nconfidential client in the `serban` realm with:\n- directAccessGrantsEnabled=true\n- 7 audience mappers (variant-/user-/permission-/report-/core-data-/\n  schema-/api-gateway-service)\n- standard & implicit flow disabled\n- rotates client secret on each run\n\nOperator flow:\n  SSH stage-sw\n  KC_ADMIN_PASS=$(docker inspect platform-keycloak-1 \\\n      --format ''{{range .Config.Env}}{{println .}}{{end}}'' \\\n      | grep ^KEYCLOAK_ADMIN_PASSWORD= | cut -d= -f2)\n  KC_ADMIN_PASS=$KC_ADMIN_PASS backend/scripts/ops/kc-provision-staging-sweeper.sh\n  # Store printed secret in GH secret STAGING_SWEEPER_CLIENT_SECRET\n\nThen the sweep workflow''s Lane B (v2) can use:\n  TOKEN_STRATEGY=password-grant \\\n    KC_CLIENT_ID=staging-sweeper \\\n    KC_CLIENT_SECRET=<secret> \\\n    node web/scripts/ops/staging-console-crawler.mjs\n\n## Lane B status\nThis PR ships the CODE for Lane B (v2 of staging-error-sweep) — the\ncrawler is now audience-correct-capable. A follow-up PR wires it into\nthe `.github/workflows/staging-error-sweep.yml` workflow once\nSTAGING_SWEEPER_CLIENT_SECRET is provisioned. Kept separate to avoid\ncoupling crawler merge to KC provisioning.\n\n## FEC\nExtended change_path_globs: `web/scripts/ops/*` (was uncovered).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ux-map): register staging-console-crawler.mjs path (QLTY-PROACTIVE-05 follow-up)\n\nUX catalog enforcement requires an exact-path entry per changed file.\nCrawler was previously untracked, so its first-time addition in the\nparent commit triggered `ux_contract:uncovered_ui_change`.\n\nMapped to: consistency_and_pattern_governance / single_component_source_of_truth\n(the crawler is a dev-ops diagnostic, not user-facing UI, but the UX\ncontract requires every scoped change to have SOME mapping — picked the\nmost neutral theme).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(fec): add ux_contract.artifacts glob for web/scripts/ops (QLTY-PROACTIVE-05 follow-up 2)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"288e621daa3b8e305e28b6686722c25cf614a839","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/trees/288e621daa3b8e305e28b6686722c25cf614a839"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/commits/f036c4e7253311728aef31cf1eccbf64ecde6fda","verification":{"payload":"tree 288e621daa3b8e305e28b6686722c25cf614a839\nparent 8c62334c9a0de2b4df31da7f4c2baa97fde82097\nauthor Halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1776640559 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1776640559 +0300\n\nfeat(ops): crawler multi-strategy token + KC sweeper provisioner (QLTY-PROACTIVE-05) (#519)\n\n* feat(ops): staging crawler multi-strategy token + KC sweeper client provisioner (QLTY-PROACTIVE-05)\n\nRework of `web/scripts/ops/staging-console-crawler.mjs` that was added\nduring QLTY-PROACTIVE-01 investigation. v1 minted tokens via canary-load\nwhose client in serban realm does NOT carry audience mappers for\nvariant-service/user-service/permission-service/report-service — so every\nsecured API returned 401 and the crawler reported ~3,700 false positives\n(see Codex thread 019da771 analysis during theme-registry incident).\n\n## crawler.mjs changes\nNew TOKEN_STRATEGY env var with 4 modes:\n- `canary-load`  (legacy, default — preserved for back-compat; emits warn)\n- `password-grant`  (new: KC_CLIENT_ID + KC_CLIENT_SECRET; recommended\n                    with a purpose-built sweeper client)\n- `env-token`    (new: KC_TOKEN is already-minted bearer; skip KC mint)\n- `anonymous`    (new: no Authorization header; useful to verify public\n                    endpoints after a __skipAuth style fix)\n\nToken diagnostic: password-grant strategy decodes and logs `sub/email/aud`\nso operators can confirm the aud list matches the tested backends.\n\nAdded browser-extension CONSOLE_ALLOW pattern for `webpage_content_reporter.js`\n— this was the ONE remaining console error observed in live staging after\nQLTY-PROACTIVE-01/02/03 fixes landed (extension-side noise, not our code).\n\n## kc-provision-staging-sweeper.sh (new)\nIdempotent KC admin-API script that creates/updates a `staging-sweeper`\nconfidential client in the `serban` realm with:\n- directAccessGrantsEnabled=true\n- 7 audience mappers (variant-/user-/permission-/report-/core-data-/\n  schema-/api-gateway-service)\n- standard & implicit flow disabled\n- rotates client secret on each run\n\nOperator flow:\n  SSH stage-sw\n  KC_ADMIN_PASS=$(docker inspect platform-keycloak-1 \\\n      --format ''{{range .Config.Env}}{{println .}}{{end}}'' \\\n      | grep ^KEYCLOAK_ADMIN_PASSWORD= | cut -d= -f2)\n  KC_ADMIN_PASS=$KC_ADMIN_PASS backend/scripts/ops/kc-provision-staging-sweeper.sh\n  # Store printed secret in GH secret STAGING_SWEEPER_CLIENT_SECRET\n\nThen the sweep workflow''s Lane B (v2) can use:\n  TOKEN_STRATEGY=password-grant \\\n    KC_CLIENT_ID=staging-sweeper \\\n    KC_CLIENT_SECRET=<secret> \\\n    node web/scripts/ops/staging-console-crawler.mjs\n\n## Lane B status\nThis PR ships the CODE for Lane B (v2 of staging-error-sweep) — the\ncrawler is now audience-correct-capable. A follow-up PR wires it into\nthe `.github/workflows/staging-error-sweep.yml` workflow once\nSTAGING_SWEEPER_CLIENT_SECRET is provisioned. Kept separate to avoid\ncoupling crawler merge to KC provisioning.\n\n## FEC\nExtended change_path_globs: `web/scripts/ops/*` (was uncovered).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ux-map): register staging-console-crawler.mjs path (QLTY-PROACTIVE-05 follow-up)\n\nUX catalog enforcement requires an exact-path entry per changed file.\nCrawler was previously untracked, so its first-time addition in the\nparent commit triggered `ux_contract:uncovered_ui_change`.\n\nMapped to: consistency_and_pattern_governance / single_component_source_of_truth\n(the crawler is a dev-ops diagnostic, not user-facing UI, but the UX\ncontract requires every scoped change to have SOME mapping — picked the\nmost neutral theme).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(fec): add ux_contract.artifacts glob for web/scripts/ops (QLTY-PROACTIVE-05 follow-up 2)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp5WIvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+9kQAKMHtrDvsl+lDqAq5zM0N+kB\n+xLdO3qFKbXlsAwNRwcSmEsV2Ps0VhjyOjF3O3plILS2ld6sQP6K80zrn8d38/uM\nxeirvacveRJU79JIsLPLKUlCFYRy9rknUfvSs4I2w7zYb/lvIF2eRIoRJWiyoiK1\n59c/gnj2TcIusoWVl22YBaAr2kZhnQoqXrcnvbpsb8Cznjo2MLPtF53ymfJAG45a\nhHOvyAobSEifFWE8yVECoCmx77pqESsez3RL/NzuaqAZ+IUh0Ge9YGyqAHgKooC0\nrJ6HZ1OFWrgV/um9+SZuky/RfuR2+vIkKu/A1qZrVg7S5cPhddQkwNaK629KrI1Q\ntST62c8CCIw1nBPvceJDG38ts6+7sb8K5UqRQX6WLgvvrJDC/iZAu8VPbxIEzx07\nXgH4W8Fq9k9l3dcLCE7bAlqWseovSS5CJWyYJR4knDQxT3tOepCh5GdHrNvAMZL9\n8m+Vn6iTS2lQcSDiptMK6yR7IncKN4SbuRQZzcSfcS9UQ4oSlQH8AZOEgfmlJKZx\nRXeJYfLtV