ts_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/275aed2127180de90b417c067d0ee839a2a9a38d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-19T22:23:00Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"Halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-19T22:23:00Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ops): staging-error-sweep JSON built in Python, not shell concat (QLTY-PROACTIVE-04 v1.1) (#516)\n\nv1 CI run (workflow run 24640439855) failed with:\n  json.decoder.JSONDecodeError: Expecting '','' delimiter: line 1 column 163\n\nRoot cause: v1 built JSON via shell heredoc concatenation of `python -c`\noutputs; the `sample_json` interpolation didn''t escape backticks, quotes,\nor `$`-characters in log lines, producing malformed JSON when real log\nsamples contained such characters.\n\nFix: refactor to use file-backed inputs + a single Python block that\nreads per-service filtered log files and emits a well-formed JSON\nsummary. No shell-concat of JSON anywhere.\n\nBehavior-preserving changes:\n- Same CLI contract (env vars, exit codes, output path)\n- Same verdict ladder (pass/warn/fail @ 3/10 default)\n- Same output schema + allowlist processing\n- Python block uses stdin-free heredoc (no interpolation risk)\n\nVerified: locally re-traced the v1 failure mode (sample_json with\nsingle-quotes); v1.1 handles cleanly because all file reads go through\nPython''s own I/O layer.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"23d4e281efc95b9b3aee48802963a66abc24b7a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/trees/23d4e281efc95b9b3aee48802963a66abc24b7a2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/commits/275aed2127180de90b417c067d0ee839a2a9a38d","verification":{"payload":"tree 23d4e281efc95b9b3aee48802963a66abc24b7a2\nparent 363c57e386b158cb0ccbd0ad442fd7a77f8b03e6\nauthor Halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1776637380 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1776637380 +0300\n\nfix(ops): staging-error-sweep JSON built in Python, not shell concat (QLTY-PROACTIVE-04 v1.1) (#516)\n\nv1 CI run (workflow run 24640439855) failed with:\n  json.decoder.JSONDecodeError: Expecting '','' delimiter: line 1 column 163\n\nRoot cause: v1 built JSON via shell heredoc concatenation of `python -c`\noutputs; the `sample_json` interpolation didn''t escape backticks, quotes,\nor `$`-characters in log lines, producing malformed JSON when real log\nsamples contained such characters.\n\nFix: refactor to use file-backed inputs + a single Python block that\nreads per-service filtered log files and emits a well-formed JSON\nsummary. No shell-concat of JSON anywhere.\n\nBehavior-preserving changes:\n- Same CLI contract (env vars, exit codes, output path)\n- Same verdict ladder (pass/warn/fail @ 3/10 default)\n- Same output schema + allowlist processing\n- Python block uses stdin-free heredoc (no interpolation risk)\n\nVerified: locally re-traced the v1 failure mode (sample_json with\nsingle-quotes); v1.1 handles cleanly because all file reads go through\nPython''s own I/O layer.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp5VXECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArOcQAFMsQq0aa8lrx8wHl/Iiz22Z\nzdvPSnmSy6qdZxNOv+RaUvre5cFnYsWoqWLkZiBeFMlOOq/Euns9KODkC9/UpncX\nf1ivqUv4907GbtBFw532ReSb2FplYBe0KQSwKXZslXHxdLJn9tUI9LKIgWrYREl9\nkte8VzdDPzevvYvl2i7GxAKuH9yu7P1uJYloLnxLDb7EKsH4F3Vw+GZfNjj99hwZ\n3zk1BlzrYD0qvd+g2oohNmw7fyyjCmrnqZ3x0bCan1TRJqFTRmA4EQs46HGkEC8e\n9wWmXzitWAbHFuu3Qgn/1wQYVG1OCJ4