s/275aed2127180de90b417c067d0ee839a2a9a38d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186576227?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/363c57e386b158cb0ccbd0ad442fd7a77f8b03e6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-19T22:10:32Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"Halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-19T22:10:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(ops): proactive staging error sweep workflow (QLTY-PROACTIVE-04 Lane A MVP) (#515)\n\nUser ask (2026-04-19 Turkish): \"tüm hataları kontrol eden bir yapı ile\nkontrol etmedik mi en azından log hatalarını\". Gap identified: the\nexisting `staging-console-crawler.mjs` produces canary-load aud-mismatch\nfalse positives; `post-deploy-validate.yml` only pings /actuator/health;\nno workflow systematically scans backend container logs for runtime\nerrors post-deploy.\n\nThis PR ships Lane A (log sweep) only. Lane B (crawler rework to use a\nproper frontend-client admin token instead of canary-load) is deferred —\nit needs a Keycloak sweeper service-account client first and is spec''d\nin Plan agent output (see commit message trailer).\n\n## Lane A design decisions\n- **Self-hosted stage-backend runner** (mirrors stage-authz-diagnose.yml\n  pattern): docker CLI already on box, zero SSH keys/secrets needed.\n- **Cron every 30m** + post-deploy-{backend,web} workflow_run cascade +\n  workflow_dispatch for manual triage.\n- **Graduated verdict** (pass/warn/fail) with per-service thresholds\n  (WARN=3, FAIL=10 in 30m window) — single JVM WARN shouldn''t red-belt.\n- **Allowlist via PR** (not runtime config) — suppression changes are\n  auditable. Seed includes Hikari/Spring/Flyway banner noise + Eureka\n  registration log + stage-authz-diagnose [diag] markers + audit mock\n  fallback lines that tests intentionally emit.\n- **Artifact upload** (30-day retention) of JSON summary. No issue-\n  comment in v1 — adds complexity without clear signal threshold.\n\n## Files\n- `backend/scripts/ops/staging-error-sweep.sh` — 8-container scan,\n  JSON emit, exit code by verdict (0=pass / 1=warn / 2=fail).\n- `backend/scripts/ops/staging-error-allowlist.txt` — seed patterns.\n- `.github/workflows/staging-error-sweep.yml` — cron + dispatch + cascade.\n- `extensions/PRJ-PM-SUITE/contract/feature_execution_contract.v1.json` —\n  FEC change_path_globs extended with `backend/scripts/ops/*` and the\n  new workflow.\n\n## What this does NOT do (tracked for Lane B v2)\n- Browser console crawler with real-user token (needs KC sweeper client\n  + audience mapping; specified in Plan agent output thread).\n- Slack/email alerting on FAIL verdict (MVP emits GH annotation only).\n- Pinned tracker issue (v2 if signal is actionable).\n- Trend/deltas across runs (v2; MVP is point-in-time snapshot).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b179ed60b42a18f35686d22fee651f4b3bf59784","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/trees/b179ed60b42a18f35686d22fee651f4b3bf59784"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/commits/363c57e386b158cb0ccbd0ad442fd7a77f8b03e6","verification":{"payload":"tree b179ed60b42a18f35686d22fee651f4b3bf59784\nparent 60611faf580cab74a13f7fdc4db0010ced972b4f\nauthor Halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1776636632 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1776636632 +0300\n\nfeat(ops): proactive staging error sweep workflow (QLTY-PROACTIVE-04 Lane A MVP) (#515)\n\nUser ask (2026-04-19 Turkish): \"tüm hataları kontrol eden bir yapı ile\nkontrol etmedik mi en azından log hatalarını\". Gap identified: the\nexisting `staging-console-crawler.mjs` produces canary-load aud-mismatch\nfalse positives; `post-deploy-validate.yml` only pings /actuator/health;\nno workflow systematically scans backend container logs for runtime\nerrors post-deploy.\n\nThis PR ships Lane A (log sweep) only. Lane B (crawler rework to use a\nproper frontend-client admin token instead of canary-load) is deferred —\nit needs a Keycloak sweeper service-account client first and is spec''d\nin Plan agent output (see commit message trailer).\n\n## Lane A design decisions\n- **Self-hosted stage-backend runner** (mirrors stage-authz-diagnose.yml\n  pattern): docker CLI already on box, zero SSH keys/secrets needed.\n- **Cron every 30m** + post-deploy-{backend,web} workflow_run cascade +\n  workflow_dispatch for manual triage.\n- **Graduated verdict** (pass/warn/fail) with per-service thresholds\n  (WARN=3, FAIL=10 in 30m window) — single JVM WARN shouldn''t red-belt.\n- **Allowlist via PR** (not runtime config) — suppression changes are\n  auditable. Seed includes Hikari/Spring/Flyway banner noise + Eureka\n  registration log + stage-authz-diagnose [diag] markers + audit mock\n  fallback lines that tests intentionally emit.\n- **Artifact upload** (30-day retention) of JSON summary. No issue-\n  comment in v1 — adds complexity without clear signal threshold.\n\n## Files\n- `backend/scripts/ops/staging-error-sweep.sh` — 8-container scan,\n  JSON emit, exit code by verdict (0=pass / 1=warn / 2=fail).\n- `backend/scripts/ops/staging-error-allowlist.txt` — seed patterns.\n- `.github/workflows/staging-error-sweep.yml` — cron + dispatch + cascade.\n- `extensions/PRJ-PM-SUITE/contract/feature_execution_contract.v1.json` —\n  FEC change_path_globs extended with `backend/scripts/ops/*` and the\n  new workflow.\n\n## What this does NOT do (tracked for Lane B v2)\n- Browser console crawler with real-user token (needs KC sweeper client\n  + audience mapping; specified in Plan agent output thread).\n- Slack/email alerting on FAIL verdict (MVP emits GH annotation only).\n- Pinned tracker issue (v2 if signal is actionable).\n- Trend/deltas across runs (v2; MVP is point-in-time snapshot).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp5VLYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANfUQAHVvoo+hgFTeWrZfx7OO4sec\n/MxBy1r2DMtRFCE1+XeajL4hH0LvbsU71GoccGfOTB277WAPW35+Nzy6lfMhw4zH\nCnLKKIRIn2VeKJv6MoWRTdGBWMyFshIunZsLrLKjkDjH5/8X9dR/3Wpl7Tnc4f58\nM42+9CbmE3qdAr0Ukee8wwYttcHDbYUoKCNuT3LcelWriEek8U6uPeIMgVJG1WI/\nxsMILIs2aQA1/j1P9ZyYVg+Nz+v19VH23Lltlmh18NslPEDxx8wlL7pe+E8N+61b\nBRzeliUf1LD+Ce6GWJYmkDB/D+iqQNjIoz+ciwmeM8UkhZsl8swGGlq9m7qXt7rZ\nCDhRIRibjCliHtRXZVEs7cNkl0I/fV1An60FAMwvP35hvqmOlqz/LL2QvI2XT+bm\n8SPfhsvRLmJjjyA9QPIz8BJJ5fwaSX9SW+0zxzGvK5qsx9hyu8u+ou/Vhlk4dij+\nz14x7P2YnMfASClMKABlBky3+3oS6JE9dE4YkouJl4GPvrNooM1Hmk2HRjQpNTJO\nQvSCE3lWUsWQZuWFATXiIIFqhK2X1tcX4ieZn7u205tUNgEQrP4KwjW7oncxIcwu\nzSNDGseuviMmeemTdxdbnXFo/3finEapfsVb0BpyIyK7E3q9/BKkngXOhEMqwVnr\nk4rSRdq4/yHHSmoStEcR\n=5y8u\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-19T22:10:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gis