m/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/02d9a1665b15a3b4b4238a5d3db9ba6fadb4c61e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-19T06:38:19Z","email":"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"github-actions[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-19T06:38:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(permission-service): OpenFGA tuple idempotency + RoleChangeEvent fastpath REQUIRES_NEW tx + async task error-swallow (OI-03 canary) (#496)\n\nFollow-up to PR #489 and PR #491/#494 — hardens the role-change propagation\npath exposed by OI-03 canary cold run. Four coupled bugs (Codex thread\n019da431 deep analysis + iter-2 REVISE):\n\n## Bug 3: OpenFGA write/delete idempotency (OpenFgaAuthzService)\n- Single writeTuple/deleteTuple: swallow SDK validation_error for\n  \"already exists\" / \"does not exist\" (idempotent no-op).\n- Batch writeTuples/deleteTuples: fast-path batch; on idempotent\n  failure, per-tuple fallback; collect non-idempotent failures and\n  rethrow at end so callers correctly skip version bump on partial\n  failure.\n- Message-based cause-chain matcher (isIdempotent{Write,Delete}Error).\n- Idempotent INFO → DEBUG to prevent batch-fallback log spam.\n\n## Bug 4: propagateRoleChange read-only tx conflict (TupleSyncService)\n@Transactional(readOnly=true) blocked the authz_sync_version UPDATE in\nauthzVersionService.incrementVersion(). Fix: drop readOnly so the method\nruns in a writable tx. Outbox poller 30s fallback still works as backstop\nbut is no longer the only success path.\n\n## Bug 5: stale relation cleanup (TupleSyncService.deleteAllFeatureTuples)\nPrevious cleanup only deleted the CURRENT grant''s mapped relation; on\nVIEW→DENY / MANAGE→VIEW transitions, the old relation tuple persisted and\nsurfaced as a phantom allow. Fix: for every (permissionType,\npermissionKey) in the user''s active roles, delete ALL possible relations\nvia the (previously unused) getRelationsForType helper. Dedupe by\ncanonical string key because SDK ClientTupleKeyWithoutCondition does not\noverride equals/hashCode.\n\n## Bug 6: unused getRelationsForType helper — now used by Bug 5 fix.\n\n## FEC\n`extensions/PRJ-PM-SUITE/contract/feature_execution_contract.v1.json`\nnow covers `common-auth/openfga/*`, `permission/event/*`,\n`permission/repository/*` globs (needed for this PR + future changes\nper the same pattern).\n\n## Non-scope (separate PRs)\n- Warehouse `operator` (write) vs `viewer` (read) mismatch — latent,\n  non-canary blocker.\n- Permission-key-removed stale cleanup — edge case.\n- `DefaultAdminRoleAssignmentInitializer` outdated comment alignment.\n\n## Verification\n- mvn -pl common-auth,permission-service test → BUILD SUCCESS\n- Staging canary re-run (after merge) should show no more \"tuple already\n  exists\" / \"does not exist\" ERROR logs during role propagation.\n- /assignments post-PR #489 JOIN FETCH + this PR''s idempotency will allow\n  5/5 canary assignments and cleaner tuple state.\n\n## Consultation\n- Codex thread 019da431 iter-1: 4-bug comprehensive analysis + hidden 5th/6th.\n- iter-2 REVISE: batch fallback must rethrow non-idempotent failures;\n  LinkedHashSet<SDK model> dedupe doesn''t work (no equals/hashCode);\n  log spam fix.\n- iter-3: post-impl review pending → will open PR when AGREE.\n\nCo-authored-by: halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fa2daa03d0e8fc548072226f2b8fb4ba4968bda8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/trees/fa2daa03d0e8fc548072226f2b8fb4ba4968bda8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/commits/02d9a1665b15a3b4b4238a5d3db9ba6fadb4c61e","verification":{"payload":"tree fa2daa03d0e8fc548072226f2b8fb4ba4968bda8\nparent 1348cd6289492f340c572fd2e039795dbf502add\nauthor github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1776580699 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1776580699 +0300\n\nfix(permission-service): OpenFGA tuple idempotency + RoleChangeEvent fastpath REQUIRES_NEW tx + async task error-swallow (OI-03 canary) (#496)\n\nFollow-up to PR #489 and PR #491/#494 — hardens the role-change propagation\npath exposed by OI-03 canary cold run. Four coupled bugs (Codex thread\n019da431 deep analysis + iter-2 REVISE):\n\n## Bug 3: OpenFGA write/delete idempotency (OpenFgaAuthzService)\n- Single writeTuple/deleteTuple: swallow SDK validation_error for\n  \"already exists\" / \"does not exist\" (idempotent no-op).\n- Batch writeTuples/deleteTuples: fast-path batch; on idempotent\n  failure, per-tuple fallback; collect non-idempotent failures and\n  rethrow at end so callers correctly skip version bump on partial\n  failure.\n- Message-based cause-chain matcher (isIdempotent{Write,Delete}Error).\n- Idempotent INFO → DEBUG to prevent batch-fallback log spam.\n\n## Bug 4: propagateRoleChange read-only tx conflict (TupleSyncService)\n@Transactional(readOnly=true) blocked the authz_sync_version UPDATE in\nauthzVersionService.incrementVersion(). Fix: drop readOnly so the method\nruns in a writable tx. Outbox poller 30s fallback still works as backstop\nbut is no longer the only success path.\n\n## Bug 5: stale relation cleanup (TupleSyncService.deleteAllFeatureTuples)\nPrevious cleanup only deleted the CURRENT grant''s mapped relation; on\nVIEW→DENY / MANAGE→VIEW transitions, the old relation tuple persisted and\nsurfaced as a phantom allow. Fix: for every (permissionType,\npermissionKey) in the user''s active roles, delete ALL possible relations\nvia the (previously unused) getRelationsForType helper. Dedupe by\ncanonical string key because SDK ClientTupleKeyWithoutCondition does not\noverride equals/hashCode.\n\n## Bug 6: unused getRelationsForType helper — now used by Bug 5 fix.\n\n## FEC\n`extensions/PRJ-PM-SUITE/contract/feature_execution_contract.v1.json`\nnow covers `common-auth/openfga/*`, `permission/event/*`,\n`permission/repository/*` globs (needed for this PR + future changes\nper the same pattern).\n\n## Non-scope (separate PRs)\n- Warehouse `operator` (write) vs `viewer` (read) mismatch — latent,\n  non-canary blocker.\n- Permission-key-removed stale cleanup — edge case.\n- `DefaultAdminRoleAssignmentInitializer` outdated comment alignment.\n\n## Verification\n- mvn -pl common-auth,permission-service test → BUILD SUCCESS\n- Staging canary re-run (after merge) should show no more \"tuple already\n  exists\" / \"does not exist\" ERROR logs during role propagation.\n- /assignments post-PR #489 JOIN FETCH + this PR''s idempotency will allow\n  5/5 canary assignments and cleaner tuple state.\n\n## Consultation\n- Codex thread 019da431 iter-1: 4-bug comprehensive analysis + hidden 5th/6th.\n- iter-2 REVISE: batch fallback must rethrow non-idempotent failures;\n  LinkedHashSet<SDK model> dedupe doesn''t work (no equals/hashCode);\n  log spam fix.\n- iter-3: post-impl review pending → will open PR when AGREE.\n\nCo-authored-by: halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp5HhbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5hoQAA4uMctI6rbVGzR2bBTDVMC8\n7GC/TMwCfPHyZ47VJWv00N2bt30e1M9/0nEw499TN9fRyMYbcJr5+EmKoHZP2F14\npISq4R2ZJmrugydJSPFb6gaRmFby4vaiaSk3bGnnzXcXe/nJrj2bFBhOu+MMGun7\nPSwYutGvOVD6sQ7GopJZExwSXCZiSxeKKkQBPK6IOKvZr4e7auMBQ/iArlM7ObUD\n7FqoFly/FbYoq8GJDbrhM3zjVGJNloUBYvB3L/EO9c3kSX/Fv/sJX/wvIMMWAcnf\ncQ7jr0NJ5Ol/460EgIz6W2MKS3S341AQgGun5UybMASsiD7O/F2EgzGXAUz6z1tb\n8uK1UR1AkWuobRxDIeWm9i9RuVe41ShOJ+SI+G1CBY0UMsZyki/pTVDUnR0FdCFo\nzyhBOEVpzPBwn7L0u/ERCUM/R/KjA60KxxH9Az/OvVgcxja5ue8l09DyHESgzGlY\nnogIgC8VjruJvC9HMCOEpHSPhEC9OPAoyFgIu8QaZXJdvNJwVn6O3AIF5p2K8wiQ\nH1B1AHdey06PbY57oqBKho2b7oQ7XuoeHjnNVkYB8qL3tJSMOH+jAZKSS8DFPgbI\nCdOpWR1sM++R5hLtNY0HWu7GvVi6AsmdejDnFKIUxWVTEYzBHAQaNXhT29IvOg13\nuKpko/Y83/ZkepVxeCv6\n=Nh9u\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-19T06:38:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commit/02d9a1665b15a3b4b4238a5d3db9ba6fadb4c61e","node_id":"C_kwDOQooUwNoAKDAyZDlhMTY2NWIxNWEzYjRiNDIzOGE1ZDNkYjliYTZmYWRiNGM2MWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commit/1348cd6289492f340c572fd2e039795dbf502add","sha":"1348cd6289492f340c572fd2e039795dbf502add","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/1348cd6289492f340c572fd2e039795dbf502add"}],"sha":"02d9a1665b15a3b4b4238a5d3db9ba6fadb4c61e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/02d9a1665b15a3b4b4238a5d3db9ba6fadb4c61e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/1348cd6289492f340c572fd2e039795dbf502add/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-19T05:58:34Z","email":"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"github-actions[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-19T05:58:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(permission): JOIN FETCH rp.role in findByRoleIdIn — LazyInit in /assignments (OI-03 canary) (#495)\n\n* fix(permission): JOIN FETCH rp.role in findByRoleIdIn — LazyInit in /assignments (OI-03 canary)\n\nCanary OI-03 smoke reveals /api/v1/authz/users/{userId}/assignments returns\n500 for 4/5 canary users with concrete role IDs. TraceId correlation\n(8c00bc74-e38c-44bb-aa84-ccc59f9d7241) traces to:\n\n  org.hibernate.LazyInitializationException: Could not initialize proxy\n    [com.example.permission.model.Role#23] - no session\n\n## Root cause (Codex 019da431 deep analysis)\n- `POST /users/{userId}/assignments` handler is NOT @Transactional.\n- `spring.jpa.open-in-view=false` (correct hardening, but no session post-controller).\n- `rolePermissionRepository.findByRoleIdIn(roleIds)` returns detached\n  `RolePermission` entities; `rp.getRole()` is a lazy proxy.\n- `TupleSyncService.resolveEffectiveGrants` (called from the sync path)\n  dereferences `rp.getRole().getName()` to populate `ResolvedGrant.sourceRole`\n  → Hibernate tries to lazy-load → no session → throws → 500.\n\n## Fix\nSingle-point repository query fetch-join: `SELECT rp FROM RolePermission rp\nJOIN FETCH rp.role WHERE rp.role.id IN :roleIds`. Role is eager-loaded in the\noriginal query. Other callers (explain, authz/me populateEnhancedFields) are\ninside @Transactional(readOnly=true) so they were never breaking there but\nalso don''t regress — fetch-join is a single round trip for all callers.\n\n## Non-regression\n- `findByRole(Role role)`, `findByRoleId(Long roleId)`, `findByRoleIdAndPermissionType`\n  untouched (different queries, callers all inside transactions).\n- `deleteByRoleId` untouched.\n\n## Consultation\nCodex MCP thread 019da431 — comprehensive 4-bug analysis. This PR addresses\nBug 1 (primary /assignments 500 blocker). Separate follow-up PRs for Bug 2\n(blocked-probe scope gate), Bug 3+4+5 (tuple sync hardening).\n\n## Verification\n- `mvn compile` PASS\n- Staging deploy will re-render; canary re-run should show 5/5 assignments\n  success (or 4 concrete-role + 1 super-admin scope-only), unblocking\n  k6 mismatch rate reduction.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: trigger full CI on PR #495\n\n* chore(fec): add permission-service event/repository + common-auth/openfga globs\n\nPR #495 module-delivery-contract-check failed because RolePermissionRepository.java\nis under repository/* which wasn''t in the FEC change_path_globs. This commit\nextends globs to cover the relevant paths for this PR + PR #496 (tuple sync\nhardening) — repository/*, event/*, and common-auth/openfga/*.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"faa8e530204e962e3db121139583ec7fbd8276b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/trees/faa8e530204e962e3db121139583ec7fbd8276b2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/commits/1348cd6289492f340c572fd2e039795dbf502add","verification":{"payload":"tree faa8e530204e962e3db121139583ec7fbd8276b2\nparent 718d4c01483ef25bd25bc9bb5f13a89ee697c485\nauthor github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1776578314 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1776578314 +0300\n\nfix(permission): JOIN FETCH rp.role in findByRoleIdIn — LazyInit in /assignments (OI-03 canary) (#495)\n\n* fix(permission): JOIN FETCH rp.role in findByRoleIdIn — LazyInit in /assignments (OI-03 canary)\n\nCanary OI-03 smoke reveals /api/v1/authz/users/{userId}/assignments returns\n500 for 4/5 canary users with concrete role IDs. TraceId correlation\n(8c00bc74-e38c-44bb-aa84-ccc59f9d7241) traces to:\n\n  org.hibernate.LazyInitializationException: Could not initialize proxy\n    [com.example.permission.model.Role#23] - no session\n\n## Root cause (Codex 019da431 deep analysis)\n- `POST /users/{userId}/assignments` handler is NOT @Transactional.\n- `spring.jpa.open-in-view=false` (correct hardening, but no session post-controller).\n- `rolePermissionRepository.findByRoleIdIn(roleIds)` returns detached\n  `RolePermission` entities; `rp.getRole()` is a lazy proxy.\n- `TupleSyncService.resolveEffectiveGrants` (called from the sync path)\n  dereferences `rp.getRole().getName()` to populate `ResolvedGrant.sourceRole`\n  → Hibernate tries to lazy-load → no session → throws → 500.\n\n## Fix\nSingle-point repository query fetch-join: `SELECT rp FROM RolePermission rp\nJOIN FETCH rp.role WHERE rp.role.id IN :roleIds`. Role is eager-loaded in the\noriginal query. Other callers (explain, authz/me populateEnhancedFields) are\ninside @Transactional(readOnly=true) so they were never breaking there but\nalso don''t regress — fetch-join is a single round trip for all callers.\n\n## Non-regression\n- `findByRole(Role role)`, `findByRoleId(Long roleId)`, `findByRoleIdAndPermissionType`\n  untouched (different queries, callers all inside transactions).\n- `deleteByRoleId` untouched.\n\n## Consultation\nCodex MCP thread 019da431 — comprehensive 4-bug analysis. This PR addresses\nBug 1 (primary /assignments 500 blocker). Separate follow-up PRs for Bug 2\n(blocked-probe scope gate), Bug 3+4+5 (tuple sync hardening).\n\n## Verification\n- `mvn compile` PASS\n- Staging deploy will re-render; canary re-run should show 5/5 assignments\n  success (or 4 concrete-role + 1 super-admin scope-only), unblocking\n  k6 mismatch rate reduction.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: trigger full CI on PR #495\n\n* chore(fec): add permission-service event/repository + common-auth/openfga globs\n\nPR #495 module-delivery-contract-check failed because RolePermissionRepository.java\nis under repository/* which wasn''t in the FEC change_path_globs. This commit\nextends globs to cover the relevant paths for this PR + PR #496 (tuple sync\nhardening) — repository/*, event/*, and common-auth/openfga/*.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp5G8KCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAa6MQACA0thlCO03GZHuyzE89zZw7\nsbqNDu3cG41tBgj2XoQf/am/h+Z9JCGM2KtZPLcu4eCUKxOjgFmcimOB+ZmTLkI4\nt2/4DVhaqiyMx/nECUmHzHd/hubJnBNJKW1fQOgmRVqXCW5ruebxOKh/XYr1uOiq\n/oV3iEj+UjgEDbfkqEfZgHLSbKG6NX1I8t19FYLCvaAfCrjMC256tWUbFAzqFNGU\nIHlcoO2R9TUoDjGKYTw5I056fnGBl8q5cj73aemwPtcR9HXwY6tW4GLdsvENtb7e\ni19oR4pHcW3nAleQ2RCXgBTuEUUOjU7xgNtlPZo0rDCOiQ/FObkDtt2IcosKyTeb\nQvK60Xz349rVqpS6Qpa8pVcUOKrNl0YkRp9MewC8jxwHwKSfMa6Ocrj9DnOZs7Ll\nOXenr2RiwyZjIELkRFtwFomaorVvuN85ftXaIxHAi8G9a4j2ceN/Qa7MOSN4O66v\nUhGOueWktw93cTtEm+9XPSAfbzlF3VtxeNOuGTWDyWxcqyzWzuuLh/0WEzvAaH/5\nmsUTIVwK0fUws3OepGkUoVSCiA7i77undjmm3Idi8gt+f6WYiCBAKr9zsVda2xD7\nzbV1moBD944zmdyz0t/XFOZkL2Ahfji4ZZ2YkaNJMwl7ENUTPHcV89DS96OH/lKi\nJgsLm3ZVaR92VTkQ+16N\n=Xrjp\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-19T05:58:34Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commit/1348cd6289492f340c572fd2e039795dbf502add","node_id":"C_kwDOQooUwNoAKDEzNDhjZDYyODk0OTJmMzQwYzU3MmZkMmUwMzk3OTVkYmY1MDJhZGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commit/718d4c01483ef25bd25bc9bb5f13a89ee697c485","sha":"718d4c01483ef25bd25bc9bb5f13a89ee697c485","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/718d4c01483ef25bd25bc9bb5f13a89ee697c485"}],"sha":"1348cd6289492f340c572fd2e039795dbf502add","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/1348cd6289492f340c572fd2e039795dbf502add"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186576227?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/718d4c01483ef25bd25bc9bb5f13a89ee697c485/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-18T21:51:30Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"Halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-18T21:51:30Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(deploy): render KC_HOSTNAME trio with canonical stage defaults (OI-03 browser login) (#494)\n\nToday''s OI-03 browser-login investigation revealed KC_HOSTNAME was manually\npatched on staging 2026-04-15 (canonical env = https://ai.acik.com) but the\nrender/Vault chain did not carry the key, so subsequent deploys silently\ndropped it. Compose fallback (http://localhost:8081) then emitted the wrong\nauthorization_endpoint → browser redirect after login POST became\nERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED for users hitting https://ai.acik.com.\n\n## Root cause\nrender/Vault chain (write-backend-deploy-stage.sh + render-backend-env.sh +\ncheck-backend-deploy-stage.sh) did not include KC_HOSTNAME or the proxy\ntrio. Each stage deploy with RENDER_ENV_BEFORE_DEPLOY=true regenerated\ncanonical env from Vault KV, and the public hostname patch fell out.\n\n## Fix\nSame pattern as PR #491 (SECURITY_JWT_SECONDARY_AUDIENCE default-injection):\n\n- `backend/scripts/vault/write-backend-deploy-stage.sh`: KC_HOSTNAME +\n  KC_PROXY_HEADERS + KC_HOSTNAME_BACKCHANNEL_DYNAMIC added to Vault KV\n  payload (operator override path preserved).\n- `deploy/ubuntu/render-backend-env.sh`: default-injection block writes\n  canonical stage defaults (https://ai.acik.com, xforwarded, true) when\n  Vault KV value is empty. Vault KV override takes priority.\n- `backend/scripts/vault/check-backend-deploy-stage.sh`: comment note only\n  (trio intentionally NOT in required_keys — render fallback keeps deploy\n  safe during rollout).\n\n## Non-goals (separate follow-ups)\n- `backend/docker-compose.yml` Keycloak fallback remains `http://localhost:8081`\n  for local/dev; only staging render chain flips to public hostname.\n- `variant-service` hardcoded localhost issuer (line 168) — separate PR.\n- Singular-issuer service SecurityConfig cleanup (core-data, schema, auth) —\n  not coupled to this drift guard.\n\n## Immediate unblock (already applied ops-side)\n- Staging canonical env appended: KC_HOSTNAME=https://ai.acik.com\n- Keycloak container recreated (docker compose up -d --force-recreate --no-deps keycloak)\n- /.well-known/openid-configuration issuer verified https://ai.acik.com/realms/serban\n- admin token via public URL /authz/me STATUS=200\n- This PR prevents future deploy drift.\n\n## Consultation\nCodex thread 019da26d iter1 AGREE on KC_HOSTNAME=https://ai.acik.com +\ntransition plan; iter2 REVISE duplicate ordered_keys + default-injection;\niter3 AGREE after dedup.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"96b22ced183fddcb6da4f32f553bc76dbea95a6f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/trees/96b22ced183fddcb6da4f32f553bc76dbea95a6f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/commits/718d4c01483ef25bd25bc9bb5f13a89ee697c485","verification":{"payload":"tree 96b22ced183fddcb6da4f32f553bc76dbea95a6f\nparent e09b83fe878a91c1258b8f0f6ef63160f6c0fe0b\nauthor Halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1776549090 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1776549090 +0300\n\nfix(deploy): render KC_HOSTNAME trio with canonical stage defaults (OI-03 browser login) (#494)\n\nToday''s OI-03 browser-login investigation revealed KC_HOSTNAME was manually\npatched on staging 2026-04-15 (canonical env = https://ai.acik.com) but the\nrender/Vault chain did not carry the key, so subsequent deploys silently\ndropped it. Compose fallback (http://localhost:8081) then emitted the wrong\nauthorization_endpoint → browser redirect after login POST became\nERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED for users hitting https://ai.acik.com.\n\n## Root cause\nrender/Vault chain (write-backend-deploy-stage.sh + render-backend-env.sh +\ncheck-backend-deploy-stage.sh) did not include KC_HOSTNAME or the proxy\ntrio. Each stage deploy with RENDER_ENV_BEFORE_DEPLOY=true regenerated\ncanonical env from Vault KV, and the public hostname patch fell out.\n\n## Fix\nSame pattern as PR #491 (SECURITY_JWT_SECONDARY_AUDIENCE default-injection):\n\n- `backend/scripts/vault/write-backend-deploy-stage.sh`: KC_HOSTNAME +\n  KC_PROXY_HEADERS + KC_HOSTNAME_BACKCHANNEL_DYNAMIC added to Vault KV\n  payload (operator override path preserved).\n- `deploy/ubuntu/render-backend-env.sh`: default-injection block writes\n  canonical stage defaults (https://ai.acik.com, xforwarded, true) when\n  Vault KV value is empty. Vault KV override takes priority.\n- `backend/scripts/vault/check-backend-deploy-stage.sh`: comment note only\n  (trio intentionally NOT in required_keys — render fallback keeps deploy\n  safe during rollout).\n\n## Non-goals (separate follow-ups)\n- `backend/docker-compose.yml` Keycloak fallback remains `http://localhost:8081`\n  for local/dev; only staging render chain flips to public hostname.\n- `variant-service` hardcoded localhost issuer (line 168) — separate PR.\n- Singular-issuer service SecurityConfig cleanup (core-data, schema, auth) —\n  not coupled to this drift guard.\n\n## Immediate unblock (already applied ops-side)\n- Staging canonical env appended: KC_HOSTNAME=https://ai.acik.com\n- Keycloak container recreated (docker compose up -d --force-recreate --no-deps keycloak)\n- /.well-known/openid-configuration issuer verified https://ai.acik.com/realms/serban\n- admin token via public URL /authz/me STATUS=200\n- This PR prevents future deploy drift.\n\n## Consultation\nCodex thread 019da26d iter1 AGREE on KC_HOSTNAME=https://ai.acik.com +\ntransition plan; iter2 REVISE duplicate ordered_keys + default-injection;\niter3 AGREE after dedup.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp4/ziCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADEsQAEWtcP4U8kOUbJxccS4ySDeA\nETbQrXgZpFqK7g3nr9aUhNBJuqbNaBuiMopIGFS4dea7820F8XNAHhTAf3M82YUO\nCUXhK2owdC1dMHINY