ldeu/platform-ssot/commit/49dfb135b41d394f9d5b8dd2778b32ae76099f9f","sha":"49dfb135b41d394f9d5b8dd2778b32ae76099f9f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/49dfb135b41d394f9d5b8dd2778b32ae76099f9f"}],"sha":"e09b83fe878a91c1258b8f0f6ef63160f6c0fe0b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/e09b83fe878a91c1258b8f0f6ef63160f6c0fe0b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186576227?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/49dfb135b41d394f9d5b8dd2778b32ae76099f9f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-18T19:46:43Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"Halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-18T19:46:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(deploy): render SECURITY_JWT_SECONDARY_AUDIENCE with canonical default + prod passthrough (OI-03) (#491)\n\nCanary cold+warm run was blocked on staging because RENDER_ENV_BEFORE_DEPLOY=true\ndropped SECURITY_JWT_SECONDARY_AUDIENCE from the canonical env (not tracked in\nVault KV chain). canary-load KC client issues JWTs with aud=account (no audience\nmapper), and permission-service rejected them because ''account'' wasn''t in the\nsecondary-audience allowlist.\n\n## Changes\n- `deploy/ubuntu/render-backend-env.sh`: writes SECURITY_JWT_SECONDARY_AUDIENCE\n  with a canonical 4-audience default (permission-service,frontend,account,\n  serban-web — aligned with primary contract in application.properties:22)\n  when Vault KV value is empty. Vault override still takes priority.\n- `backend/scripts/vault/write-backend-deploy-stage.sh`: forwards the env var\n  to Vault KV so operators can push a custom value via CI.\n- `backend/scripts/vault/check-backend-deploy-stage.sh`: explanatory comment\n  (intentionally NOT in required_keys — render fallback keeps deploys safe).\n- `deploy/docker-compose.prod.yml`: adds SECURITY_JWT_SECONDARY_AUDIENCE\n  passthrough to permission-service (prod chain parity with staging).\n\n## Design\n- Non-regression: existing deploys keep working when Vault KV hasn''t been\n  repopulated (default injection in render, not required_keys).\n- Vault KV override path preserved: operators set GH Actions secret → write\n  script pushes to Vault KV → next render picks the custom value up.\n- Default mirrors primary `security.jwt.audience` default so the secondary\n  allowlist never diverges from the primary one (prevents silent 401 when\n  secondary decoder is reached).\n\n## Consultation\n- Codex thread 019da211 iter1 REVISE — default list too broad (8-value) +\n  prod compose passthrough missing + wrong class name in comment.\n- Codex thread 019da211 iter2 AGREE — 4-value aligned with primary +\n  prod compose wired + comment fixed (FallbackJwtDecoder + AudienceValidator).\n\n## Test plan\n- CI: ci-gate-backend, schema-policy-enforcement, module-delivery\n- Deploy: `render-backend-env.sh` writes `SECURITY_JWT_SECONDARY_AUDIENCE=...`\n  to canonical env on staging; canary run produces super-admin JWT whose\n  aud=account passes audience validator; `/authz/me` + `/api/v1/roles` 200\n  instead of 401; granule PUT succeeds (V13 from PR #489); full cold+warm\n  produces evidence manifest → OI-03 CLOSED.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f854da3ddd92679d34f03b107427c23dd3889923","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/trees/f854da3ddd92679d34f03b107427c23dd3889923"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/commits/49dfb135b41d394f9d5b8dd2778b32ae76099f9f","verification":{"payload":"tree f854da3ddd92679d34f03b107427c23dd3889923\nparent 7b374612d51115b0f499e7758d3b0cc6522f7062\nauthor Halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1776541603 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1776541603 +0300\n\nfix(deploy): render SECURITY_JWT_SECONDARY_AUDIENCE with canonical default + prod passthrough (OI-03) (#491)\n\nCanary cold+warm run was blocked on staging because RENDER_ENV_BEFORE_DEPLOY=true\ndropped SECURITY_JWT_SECONDARY_AUDIENCE from the canonical env (not tracked in\nVault KV chain). canary-load KC client issues JWTs with aud=account (no audience\nmapper), and permission-service rejected them because ''account'' wasn''t in the\nsecondary-audience allowlist.\n\n## Changes\n- `deploy/ubuntu/render-backend-env.sh`: writes SECURITY_JWT_SECONDARY_AUDIENCE\n  with a canonical 4-audience default (permission-service,frontend,account,\n  serban-web — aligned with primary contract in application.properties:22)\n  when Vault KV value is empty. Vault override still takes priority.\n- `backend/scripts/vault/write-backend-deploy-stage.sh`: forwards the env var\n  to Vault KV so operators can push a custom value via CI.\n- `backend/scripts/vault/check-backend-deploy-stage.sh`: explanatory comment\n  (intentionally NOT in required_keys — render fallback keeps deploys safe).\n- `deploy/docker-compose.prod.yml`: adds SECURITY_JWT_SECONDARY_AUDIENCE\n  passthrough to permission-service (prod chain parity with staging).\n\n## Design\n- Non-regression: existing deploys keep working when Vault KV hasn''t been\n  repopulated (default injection in render, not required_keys).\n- Vault KV override path preserved: operators set GH Actions secret → write\n  script pushes to Vault KV → next render picks the custom value up.\n- Default mirrors primary `security.jwt.audience` default so the secondary\n  allowlist never diverges from the primary one (prevents silent 401 when\n  secondary decoder is reached).\n\n## Consultation\n- Codex thread 019da211 iter1 REVISE — default list too broad (8-value) +\n  prod compose passthrough missing + wrong class name in comment.\n- Codex thread 019da211 iter2 AGREE — 4-value aligned with primary +\n  prod compose wired + comment fixed (FallbackJwtDecoder + AudienceValidator).\n\n## Test plan\n- CI: ci-gate-backend, schema-policy-enforcement, module-delivery\n- Deploy: `render-backend-env.sh` writes `SECURITY_JWT_SECONDARY_AUDIENCE=...`\n  to canonical env on staging; canary run produces super-admin JWT whose\n  aud=account passes audience validator; `/authz/me` + `/api/v1/roles` 200\n  instead of 401; granule PUT succeeds (V13 from PR #489); full cold+warm\n  produces evidence manifest → OI-03 CLOSED.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp49+jCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAApYQQAE5j+iqTHYhd3qLGICfAy3N8\nmYogw2CUZpeu5zIiaL52D719j1R+2g0BQVogocoZJZ9wTJngiKFfEFt9Zd1N1aM/\n2eSQjExccozl5jcwNIUgTHgdt4w3J5pRTIG5SJazOdcF7011d76Blg6OC24GfvE6\nluuvMycm24xl1uvKqHDwSqcNjpok7nihz1sA+qZzK5rXUDn8KFuYPtAKtWo4AMnq\nw9J616UG3UeJEFcQqSOmGla4X7YMTU8Bxy7HXY+gfTXTXGUGuVY1otRVpusOH19Z\nKmH9Etkaslxs3IRwUTOefbfrbvTBHVM3aDmjNPbY3g+mKpKh7JaoNSCYfdoEPVJK\n6XdbAZAix5baFiuj0UNx1RqpAb8yfk4bUDC/5z8c2JcWQ+q4Q8tBgri5lfFwmGyj\nOMmLaqDOoqRf+uyecrrkwtZVqhbIuHb60LBkwhjJr13HarPQy4k/eb9Nrt4PlrMY\ne6YzBfkJy1Jrfq8/qmOv8F7m+3ypExPTFOTMCBKh9j3NfhRyhsvWQC89251BnSkD\nrth0k4KnfXuqQDPYyeH7bJ4cxgrBxPttY8a6x56ejM+fbZrm6yePy+DFAsi9J6ql\nH1GDpz24qGjyQYZ7W3gO+Z9cXRsnD