"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/e59b0f5bf47eb08a9b97e864fc6368859781e152/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-18T15:44:45Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"Halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-18T15:44:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(compose): permission-service SECURITY_AUTH_ALLOWED_CLIENT_IDS env wire (OI-03 Bug B) (#486)\n\n2026-04-18 OI-03 canary deep debug (Codex thread 019da137): canary-restricted\nvalid KC token returns 401 on `/api/v1/authz/me`. Root cause: permission-service\nAudienceValidator uses `SECURITY_AUTH_ALLOWED_CLIENT_IDS` as `azp` fallback\nwhen `aud` doesn''t match (per PR #426 CNS-20260416-003). Canonical env had\nthis key but compose env chain didn''t propagate it to permission-service\ncontainer — `canary-load` client tokens rejected.\n\nSame env-chain drift class as PR #484 (auth-service SERVICE_CLIENT_USER_SERVICE_SECRET).\nOne more missing wire.\n\nFix: add `SECURITY_AUTH_ALLOWED_CLIENT_IDS: ${...:-frontend,admin-cli,serban-web,account,canary-load}` to permission-service compose env. Same default value as api-gateway (line 259). Canonical env override preserved.\n\nExpected post-deploy: canary-restricted `/authz/me` → 200 (valid user lookup).\nUnblocks probe step + subsequent canary flow.\n\nCodex review: thread 019da137 — Bug B identified via allowlist drift, not\nAuthenticatedUserLookup failure (which would produce 200 with degraded scope,\nnot 401).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a66b4a48feb0c0ada8260ff8c33809cfb0a341ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/trees/a66b4a48feb0c0ada8260ff8c33809cfb0a341ef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/commits/e59b0f5bf47eb08a9b97e864fc6368859781e152","verification":{"payload":"tree a66b4a48feb0c0ada8260ff8c33809cfb0a341ef\nparent c9cd531336e0e3af6415d2c819d18fe37a6ac250\nauthor Halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1776527085 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1776527085 +0300\n\nfix(compose): permission-service SECURITY_AUTH_ALLOWED_CLIENT_IDS env wire (OI-03 Bug B) (#486)\n\n2026-04-18 OI-03 canary deep debug (Codex thread 019da137): canary-restricted\nvalid KC token returns 401 on `/api/v1/authz/me`. Root cause: permission-service\nAudienceValidator uses `SECURITY_AUTH_ALLOWED_CLIENT_IDS` as `azp` fallback\nwhen `aud` doesn''t match (per PR #426 CNS-20260416-003). Canonical env had\nthis key but compose env chain didn''t propagate it to permission-service\ncontainer — `canary-load` client tokens rejected.\n\nSame env-chain drift class as PR #484 (auth-service SERVICE_CLIENT_USER_SERVICE_SECRET).\nOne more missing wire.\n\nFix: add `SECURITY_AUTH_ALLOWED_CLIENT_IDS: ${...:-frontend,admin-cli,serban-web,account,canary-load}` to permission-service compose env. Same default value as api-gateway (line 259). Canonical env override preserved.\n\nExpected post-deploy: canary-restricted `/authz/me` → 200 (valid user lookup).\nUnblocks probe step + subsequent canary flow.\n\nCodex review: thread 019da137 — Bug B identified via allowlist drift, not\nAuthenticatedUserLookup failure (which would produce 200 with degraded scope,\nnot 401).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp46btCRC1a