latform-ssot/commit/c9cd531336e0e3af6415d2c819d18fe37a6ac250","sha":"c9cd531336e0e3af6415d2c819d18fe37a6ac250","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/c9cd531336e0e3af6415d2c819d18fe37a6ac250"}],"sha":"e59b0f5bf47eb08a9b97e864fc6368859781e152","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/e59b0f5bf47eb08a9b97e864fc6368859781e152"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186576227?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/c9cd531336e0e3af6415d2c819d18fe37a6ac250/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-18T15:25:19Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"Halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-18T15:25:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(canary): setup 3 fixes — KC password reset + user-service fallback + super-admin user JWT (OI-03) (#485)\n\n* fix(canary): setup script 3 fixes — KC password reset + user-service UPSERT fallback + super-admin user JWT for /roles (Codex 019da124)\n\n2026-04-18 OI-03 canary setup revealed 3 independent bugs:\n\n**Bug 1 (partial blocker): user-service provision 500 duplicate key**\n- INSERT hits users_pkey unique constraint for pre-existing personas\n  (ADMIN DefaultInitializer or prior seed). Backend UserService.provisionFromKeycloak\n  is logical UPSERT (findByEmail + update) but users_id_seq drift or race\n  can still produce duplicates.\n- Fix: fallback to `GET /api/users/internal/by-email/{email}` and resolve\n  existing userId when provision returns !ok. Script becomes idempotent;\n  underlying backend issue tracked separately.\n\n**Bug 2 (critical blocker): permission-service /api/v1/roles POST 401 null**\n- Endpoint uses @RequireModule (user-based OpenFGA check via\n  AccessControllerV1:80-82 + RequireModuleInterceptor:55-61). Minted\n  service token has no authenticated user context — auth chain rejects.\n- Fix: use super-admin persona user JWT (password grant) for role\n  creation. Added `getSuperAdminUserToken()` helper, `psAuthHeaders()`\n  prefers user JWT over service token. Service-token fallback kept for\n  break-glass (warn+401 is still visible in log).\n\n**Bug 3 (graceful-degrade): KC persona password tokens 401**\n- `kcEnsureUser` create path sets password but existing-user path skipped\n  reset. All re-runs had 4/5 personas without password set.\n- Fix: in existing-user path, call `PUT /admin/realms/{realm}/users/{id}/reset-password`\n  each invocation (idempotent — Keycloak accepts unchanged password).\n\nImpact: OI-03 canary setup can now produce 5/5 persona tokens + role\ncreation via super-admin path. Password reset needs Keycloak admin token\n(already required for user create). No new env vars.\n\nCodex review: thread 019da124. Fix order per Codex: Bug 2 first (critical),\n1 + 3 parallel (same identity-idempotency class).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(fec): cover zanzibar-canary-setup.mjs (CI unblock PR #485)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3906b88f486ca9e8603b2f3c7a328ad99189c0ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/trees/3906b88f486ca9e8603b2f3c7a328ad99189c0ef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/commits/c9cd531336e0e3af6415d2c819d18fe37a6ac250","verification":{"payload":"tree 3906b88f486ca9e8603b2f3c7a328ad99189c0ef\nparent b56339dc0748c33c2857fcdff45bf5321994b81d\nauthor Halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1776525919 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1776525919 +0300\n\nfix(canary): setup 3 fixes — KC password reset + user-service fallback + super-admin user JWT (OI-03) (#485)\n\n* fix(canary): setup script 3 fixes — KC password reset + user-service UPSERT fallback + super-admin user JWT for /roles (Codex 019da124)\n\n2026-04-18 OI-03 canary setup revealed 3 independent bugs:\n\n**Bug 1 (partial blocker): user-service provision 500 duplicate key**\n- INSERT hits users_pkey unique constraint for pre-existing personas\n  (ADMIN DefaultInitializer or prior seed). Backend UserService.provisionFromKeycloak\n  is logical UPSERT (findByEmail + update) but users_id_seq drift or race\n  can still produce duplicates.\n- Fix: fallback to `GET /api/users/internal/by-email/{email}` and resolve\n  existing userId when provision returns !ok. Script becomes idempotent;\n  underlying backend issue tracked separately.\n\n**Bug 2 (critical blocker): permission-service /api/v1/roles POST 401 null**\n- Endpoint uses @RequireModule (user-based OpenFGA check via\n  AccessControllerV1:80-82 + RequireModuleInterceptor:55-61). Minted\n  service token has no authenticated user context — auth chain rejects.\n- Fix: use super-admin persona user JWT (password grant) for role\n  creation. Added `getSuperAdminUserToken()` helper, `psAuthHeaders()`\n  prefers user JWT over service token. Service-token fallback kept for\n  break-glass (warn+401 is still visible in log).\n\n**Bug 3 (graceful-degrade): KC persona password tokens 401**\n- `kcEnsureUser` create path sets password but existing-user path skipped\n  reset. All re-runs had 4/5 personas without password set.\n- Fix: in existing-user path, call `PUT /admin/realms/{realm}/users/{id}/reset-password`\n  each invocation (idempotent — Keycloak accepts unchanged password).\n\nImpact: OI-03 canary setup can now produce 5/5 persona tokens + role\ncreation via super-admin path. Password reset needs Keycloak admin token\n(already required for user create). No new env vars.\n\nCodex review: thread 019da124. Fix order per Codex: Bug 2 first (critical),\n1 + 3 parallel (same identity-idempotency class).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(fec): cover zanzibar-canary-setup.mjs (CI unblock PR #485)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp46JfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVv8QAJkkxa8CVafxjIGKtIJiz/xF\nhwhZA5UH5pBQ/+7/120bXril57VKGK4OellZVXPW6P+yJBSq7YCQ7vvv5d/K8NDw\nRQhe42nvJyhdHjrqo4ZkzAOw4AL6VA8RaJHvnONF/EArYMHnFO80oX/KMaA3spz9\nyE08jC2Vhw1uSMvDrKOaXDXUceLEwb5GxAl5R2+7Jkwub+U/2O3Ib1Okz3TMWi5C\nihukvoCRRV7aEiLJxmwtoWoaY5oge4cYNLrF3z+rForqgSKC0UdkTclCXxGxn0oP\nBbfQZa/OiMJ14JsizZfEDSkq7MHBDsthD3ihDzTSCvVfinL5FaEhSgP6pOLHMzyU\ntfpzgSZmlXa9iiPGlyIHw7wVYI8IK6YVNYZpJ9Zsz868J/coO5DbkyDD8x9GQaqT\ntTD4N2Qq8fHS8ig4Tkqns7fss9MIuMFa8KBhlYHqLXepj41MK22327qu7YuAeUTX\nz2GhoTWmI2RIZ0R/bhYLQMAS1cWD2SA/vapXfALvLtSLzCN0coqbFh/698xXxjM9\nFSNn76r5NAuf/VEPdFSmqGCUn9GEQnKaiTwh3SHFD64K3oq76tkQhoFNycVpJpJ2\nf29bBbbfbMiC2GB45GtxusXrwTKBj8TigDc7gPltsE8NoAnhNW9d6R7fD28siWGZ\nrhTaQIPOFi7JY9P5DmHl\n=f7kb\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-18T15:25:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}