thub.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/b56339dc0748c33c2857fcdff45bf5321994b81d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-18T14:26:53Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"Halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-18T14:26:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(compose): auth-service SERVICE_CLIENT_USER_SERVICE_SECRET env wire-up (OI-03 canary blocker) (#484)\n\n2026-04-18 OI-03 canary setup execution revealed a compose env chain gap:\n`SERVICE_CLIENT_USER_SERVICE_SECRET` (P1.8 service token mint contract, PR\n#447) was set in canonical env but NOT passed to auth-service container.\n\nAuth-service ServiceTokenController reads `security.service-clients.user-service`\nvia application.properties `${SERVICE_CLIENT_USER_SERVICE_SECRET:}`. Without\ncontainer env the fallback is empty → no clients registered →\n`/oauth2/token` always returns 401 invalid_client.\n\nBlocked `zanzibar-canary-setup.mjs` userServiceProvision step (mint service\ntoken for audience=user-service) — canary evidence path gated.\n\nFix: wire `SERVICE_CLIENT_USER_SERVICE_SECRET` + `PERMISSION_SERVICE_INTERNAL_API_KEY`\n(same contract class) into auth-service compose block with canonical env\npass-through pattern.\n\nRelated: this is the same drift class the 5 Codex Thread 5 follow-up PRs\n(#479-#483) addressed for other env chain mismatches (ERP_OPENFGA_*,\nSECURITY_JWT_ISSUER, etc.). Same root cause, just one more symptom.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"870e1dc07f4fa6f8ffe43029c9572183695a18d9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/trees/870e1dc07f4fa6f8ffe43029c9572183695a18d9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/commits/b56339dc0748c33c2857fcdff45bf5321994b81d","verification":{"payload":"tree 870e1dc07f4fa6f8ffe43029c9572183695a18d9\nparent c60b60bf73c4c7d4af6f765b2f869ad89f3f3f32\nauthor Halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1776522413 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1776522413 +0300\n\nfix(compose): auth-service SERVICE_CLIENT_USER_SERVICE_SECRET env wire-up (OI-03 canary blocker) (#484)\n\n2026-04-18 OI-03 canary setup execution revealed a compose env chain gap:\n`SERVICE_CLIENT_USER_SERVICE_SECRET` (P1.8 service token mint contract, PR\n#447) was set in canonical env but NOT passed to auth-service container.\n\nAuth-service ServiceTokenController reads `security.service-clients.user-service`\nvia application.properties `${SERVICE_CLIENT_USER_SERVICE_SECRET:}`. Without\ncontainer env the fallback is empty → no clients registered →\n`/oauth2/token` always returns 401 invalid_client.\n\nBlocked `zanzibar-canary-setup.mjs` userServiceProvision step (mint service\ntoken for audience=user-service) — canary evidence path gated.\n\nFix: wire `SERVICE_CLIENT_USER_SERVICE_SECRET` + `PERMISSION_SERVICE_INTERNAL_API_KEY`\n(same contract class) into auth-service compose block with canonical env\npass-through pattern.\n\nRelated: this is the same drift class the 5 Codex Thread 5 follow-up PRs\n(#479-#483) addressed for other env chain mismatches (ERP_OPENFGA_*,\nSECURITY_JWT_ISSUER, etc.). Same root cause, just one more symptom.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp45StCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADTMQAB3YpG8jnhLNDnkzrTR7leQT\nxZntfuwZTWym1F96WD9EpYjxdgal+0PsswiORpnU8RancwsoHLZsBo52J39qc0me\nRy1aIkX60NjwOQRHMrkGS/eJiNMiKtL6Z+3ElWlPpVFz7Y8xe2tW7i8lRij6c2bN\nNIv5jZatQMBcraFtG12hROJdU85F2SG/QM52FxR7+h8Jo/05FjUk5YAfU7Ce0eW8\nHjrq5FEgndKLC/yhEmGyJCATiC7NGmTEU6YzP5w/BbrR37MeD6Ip0ldGfNunQeU1\nxhxdHFFx8aaHrKEtPClJIZqLlm+JMhd0o+/uoi24A0HIO9ayjyam3ROA8ec1BlOi\nowMolicF2qfpfDWkJ