r":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186576227?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/c60b60bf73c4c7d4af6f765b2f869ad89f3f3f32/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-18T13:48:38Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"Halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-18T13:48:38Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(deploy): BACKEND_HEALTH_URLS edge-path validation in post-deploy-health-check (Codex Thread 5 #5) (#483)\n\n2026-04-18 Codex Thread 5 finding #5: post-deploy-health-check.sh validated\ncontainer-internal health (docker inspect, Vault seal, OpenFGA /healthz)\nbut NOT the public edge paths defined by BACKEND_HEALTH_URLS. The GH\nActions post-deploy-validate workflow does probe that secret, but host-\nside script was silent on it — false-green risk when container healthy\nbut edge path broken (e.g. 2026-04-18 nginx 502 incident class).\n\nThis commit adds Step 5: if BACKEND_HEALTH_URLS env set, parse comma-\nseparated list and probe each:\n- 200/204: healthy\n- 301/302: redirect to login — healthy (route works)\n- 401/403: auth gate — healthy (route works, just requires auth)\n- anything else: FAIL with status code\n- curl exit != 0: FAIL with exit code\n\nUnset variable emits a note (not failure) — local dev doesn''t need this.\n\nMirrors the GH Actions workflow probe logic so drift between the two paths\nsurfaces immediately on deploy host.\n\nCodex review: thread 019da045 drift hunt #5.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9efd883be773a6e769400eafcba79d09d34948a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/trees/9efd883be773a6e769400eafcba79d09d34948a4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/commits/c60b60bf73c4c7d4af6f765b2f869ad89f3f3f32","verification":{"payload":"tree 9efd883be773a6e769400eafcba79d09d34948a4\nparent 146eba4c10464af5b3c028dca678199f1fc12e5d\nauthor Halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1776520118 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1776520118 +0300\n\nfeat(deploy): BACKEND_HEALTH_URLS edge-path validation in post-deploy-health-check (Codex Thread 5 #5) (#483)\n\n2026-04-18 Codex Thread 5 finding #5: post-deploy-health-check.sh validated\ncontainer-internal health (docker inspect, Vault seal, OpenFGA /healthz)\nbut NOT the public edge paths defined by BACKEND_HEALTH_URLS. The GH\nActions post-deploy-validate workflow does probe that secret, but host-\nside script was silent on it — false-green risk when container healthy\nbut edge path broken (e.g. 2026-04-18 nginx 502 incident class).\n\nThis commit adds Step 5: if BACKEND_HEALTH_URLS env set, parse comma-\nseparated list and probe each:\n- 200/204: healthy\n- 301/302: redirect to login — healthy (route works)\n- 401/403: auth gate — healthy (route works, just requires auth)\n- anything else: FAIL with status code\n- curl exit != 0: FAIL with exit code\n\nUnset variable emits a note (not failure) — local dev doesn''t need this.\n\nMirrors the GH Actions workflow probe logic so drift between the two paths\nsurfaces immediately on deploy host.\n\nCodex review: thread 019da045 drift hunt #5.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp44u2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiqIQAIeqsFL3CHlXth7EBfYd2KA9\nEQW9wMY38Cg8JfO/Ah60QKQRaGQMihvkK1BRTZ8s6YY55KdVcHbJEJfThQXZfGX0\naikPi1Jcl8YOTzxkVt1ESgnDZZgEy2Z/sUMI5dQqH9SykzV1pSrW0aiiL/2pTwCL\nucuIZeqAhCx5+waPBALEbIvw0hYLiw5GbUmst8cj3eGq+h1gRcSjtiymYzUkuhdt\nca8hiB22WtIIUT+poRFfuy/9+MDu+6pex40HrlsHX8exUMHIC1xJxrYPXY8/oE8M\nOxEvF+O3kc+5sve/+42qiCB7dvDHhNMyysQNEF59G6TM9ww3a5wxTfMBgDrp1ujk\nM5d47TUtWepSkFyzPDAKqExB5Su4j+zMMB6LiqjjeDfYA1qF26PzF6KfOO0Xzalm\nIu+bO3C5M04wW5pb69Yu3/U/qC5OAUaLXguxGBx4QZeNwfczqk+tWRn8L40iWBOe\nqsCkz8/QdJZpqbv1kD1Cb5o0kBk7ynZcb+XeGPc5wNee32zpIZ3+As77Le+M5jwH\nX/pu/AFeU3wJ66Lb+jc3EleUQuS9WzJ6+TwwQzhXnOUZcNXVB+qgoX+5617NKKs9\nAaqNbziYVJrVVsRpHE9g2AKmD44jwcb9aQ0AADZzbOCxYMNPFzYddxxWSz/x8i5R\nakl/tuDi8GE1354ibJb2\n=BuWO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-18T13:48:39Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commit/c60b60bf73c4c7d4af6f765b2f869ad89f3f3f32","node_id":"C_kwDOQooUwNoAKGM2MGI2MGJmNzNjNGM3ZDRhZjZmNzY1YjJmODY5YWQ4OWYzZjNmMzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commit/146eba4c10464af5b3c028dca678199f1fc12e5d","sha":"146eba4c10464af5b3c028dca678199f1fc12e5d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/146eba4c10464af5b3c028dca678199f1fc12e5d"}],"sha":"c60b60bf73c4c7d4af6f765b2f869ad89f3f3f32","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/c60b60bf73c4c7d4af6f765b2f869ad89f3f3f32"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186576227?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/146eba4c10464af5b3c028dca678199f1fc12e5d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-18T13:42:56Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"Halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-18T13:42:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(compose): schema-service reads SCHEMA_MSSQL_* canonical (Codex Thread 5 #3) (#481)\n\n2026-04-18 Codex Thread 5 finding #3 (stage vs prod contract drift):\nschema-service in backend/docker-compose.yml was reading REPORT_MSSQL_*\nenv vars directly, ignoring the canonical SCHEMA_MSSQL_* contract that\nprod compose + canonical env + write-backend-deploy-stage.sh all use.\n\nResult: stage and prod schema-service had divergent behaviour — stage\nhardcoded to REPORT_MSSQL_* (MSSQL reporting DB), prod wired to\nSCHEMA_MSSQL_* (dedicated schema DB). Operators updating SCHEMA_MSSQL_*\nin canonical env saw no effect on stage schema-service.\n\nFix: chain `${SCHEMA_MSSQL_*:-${REPORT_MSSQL_*:-<default>}}`:\n- Primary: explicit SCHEMA_MSSQL_* from canonical env (prod-aligned)\n- Fallback 1: REPORT_MSSQL_* (legacy stage behaviour — non-breaking)\n- Fallback 2: hardcoded local dev defaults\n\nThis preserves existing stage behaviour while enabling canonical env to\noverride. Prod compose (deploy/docker-compose.prod.yml) uses SCHEMA_MSSQL_*\ndirectly, unchanged.\n\nCodex review: thread 019da045 drift hunt #3.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"789d899da702f91b0144443ecae82eebc07b66d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/trees/789d899da702f91b0144443ecae82eebc07b66d6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/commits/146eba4c10464af5b3c028dca678199f1fc12e5d","verification":{"payload":"tree 789d899da702f91b0144443ecae82eebc07b66d6\nparent 22e6b50c0afb6c5ef41c62edd99c57f71405fc57\nauthor Halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1776519776 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1776519776 +0300\n\nfix(compose): schema-service reads SCHEMA_MSSQL_* canonical (Codex Thread 5 #3) (#481)\n\n2026-04-18 Codex Thread 5 finding #3 (stage vs prod contract drift):\nschema-service in backend/docker-compose.yml was reading REPORT_MSSQL_*\nenv vars directly, ignoring the canonical SCHEMA_MSSQL_* contract that\nprod compose + canonical env + write-backend-deploy-stage.sh all use.\n\nResult: stage and prod schema-service had divergent behaviour — stage\nhardcoded to REPORT_MSSQL_* (MSSQL reporting DB), prod wired to\nSCHEMA_MSSQL_* (dedicated schema DB). Operators updating SCHEMA_MSSQL_*\nin canonical env saw no effect on stage schema-service.\n\nFix: chain `${SCHEMA_MSSQL_*:-${REPORT_MSSQL_*:-<default>}}`:\n- Primary: explicit SCHEMA_MSSQL_* from canonical env (prod-aligned)\n- Fallback 1: REPORT_MSSQL_* (legacy stage behaviour — non-breaking)\n- Fallback 2: hardcoded local dev defaults\n\nThis preserves existing stage behaviour while enabling canonical env to\noverride. Prod compose (deploy/docker-compose.prod.yml) uses SCHEMA_MSSQL_*\ndirectly, unchanged.\n\nCodex review: thread 019da045 drift hunt #3.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp44pgCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUfAQAJvF1zFS9d9x9ORnFGttPj3U\npoAVxHyqcyjNEspI4Eena3K5OiVRF5wAtsSM3G9MTQ7TrW1i/yN6I/NuBdNYHCaU\nuv8EuHvLCUvKlxu3O0PseTFsz4KvIi8J/p9eiuN17QtUjS/60SR8imD7bZ6+BPAD\n4/cGtOGw+2KSfcwFIr5rR89gwRRfvihHY7Br0HZyRCL7Y50Kx4UwofUwVxYHAduv\nADE73WCm9Ne4uEqjhn7OyypKRBRH6eBDhnoxgM9Y4uRccgWaJZ43/UocBhoYiRP+\nkWpnWOgiUKfZTxhPTYWsI2My39E/zCGriOBq4LVJj9OnVNYj/jZcUML5yytCoOoi\nK5r40LClfgCjnraagKIN6NInqpW0P3Pwkg0pHmx8HW7UCFxSCQZn0M7mpmegKysC\nL1ZqwBUuR1nrBxJD0eeH+JvCgmHwcYC6fq7BuJCVFibrcSWE71thpcaVIZ8eYNSI\n6jXgXH1/2LvmJAWZ14QRix4M5tqZX/779XpoXDyKwkFsvMAOhZkhasmIn0dQ+YwK\n9Zyz2U1i1WYSyL8s9E3xnmVDL7hCgO1OXth5WL5rfsv3tgVXHwwIePcKk9NqxGU2\n5DCIaxVsLSFglNHqMNJmzdhTXz1qwgIy5zD+/o3kL4CMAF8K4zF6voP1HQDlO9Ph\ncrklp00Y0QmXR+jYCAZa\n=7NO3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-18T13:42:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commit/146eba4c10464af5b3c028dca678199f1fc12e5d","node_id":"C_kwDOQooUwNoAKDE0NmViYTRjMTA0NjRhZjViM2MwMjhkY2E2NzgxOTlmMWZjMTJlNWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commit/22e6b50c0afb6c5ef41c62edd99c57f71405fc57","sha":"22e6b50c0afb6c5ef41c62edd99c57f71405fc57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/22e6b50c0afb6c5ef41c62edd99c57f71405fc57"}],"sha":"146eba4c10464af5b3c028dca678199f1fc12e5d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/146eba4c10464af5b3c028dca678199f1fc12e5d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186576227?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/22e6b50c0afb6c5ef41c62edd99c57f71405fc57/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-18T13:37:07Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"Halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-18T13:37:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(render): DB schema dual-read — canonical + spring.datasource.* alias (Codex Thread 5 #2) (#480)\n\n2026-04-18 Codex Thread 5 finding #2: staging Vault KV at\n`secret/stage/db/auth-service` historically seeded with Spring-style\n`{spring.datasource.url, spring.datasource.username, spring.datasource.password}`,\nbut render-backend-env.sh expected canonical `{url, user, password}` triple.\nEmpty reads → AUTH_SERVICE_DB_* env vars silently absent → services fall\nback to shared POSTGRES_USER/PASSWORD. Per-service isolation lost, no\ndoctor signal.\n\nThis commit adds `kv_dual_read` helper that tries canonical first, falls\nback to spring.datasource.* alias. Fix is backward-compatible:\n- New paths (written via `write-secrets-stage.sh`) use canonical schema\n- Legacy paths with spring.datasource.* get picked up transparently\n- Operators don''t need to rewrite historical KV to benefit\n\nAfter this lands, staging per-service DB env populated as canonical env:\n  AUTH_SERVICE_DB_USERNAME=postgres  (was empty pre-fix)\n  AUTH_SERVICE_DB_PASSWORD=<from spring.datasource.password>  (was empty)\n  USER_SERVICE_DB_*, PERMISSION_SERVICE_DB_*, VARIANT_SERVICE_DB_* similarly.\n\nWrite path (`backend/scripts/vault/write-secrets-stage.sh`) remains canonical\n`{url, user, password}` — fresh seeds use canonical.\n\nCodex review: thread 019da045 drift hunt #2.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6f5299ef9510bb16d8d1c68c722bd320386e7bbe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/trees/6f5299ef9510bb16d8d1c68c722bd320386e7bbe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/commits/22e6b50c0afb6c5ef41c62edd99c57f71405fc57","verification":{"payload":"tree 6f5299ef9510bb16d8d1c68c722bd320386e7bbe\nparent da6b72e22f3879b684b04c019c8954dedb7a6bb0\nauthor Halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1776519427 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1776519427 +0300\n\nfix(render): DB schema dual-read — canonical + spring.datasource.* alias (Codex Thread 5 #2) (#480)\n\n2026-04-18 Codex Thread 5 finding #2: staging Vault KV at\n`secret/stage/db/auth-service` historically seeded with Spring-style\n`{spring.datasource.url, spring.datasource.username, spring.datasource.password}`,\nbut render-backend-env.sh expected canonical `{url, user, password}` triple.\nEmpty reads → AUTH_SERVICE_DB_* env vars silently absent → services fall\nback to shared POSTGRES_USER/PASSWORD. Per-service isolation lost, no\ndoctor signal.\n\nThis commit adds `kv_dual_read` helper that tries canonical first, falls\nback to spring.datasource.* alias. Fix is backward-compatible:\n- New paths (written via `write-secrets-stage.sh`) use canonical schema\n- Legacy paths with spring.datasource.* get picked up transparently\n- Operators don''t need to rewrite historical KV to benefit\n\nAfter this lands, staging per-service DB env populated as canonical env:\n  AUTH_SERVICE_DB_USERNAME=postgres  (was empty pre-fix)\n  AUTH_SERVICE_DB_PASSWORD=<from spring.datasource.password>  (was empty)\n  USER_SERVICE_DB_*, PERMISSION_SERVICE_DB_*, VARIANT_SERVICE_DB_* similarly.\n\nWrite path (`backend/scripts/vault/write-secrets-stage.sh`) remains canonical\n`{url, user, password}` — fresh seeds use canonical.\n\nCodex review: thread 019da045 drift hunt #2.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp44kDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjosQAE/O7QSB5C9ETfCTXpgP+LCi\nkl6cZDQsPQX8OnyPa45ehC0svKQzyaIVYdm0IgA8Ba2LyOs/m7SPLa88m1KFX+DW\n9uLhxsaSDeje3WP1FkpNCsgQrKjr1Ca0TXDAaYA2JiOM5fiszk9ylyXnMfhla0E7\n1/emkfX9BKoQDKMLh4P99cm3w8qCJDDyOAVJoDtVkvvBS7UooeXJvMdc+F2/38Mr\nbckcHTzZksdzlZk6mwYwIQoQLXQi0ImpgPhg2Q2diADuCOJJMfGNwNbFKQMwdA+v\nY+dUSuN904qEwqhfcZTQcN4IM4PIXaKdHp0U+SYygB6YuG+ycFzXIdk4wrje509l\n3an/87TCcduRfO+LBQ/yj7spyWnXVAWq6LUK4SQw7xVIkESvHN1EXZGyV+8KRlUe\noEEIVVShk2CDyLlOYmy2pmcaFyHIApUwTxjgtXT8ORxKTy7YtnwZwYtZdHf/mxwn\ntwsRliOkGDuCz6NyeXv/P3PiuD152rP+j6tJHy3Jr+bGINFSoc1H2tYL0rp8QL15\nlkofbmwAji47AEKDQ/XpG06SrdtyuUvBUekZmOeXUVPU37OseuKp+7Y2gQGVTPEE\nvibF0VYNzD+tZ2Bqv/x6ZCx98eTLmObbkHLHKNKMUBWIYgiXspAv7BMDEIms8rDU\npZQ4U0ob0329s+A5BeGR\n=Ge5y\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-18T13:37:08Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commit/22e6b50c0afb6c5ef41c62edd99c57f71405fc57","node_id":"C_kwDOQooUwNoAKDIyZTZiNTBjMGFmYjZjNWVmNDFjNjJlZGQ5OWM1N2Y3MTQwNWZjNTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commit/da6b72e22f3879b684b04c019c8954dedb7a6bb0","sha":"da6b72e22f3879b684b04c019c8954dedb7a6bb0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/da6b72e22f3879b684b04c019c8954dedb7a6bb0"}],"sha":"22e6b50c0afb6c5ef41c62edd99c57f71405fc57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/22e6b50c0afb6c5ef41c62edd99c57f71405fc57"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186576227?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/da6b72e22f3879b684b04c019c8954dedb7a6bb0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-18T13:30:09Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"Halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-18T13:30:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(render-approle): state file preflight + age warn + login error hints (Codex Thread 5 #4) (#482)\n\n2026-04-18 Codex Thread 5 finding #4: AppRole render wrapper (render-backend-\nenv-approle.sh) body was reading state files blindly. Missing file produced\npython3 traceback; TTL-expired secret-id produced opaque `curl exit=22`\nfrom the Vault login endpoint. Operator had to guess root cause.\n\nThis commit adds three layers of explicit diagnostics:\n\n**1. preflight_state_files (runs first):**\n- File existence check — clear \"state file missing\" with operator action\n- Non-empty check — catches truncated/corrupt files\n- Age check (WARN only) — if file older than 25 days, hint that\n  secret-id TTL (default 768h = 32d) is approaching. Gives operator a\n  buffer to re-seed before login actually fails.\n\n**2. Login wrapper with curl exit capture:**\n- Previous: `curl -sSf ... -d \"$payload\"` — exit 22 on HTTP error, but no\n  context why.\n- Now: wrapped in `|| { curl_exit=$?; echo helpful; exit 1; }` showing\n  role_id prefix (for diffing against Vault server state) + remediation\n  command.\n\n**3. Empty client_token response hint:**\n- Shows response body snippet (200 chars) for JSON parse debugging.\n\nNo auto-rotate — that needs root/service token the wrapper doesn''t have.\nSignal is early and loud so operator can act before the canary/deploy\nwindow burns.\n\nCodex review: thread 019da045 drift hunt #4.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"afd791808beaeda0642567d46a9c2e1f638abfe3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/trees/afd791808beaeda0642567d46a9c2e1f638abfe3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/commits/da6b72e22f3879b684b04c019c8954dedb7a6bb0","verification":{"payload":"tree afd791808beaeda0642567d46a9c2e1f638abfe3\nparent c90e737954186a13b24e06f77e878ca4c3c5d9bf\nauthor Halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1776519009 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1776519009 +0300\n\nfix(render-approle): state file preflight + age warn + login error hints (Codex Thread 5 #4) (#482)\n\n2026-04-18 Codex Thread 5 finding #4: AppRole render wrapper (render-backend-\nenv-approle.sh) body was reading state files blindly. Missing file produced\npython3 traceback; TTL-expired secret-id produced opaque `curl exit=22`\nfrom the Vault login endpoint. Operator had to guess root cause.\n\nThis commit adds three layers of explicit diagnostics:\n\n**1. preflight_state_files (runs first):**\n- File existence check — clear \"state file missing\" with operator action\n- Non-empty check — catches truncated/corrupt files\n- Age check (WARN only) — if file older than 25 days, hint that\n  secret-id TTL (default 768h = 32d) is approaching. Gives operator a\n  buffer to re-seed before login actually fails.\n\n**2. Login wrapper with curl exit capture:**\n- Previous: `curl -sSf ... -d \"$payload\"` — exit 22 on HTTP error, but no\n  context why.\n- Now: wrapped in `|| { curl_exit=$?; echo helpful; exit 1; }` showing\n  role_id prefix (for diffing against Vault server state) + remediation\n  command.\n\n**3. Empty client_token response hint:**\n- Shows response body snippet (200 chars) for JSON parse debugging.\n\nNo auto-rotate — that needs root/service token the wrapper doesn''t have.\nSignal is early and loud so operator can act before the canary/deploy\nwindow burns.\n\nCodex review: thread 019da045 drift hunt #4.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp44dhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAzQQAI5na9s2MLUcg2esJoHsBKZw\ngAz8pc4GVg1EGFRZPorlHfEASVWRPjDdn86E1572d0pDO3+AAHY2uFqJgXcXLFno\nurIjmP80kdpyijH2XSqwiCwApwTOrjSpC+h2vwVPJrNZIYOfxgDI+G09bPD15YJx\nsDD3gb4Wf5sRaYS5vs1aRkBiZRyHYV1latHICN1Nz1QWoCPxbwsf3Vot/zmRR3Ak\n6aHuXxnO8SDsyOapiQpvxZciS68J+G3JPBT/9tottdvPz5HzLE8FmPEVYBrkeft9\nEEklsRZVAhxZXMbhQYxJRX6GrQTkUgrszgFEhjXYHt1RIgc/wssQHP7jWduF3BWl\n7S85GnXB9ZxwGDYW1wsbJL7rmGHqJsq3D2BMUgDWbfb2ml297KsjVmCQZrXEIzj9\ngiit3UJK64ogGszHAom2IDRCNK6eP27kDE0t+TaPp3lMCsFRDK+TpZOQvQL2qvC8\nvUWCD+XYnaWlZpDQPl414MZBgLjncJiu8XTy5i9ZHf7eMgsHtBWdhgai/REWdwPM\nc5O6r1tzvMw6AYH07D3Cbig17ER6JPt0c0oGO3CvxzorD6fQ0WKD3okQFcLpRuqk\nC356MxSLLtHQiMIc2HUuV8smUIzf7vQ5NtfGWGrb3jaYEdDWOdIw3JyUkUsifQ5J\nbf/WuYwrqIYok7w5GNMN\n=y7n3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-18T13:30:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commit/da6b72e22f3879b684b04c019c8954dedb7a6bb0","node_id":"C_kwDOQooUwNoAKGRhNmI3MmUyMmYzODc5YjY4NGIwNGMwMTljODk1NGRlZGI3YTZiYjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commit/c90e737954186a13b24e06f77e878ca4c3c5d9bf","sha":"c90e737954186a13b24e06f77e878ca4c3c5d9bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/c90e737954186a13b24e06f77e878ca4c3c5d9bf"}],"sha":"da6b72e22f3879b684b04c019c8954dedb7a6bb0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/da6b72e22f3879b684b04c019c8954dedb7a6bb0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186576227?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/c90e737954186a13b24e06f77e878ca4c3c5d9bf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-18T13:06:58Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"Halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-18T13:06:58Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(canary): preflight fail-closed — tools + reachability + env gates (OI-03) (#479)\n\n* feat(canary): preflight fail-closed — tools + reachability + env gates (OI-03 unblock)\n\n2026-04-18 Codex Thread 5 finding #5 (preflight eksik): run-zanzibar-canary.sh\nstarts expensive setup + k6 orchestration without verifying host has required\nCLI tools or that target URLs respond. Failures surface mid-stream as\n\"node: not found\" or curl connection errors, masking the actual drift and\nwasting minutes of canary runtime.\n\nThis commit adds a [0/10] PREFLIGHT block that runs BEFORE any orchestration\nwork, fail-closed, producing clear diagnostics upfront:\n\n**Step A — Required CLI tools:**\n- Always: bash, curl, python3\n- When SKIP_SETUP!=1: +node (zanzibar-canary-setup.mjs)\n- When ESTIMATE_ONLY!=1 OR SKIP_SETUP!=1: +k6\n- When SKIP_METRICS!=1: +jq (guardrail-check)\n- Missing tools → print install hints (apt + k6 official docs URL).\n\n**Step B — BASE_URL reachability:**\n- curl exit-code first (DNS/connection failure catch)\n- --max-redirs 0 prevents %{http_code} concat weirdness on redirect chains\n- Any HTTP status = reachable (401/404/500 all pass here; route works)\n\n**Step C — Prometheus reachability:**\n- Only when SKIP_METRICS!=1\n- GET /-/healthy must return 200\n- Skip hint for local smoke runs.\n\n**Step D — OPENFGA_STORE_ID env:**\n- Required by setup script (persona seed needs store id)\n- Staging canonical env has this; missing = operator forgot to export\n\n**Step E — Canary client secrets (WARN only):**\n- KC_CANARY_CLIENT_SECRET or SERVICE_CLIENT_USER_SERVICE_SECRET\n- Setup has fallback logic; WARN if neither set\n\nExit 1 with blocker count before any network or orchestration I/O. Tested\nlocally: unreachable BASE_URL caught with clear `curl exit=6` message.\n\nRelated: Codex thread 019da045 (R5 post-mortem deep review), unblocks OI-03\ncanary run path once staging tooling is installed (separate ops).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(fec): cover run-zanzibar-canary.sh path (CI unblock PR #479)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d43be4bafb2c1eccb0a20d814efb8bddd70131f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/trees/d43be4bafb2c1eccb0a20d814efb8bddd70131f3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/commits/c90e737954186a13b24e06f77e878ca4c3c5d9bf","verification":{"payload":"tree d43be4bafb2c1eccb0a20d814efb8bddd70131f3\nparent d0163f49ce28356c102cf79213a726a0dbcec998\nauthor Halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1776517618 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1776517618 +0300\n\nfeat(canary): preflight fail-closed — tools + reachability + env gates (OI-03) (#479)\n\n* feat(canary): preflight fail-closed — tools + reachability + env gates (OI-03 unblock)\n\n2026-04-18 Codex Thread 5 finding #5 (preflight eksik): run-zanzibar-canary.sh\nstarts expensive setup + k6 orchestration without verifying host has required\nCLI tools or that target URLs respond. Failures surface mid-stream as\n\"node: not found\" or curl connection errors, masking the actual drift and\nwasting minutes of canary runtime.\n\nThis commit adds a [0/10] PREFLIGHT block that runs BEFORE any orchestration\nwork, fail-closed, producing clear diagnostics upfront:\n\n**Step A — Required CLI tools:**\n- Always: bash, curl, python3\n- When SKIP_SETUP!=1: +node (zanzibar-canary-setup.mjs)\n- When ESTIMATE_ONLY!=1 OR SKIP_SETUP!=1: +k6\n- When SKIP_METRICS!=1: +jq (guardrail-check)\n- Missing tools → print install hints (apt + k6 official docs URL).\n\n**Step B — BASE_URL reachability:**\n- curl exit-code first (DNS/connection failure catch)\n- --max-redirs 0 prevents %{http_code} concat weirdness on redirect chains\n- Any HTTP status = reachable (401/404/500 all pass here; route works)\n\n**Step C — Prometheus reachability:**\n- Only when SKIP_METRICS!=1\n- GET /-/healthy must return 200\n- Skip hint for local smoke runs.\n\n**Step D — OPENFGA_STORE_ID env:**\n- Required by setup script (persona seed needs store id)\n- Staging canonical env has this; missing = operator forgot to export\n\n**Step E — Canary client secrets (WARN only):**\n- KC_CANARY_CLIENT_SECRET or SERVICE_CLIENT_USER_SERVICE_SECRET\n- Setup has fallback logic; WARN if neither set\n\nExit 1 with blocker count before any network or orchestration I/O. Tested\nlocally: unreachable BASE_URL caught with clear `curl exit=6` message.\n\nRelated: Codex thread 019da045 (R5 post-mortem deep review), unblocks OI-03\ncanary run path once staging tooling is installed (separate ops).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(fec): cover run-zanzibar-canary.sh path (CI unblock PR #479)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp44HyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACCMQABZs/gGkVZbFYAGP3VouK59j\