f79213a726a0dbcec998","sha":"d0163f49ce28356c102cf79213a726a0dbcec998","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/d0163f49ce28356c102cf79213a726a0dbcec998"}],"sha":"c90e737954186a13b24e06f77e878ca4c3c5d9bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/c90e737954186a13b24e06f77e878ca4c3c5d9bf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186576227?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/d0163f49ce28356c102cf79213a726a0dbcec998/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-18T10:52:59Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"Halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-18T10:52:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(deploy): render/write/check chain — add 5 missing keys (Drift #2 rehearsal #4 root cause) (#478)\n\n2026-04-18 Drift #2 Rehearsal #4 (post-render fail-closed flip) revealed 3\npost-deploy doctor-infra FAILs:\n- L4 ERP_OPENFGA_STORE_ID empty in report-service container\n- L5 ERP_OPENFGA_MODEL_ID empty\n- L8 SECURITY_JWT_ISSUER does not contain ''ai.acik.com''\n\nRoot cause: The write/render/check chain was missing 5 canonical keys.\nEven though the render-backend-env.sh write was technically successful\nafter PR #477 (write_kv_if_present return 0 fix), the canonical env it\nproduced lacked these 5 keys because:\n- `ordered_keys`: 2 OPENFGA_* present, ERP_OPENFGA_* absent\n- `required_keys`: no drift guard for missing ISSUER/AUTHZ_USER_TABLE\n- `write-backend-deploy-stage.sh` payload: same 5 keys missing\n\nResolution (Codex thread 019da02f REVISE):\n\n**`deploy/ubuntu/render-backend-env.sh`:**\n- `required_keys`: +5 keys. Ensures fail-closed on missing Vault KV.\n- `ordered_keys`: +5 keys. Ensures canonical env write.\n\n**`backend/scripts/vault/write-backend-deploy-stage.sh`:**\n- payload: +5 keys (`ERP_OPENFGA_STORE_ID`, `ERP_OPENFGA_MODEL_ID`,\n  `SECURITY_JWT_ISSUER`, `SECURITY_JWT_ISSUERS`, `AUTHZ_USER_TABLE`).\n  Operator must export these before invocation (no default values).\n\n**`backend/scripts/vault/check-backend-deploy-stage.sh`:**\n- `config_required`: +3 keys (ERP_OPENFGA_STORE_ID/MODEL_ID + AUTHZ_USER_TABLE).\n  SECURITY_JWT_ISSUER/ISSUERS already added in PR #469.\n\nSemantic notes:\n- `ERP_OPENFGA_*` = compose-level service config contract (report-service\n  application.yml, core-data-service). `OPENFGA_*` = legacy tooling contract\n  (canary setup, backend/openfga/init.sh). Duplicates acceptable and\n  necessary (Codex verified both paths active).\n- `SECURITY_JWT_ISSUER` must be public URL (https://ai.acik.com/realms/serban)\n  — report-service reads ISSUER (not ISSUERS) so public issuer is mandatory\n  here, not in ISSUERS alone.\n- `AUTHZ_USER_TABLE` explicit value removes compose-default dependency —\n  drift guard rigor.\n\nNext ops (separate commit): populate staging canonical env + re-run\n`write-backend-deploy-stage.sh` + re-trigger deploy. Post-deploy doctor\nL4/L5/L8 expected to pass.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f07c57ee68d8cd50fc53d5d7eb4be8fadb0c9d85","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/trees/f07c57ee68d8cd50fc53d5d7eb4be8fadb0c9d85"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/commits/d0163f49ce28356c102cf79213a726a0dbcec998","verification":{"payload":"tree f07c57ee68d8cd50fc53d5d7eb4be8fadb0c9d85\nparent 1b66a0db4774678e1cd741093bd1bf0490386e8f\nauthor Halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1776509579 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1776509579 +0300\n\nfix(deploy): render/write/check chain — add 5 missing keys (Drift #2 rehearsal #4 root cause) (#478)\n\n2026-04-18 Drift #2 Rehearsal #4 (post-render fail-closed flip) revealed 3\npost-deploy doctor-infra FAILs:\n- L4 ERP_OPENFGA_STORE_ID empty in report-service container\n- L5 ERP_OPENFGA_MODEL_ID empty\n- L8 SECURITY_JWT_ISSUER does not contain ''ai.acik.com''\n\nRoot cause: The write/render/check chain was missing 5 canonical keys.\nEven though the render-backend-env.sh write was technically successful\nafter PR #477 (write_kv_if_present return 0 fix), the canonical env it\nproduced lacked these 5 keys because:\n- `ordered_keys`: 2 OPENFGA_* present, ERP_OPENFGA_* absent\n- `required_keys`: no drift guard for missing ISSUER/AUTHZ_USER_TABLE\n- `write-backend-deploy-stage.sh` payload: same 5 keys missing\n\nResolution (Codex thread 019da02f REVISE):\n\n**`deploy/ubuntu/render-backend-env.sh`:**\n- `required_keys`: +5 keys. Ensures fail-closed on missing Vault KV.\n- `ordered_keys`: +5 keys. Ensures canonical env write.\n\n**`backend/scripts/vault/write-backend-deploy-stage.sh`:**\n- payload: +5 keys (`ERP_OPENFGA_STORE_ID`, `ERP_OPENFGA_MODEL_ID`,\n  `SECURITY_JWT_ISSUER`, `SECURITY_JWT_ISSUERS`, `AUTHZ_USER_TABLE`).\n  Operator must export these before invocation (no default values).\n\n**`backend/scripts/vault/check-backend-deploy-stage.sh`:**\n- `config_required`: +3 keys (ERP_OPENFGA_STORE_ID/MODEL_ID + AUTHZ_USER_TABLE).\n  SECURITY_JWT_ISSUER/ISSUERS already added in PR #469.\n\nSemantic notes:\n- `ERP_OPENFGA_*` = compose-level service config contract (report-service\n  application.yml, core-data-service). `OPENFGA_*` = legacy tooling contract\n  (canary setup, backend/openfga/init.sh). Duplicates acceptable and\n  necessary (Codex verified both paths active).\n- `SECURITY_JWT_ISSUER` must be public URL (https://ai.acik.com/realms/serban)\n  — report-service reads ISSUER (not ISSUERS) so public issuer is mandatory\n  here, not in ISSUERS alone.\n- `AUTHZ_USER_TABLE` explicit value removes compose-default dependency —\n  drift guard rigor.\n\nNext ops (separate commit): populate staging canonical env + re-run\n`write-backend-deploy-stage.sh` + re-trigger deploy. Post-deploy doctor\nL4/L5/L8 expected to pass.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp42KLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAcPcQABG3o9c2iUC4LaCBOqBTBGpR\nlwtAYArSvewoq/B86b006BX7eHOg2FotWAe8fz5RTFy+8lTx90vulpPR0nV8zVTg\nryJ3azZ48OrEyhZycc3usk7lVWEkmOOmrP4+KkH/w/wWBkEsWP0F20YbQYpcGHAq\n8XOgCEtvxTiShusHmi8nKobh94AIT57Zh0Su+3LDhng1JRFWL8/lZ7FYPBFdKZ/c\ng2YIF2sGlHpAjzbvRwSSTrwMRGZQXoUrn1VjNfJ6B0U7m+dDWpc+DgOfYKsQygpA\nZK6UHm++3JDH892K12YUkz0WxVS5/MAs1UGNo0NauvWu0b0RB9UQuqVbF6rev17k\nsdBDvUm7aVR0J3zrsBzqk1u/mTZZWoWZV8Huv/d7EiwYN1wyhAeSrGcFX2XlzAhc\nxeceQ4wJbllfnj4d4z8H8pE2xhFJJCp7QW1eBizKbYDmioyaDA3EH05smROt8EqW\nLvMLkxnQcn176b5FD7rj4Q2pK3x/4tsOPS28TW34WexAgUaSXlLlHaW46n7F2FaP\nV6YbDxKSJUrSMmSfxbMsPiGzdk/cQzZfPFgQTdsOIdiiMqHFcjbuqrhKrw65glC0\nrvTuExYNclNVNVbVmn9CBtrplc4jox3+u4/ludMUMpha8YYpqTikoY3wlnXRj/xP\ny31hy2G+SYoDEb4ichtU\n=kIpq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-18T10:53:00Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commit/d0163f49ce28356c102cf79213a726a0dbcec998","node_id":"C_kwDOQooUwNoAKGQwMTYzZjQ5Y2UyODM1NmMxMDJjZjc5MjEzYTcyNmEwZGJjZWM5OTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commit/1b66a0db4774678e1cd741093bd1bf0490386e8f","sha":"1b66a0db4774678e1cd741093bd1bf0490386e8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/1b66a0db4774678e1cd741093bd1bf0490386e8f"}],"sha":"d0163f49ce28356c102cf79213a726a0dbcec998","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/d0163f49ce28356c102cf79213a726a0dbcec998"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186576227?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/1b66a0db4774678e1cd741093bd1bf0490386e8f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-18T10:11:47Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"Halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-18T10:11:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(render): write_kv_if_present explicit return 0 — silent script death fix (#477)\n\n2026-04-18 Drift #2 rehearsal FAIL root cause (Codex thread 019da008 deep review):\n\nPrevious:\n  write_kv_if_present() {\n    local file=\"$1\" key=\"$2\" val=\"$3\"\n    [[ -n \"${val}\" ]] && write_kv \"${file}\" \"${key}\" \"${val}\"\n  }\n\nWhen val is empty, `[[ -n \"\" ]]` returns false → `&&` short-circuits →\nfunction''s last command exit code is 1 → with `set -euo pipefail`, the\nscript DIES SILENTLY at the first empty-val call. No stderr, no mv, no\noutput file finalization.\n\nObserved failure: rehearsal deploy 24601989117 failed at deploy-backend.sh\nline 175 (render-backend-env-approle.sh exit=1) with NO render output in\nlog. Staging Vault KV has drifted schema (`spring.datasource.username` vs\nexpected `user`), so `kv_get_value \"${auth_db_payload}\" url` returned\nempty → first `write_kv_if_present AUTH_SERVICE_DB_URL \"\"` killed script.\n\nFix:\n  write_kv_if_present() {\n    local file=\"$1\" key=\"$2\" val=\"$3\"\n    if [[ -n \"${val}\" ]]; then\n      write_kv \"${file}\" \"${key}\" \"${val}\"\n    fi\n    return 0\n  }\n\nExplicit `return 0` ensures the \"empty = skip\" contract survives errexit.\nPer-service DB paths can now genuinely fall back to shared POSTGRES_USER/\nPASSWORD as the comment promises.\n\nNote: the underlying schema drift (`spring.datasource.*` vs `url/user/\npassword`) is a separate concern and will be addressed in a follow-up —\nthe current fix unblocks render so the shared-creds fallback path works.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"81eca126041caf37b91b5d4d20a2b2c3c7007586","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/trees/81eca126041caf37b91b5d4d20a2b2c3c7007586"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/commits/1b66a0db4774678e1cd741093bd1bf0490386e8f","verification":{"payload":"tree 81eca126041caf37b91b5d4d20a2b2c3c7007586\nparent 81a2ccd5ee14417705f9dd78b67514e953e975d5\nauthor Halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1776507107 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1776507107 +0300\n\nfix(render): write_kv_if_present explicit return 0 — silent script death fix (#477)\n\n2026-04-18 Drift #2 rehearsal FAIL root cause (Codex thread 019da008 deep review):\n\nPrevious:\n  write_kv_if_present() {\n    local file=\"$1\" key=\"$2\" val=\"$3\"\n    [[ -n \"${val}\" ]] && write_kv \"${file}\" \"${key}\" \"${val}\"\n  }\n\nWhen val is empty, `[[ -n \"\" ]]` returns false → `&&` short-circuits →\nfunction''s last command exit code is 1 → with `set -euo pipefail`, the\nscript DIES SILENTLY at the first empty-val call. No stderr, no mv, no\noutput file finalization.\n\nObserved failure: rehearsal deploy 24601989117 failed at deploy-backend.sh\nline 175 (render-backend-env-approle.sh exit=1) with NO render output in\nlog. Staging Vault KV has drifted schema (`spring.datasource.username` vs\nexpected `user`), so `kv_get_value \"${auth_db_payload}\" url` returned\nempty → first `write_kv_if_present AUTH_SERVICE_DB_URL \"\"` killed script.\n\nFix:\n  write_kv_if_present() {\n    local file=\"$1\" key=\"$2\" val=\"$3\"\n    if [[ -n \"${val}\" ]]; then\n      write_kv \"${file}\" \"${key}\" \"${val}\"\n    fi\n    return 0\n  }\n\nExplicit `return 0` ensures the \"empty = skip\" contract survives errexit.\nPer-service DB paths can now genuinely fall back to shared POSTGRES_USER/\nPASSWORD as the comment promises.\n\nNote: the underlying schema drift (`spring.datasource.*` vs `url/user/\npassword`) is a separate concern and will be addressed in a follow-up —\nthe current fix unblocks render so the shared-creds fallback path works.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp41jjCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABngQAJ6+vfwgyR8LFv/0W1JbT+LB\n/zO+NuBKomIfHK5UowyzV9ODCYClUEWjHMbDUhxq3EACI6opAnAU8NoDrfO08+9u\nmWuG4k0IynJsDE8oVZGIZO74fgIc4hvV211WgnQlfS4fQTFmf04Xb6Yxk+0hXVNF\nrRQ2D0sfXp73vbI2KxJabUT92Yfy6EwJqThDBilP33e9Z1bgOIbsouxeolCzcPE9\nlT5IV/yfStdEIiI1PCfgEprTHeid01LjHtYB25CUujuUjQ1H9L3/K9KdEYxjifNV\nOOxamnIwUGyQITZry7AaDaIowlogjN8njM8AvW48JvekNSQbv2cg+UzEoRdfLBej\n3DEtd7X0BrAItiSdhl6h4/uITZD8RaEGTpPU6kB5Cqqli2lizxPBwDSqcLOf9R0s\n+NPZb3W4p42fWcDYqBKa4PNbasJwt3meqV3ee7eAnQvZDvqDLFBzXv0apKz5Ufrg\nelSztl9H3zwcC5oGdCpV3ilnlRJ7t09UzcPHSNVAjIZ16phZZMQmouaJgHXBrPZE\nKMQu192NCCZ7pz/JIcy9W8Gd2omJ6ySSdsxeSFrUABxtV254j2F1AImCJAQVWg83\n4psOu0E1SuCPt91MM7iQFPhiFmO9LiATPy2pWvt0iVOMEnqcWJNUfFnGYv42jg42\ng2t30jC7WGL0bPK1Utq3\n=72pt\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-18T10:11:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commit/1b66a0db4774678e1cd741093bd1bf0490386e8f","node_id":"C_kwDOQooUwNoAKDFiNjZhMGRiNDc3NDY3OGUxY2Q3NDEwOTNiZDFiZjA0OTAzODZlOGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commit/81a2ccd5ee14417705f9dd78b67514e953e975d5","sha":"81a2ccd5ee14417705f9dd78b67514e953e975d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/81a2ccd5ee14417705f9dd78b67514e953e975d5"}],"sha":"1b66a0db4774678e1cd741093bd1bf0490386e8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/1b66a0db4774678e1cd741093bd1bf0490386e8f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186576227?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/81a2ccd5ee14417705f9dd78b67514e953e975d5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-18T09:33:54Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"Halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-18T09:33:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(doctor-infra): F5 keycloak postgres-db check flake-free (SIGPIPE+pipefail) (#476)\n\n2026-04-18 OI-02 Option B rehearsal revealed F5 is flaky: same commit SHA\nproduced [PASS] at 08:51 and [FAIL] at 08:57 (deploy runs 24601157204 vs\n24601257956). Failure correlated with `grep: write error: Broken pipe` in\nCI log.\n\nRoot cause: `grep -A5 \"keycloak:\" | grep -q \"postgres-db\"` — when the\nsecond grep found a match early and exited, first grep got SIGPIPE (exit\n141). With `set -o pipefail` active at script-level, this propagated as\nnon-zero → `if` saw false → F5 falsely failed.\n\nAdditional bug: grep matched ALL `keycloak:` occurrences including URL\nreferences (`http://keycloak:8080/...`). Even when passing, the check was\nonly incidentally correct (some later keycloak: match''s -A5 window\naccidentally contained \"postgres-db\").\n\nFix: awk single-process scan anchored to the exact service block header\n`^  keycloak:$`, printing lines until next service header. No pipeline →\nno SIGPIPE → deterministic. No URL matches → correctly validates\nservice-level depends_on semantics.\n\nLocal smoke: repeated runs produce PASS consistently.\n\nCodex review: thread `019d9fe6` advised F5 fix before re-rehearsal rather\nthan \"hope it passes next time\". This PR unblocks Drift #2 rehearsal.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d8e6f43ad18164083ecac7d764c88d36f8ba100e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/trees/d8e6f43ad18164083ecac7d764c88d36f8ba100e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/commits/81a2ccd5ee14417705f9dd78b67514e953e975d5","verification":{"payload":"tree d8e6f43ad18164083ecac7d764c88d36f8ba100e\nparent 50c1fa29051046694722cae6470bb1d48b728207\nauthor Halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1776504834 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1776504834 +0300\n\nfix(doctor-infra): F5 keycloak postgres-db check flake-free (SIGPIPE+pipefail) (#476)\n\n2026-04-18 OI-02 Option B rehearsal revealed F5 is flaky: same commit SHA\nproduced [PASS] at 08:51 and [FAIL] at 08:57 (deploy runs 24601157204 vs\n24601257956). Failure correlated with `grep: write error: Broken pipe` in\nCI log.\n\nRoot cause: `grep -A5 \"keycloak:\" | grep -q \"postgres-db\"` — when the\nsecond grep found a match early and exited, first grep got SIGPIPE (exit\n141). With `set -o pipefail` active at script-level, this propagated as\nnon-zero → `if` saw false → F5 falsely failed.\n\nAdditional bug: grep matched ALL `keycloak:` occurrences including URL\nreferences (`http://keycloak:8080/...`). Even when passing, the check was\nonly incidentally correct (some later keycloak: match''s -A5 window\naccidentally contained \"postgres-db\").\n\nFix: awk single-process scan anchored to the exact service block header\n`^  keycloak:$`, printing lines until next service header. No pipeline →\nno SIGPIPE → deterministic. No URL matches → correctly validates\nservice-level depends_on semantics.\n\nLocal smoke: repeated runs produce PASS consistently.\n\nCodex review: thread `019d9fe6` advised F5 fix before re-rehearsal rather\nthan \"hope it passes next time\". This PR unblocks Drift #2 rehearsal.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp41ACCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4TMQAIRJA9E0ItLrcBLIn8zWiF4k\n1a9wEU4LxCOEqh2oM8Ocr8MGVGctUoEl5Bx3tmbjybRvJ5zLKTZisWJJ80074vAP\nIwkzRB+Jm4rjGqC3zwQ04BeWIzutk+d+dvOpH5SopS5ozfPR2TpJ5/kPZVnD8UHt\nUQpAgvwEwU+tYct4kgP/gMmhmY5F6ym6tSMVFp+X9G8t4oZb8wJd7vYcUGrYWS0e\nO59ykKHFPrkgKkDp5bjo9b5C5r14GLBg9GrUL6WI4mZWYKy9naeRyT8GxOAchl3a\nueSTTw9hU5Z4mBoe4t4DeHO8kjsovddZ0+ra2KQZi4La97Hlg049+m9npGD7QKUQ\n6UkgObjfug+Q6ii/Zp3URxQfNBcBiyZqUS9iXz/mZ5sID5kqVjbUVrNgjR6p2zmp\nnHqo1dBsSN+AxO8RJSxOdLPmidjqochdb8iUL0kwybHsCqEAzPBIhRTMXDA6X94T\noBiQ/LZaydfKV/F5mh62Q5nOTp1YewgU7+W9a/iWwZ1I/