ts/68c47f6ba3f736c0f1ba87590a2711a8884d3908/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-18T07:08:37Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"Halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-18T07:08:37Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(infra): latent drift class guards — issuer/audience contract + OpenFGA idempotency (Codex Thread 3) (#469)\n\n* feat(infra): latent drift class guards — issuer/audience contract + OpenFGA idempotency + doctor-infra L2b (Codex Thread 3)\n\nCodex Thread 3 drift hunt (2026-04-18) identified 5 latent drift classes\npost-502-incident. This PR implements 3 of them; the other 2 (render\npre-deploy flip, KV db/* path check) are deferred to separate PRs per\nCodex''s review recommendation (render flip is breaking-risk, KV db/* is\nscope-adjacent).\n\n**Drift #3 — Issuer/audience check**\n`backend/scripts/vault/check-backend-deploy-stage.sh` `config_required`\nlist now includes SECURITY_JWT_ISSUER, SECURITY_JWT_ISSUERS, and\nSECURITY_AUTH_ALLOWED_CLIENT_IDS. Stage compose fallback points at the\ninternal Keycloak URL (`keycloak:8080/realms/serban`), which rejects\nbrowser tokens minted with the public issuer\n(`https://ai.acik.com/realms/serban`) — silent 401/500. Canonical env\nmust provide these three keys; check-time enforcement prevents drift.\n\n**Drift #5 — OpenFGA init.sh idempotency**\n`backend/openfga/init.sh` rewrote store + model provisioning to lookup-or-\nreuse. Store: if OPENFGA_STORE_ID env is set, verify it exists by ID and\nreuse. Otherwise name-match with exactly-1 uniqueness guard (name is not\nguaranteed unique in OpenFGA; ambiguous results abort rather than guess).\nModel: if OPENFGA_MODEL_ID is set and present in the store, reuse;\notherwise append a new model version (models are append-only, tuples\nremain valid). Previously the script created a new store + model on every\ninvocation, producing ID churn + silent fail-open (\"disabled authz\" → all\nchecks return true).\n\n**doctor-infra L2b expansion (Codex PR #9 review)**\nL2 currently probes permission-service (:8090) for JWT enforcement.\nExpanded to 3 additional services that expose `/api/v1/authz/check`:\napi-gateway (:8080), user-service (:8089), core-data-service (:8092).\nScope deliberately excludes auth-service (:8088) and variant-service\n(:8091) — Codex verified they do not expose this endpoint; probing would\ngenerate 404 noise rather than drift signal.\n\nVerified on staging (2026-04-18):\n  [PASS] L2: Token''sız /authz/check → 401 (JWT zorunlu, permitAll kapalı)\n  [PASS] L2b-gateway: Token''sız /authz/check → 401 (JWT zorunlu)\n  [PASS] L2b-user-service: Token''sız /authz/check → 401 (JWT zorunlu)\n  [PASS] L2b-core-data-service: Token''sız /authz/check → 401 (JWT zorunlu)\n\nOut of scope (planned follow-ups):\n- Drift #1 (doc parity README 8082) → merged via PR #467\n- Drift #2 (render pre-deploy flip) → separate PR, operational-risk flip\n- Drift #4 (KV db/* + jwt/auth-service path check) → separate PR\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(contract,openfga): FEC contract coverage + tuple seed idempotency note (CI unblock + Codex PR #469 review)\n\n- FEC contract (`extensions/PRJ-PM-SUITE/contract/feature_execution_contract.v1.json`)\n  `delivery_scope.change_path_globs` did not include `backend/openfga/init.sh`\n  → enforcement-check blocking FAIL on scoped_changed_files_count=3 with\n  errors=1 (`delivery_scope:uncovered_change`). Added; local re-run OK.\n- `backend/openfga/init.sh` §5 tuple seed: Codex PR #469 review noted\n  store/model are idempotent but seed tuples re-write blindly. Added\n  explicit NOTE block explaining intentional seed-once semantics —\n  duplicate-write 4xx IS the correct drift signal (operator should use\n  `fga tuple write` CLI which short-circuits duplicates, or clear store).\n  No behavior change; documentation only (store/model reuse path remains\n  the safe re-entry).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4d5860af6642821744fe1d207c46085d32e3a438","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/trees/4d5860af6642821744fe1d207c46085d32e3a438"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/commits/68c47f6ba3f736c0f1ba87590a2711a8884d3908","verification":{"payload":"tree 4d5860af6642821744fe1d207c46085d32e3a438\nparent 30b1973aeddf3819cdf252bfb150b930d567c886\nauthor Halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1776496117 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1776496117 +0300\n\nfeat(infra): latent drift class guards — issuer/audience contract + OpenFGA idempotency (Codex Thread 3) (#469)\n\n* feat(infra): latent drift class guards — issuer/audience contract + OpenFGA idempotency + doctor-infra L2b (Codex Thread 3)\n\nCodex Thread 3 drift hunt (2026-04-18) identified 5 latent drift classes\npost-502-incident. This PR implements 3 of them; the other 2 (render\npre-deploy flip, KV db/* path check) are deferred to separate PRs per\nCodex''s review recommendation (render flip is breaking-risk, KV db/* is\nscope-adjacent).\n\n**Drift #3 — Issuer/audience check**\n`backend/scripts/vault/check-backend-deploy-stage.sh` `config_required`\nlist now includes SECURITY_JWT_ISSUER, SECURITY_JWT_ISSUERS, and\nSECURITY_AUTH_ALLOWED_CLIENT_IDS. Stage compose fallback points at the\ninternal Keycloak URL (`keycloak:8080/realms/serban`), which rejects\nbrowser tokens minted with the public issuer\n(`https://ai.acik.com/realms/serban`) — silent 401/500. Canonical env\nmust provide these three keys; check-time enforcement prevents drift.\n\n**Drift #5 — OpenFGA init.sh idempotency**\n`backend/openfga/init.sh` rewrote store + model provisioning to lookup-or-\nreuse. Store: if OPENFGA_STORE_ID env is set, verify it exists by ID and\nreuse. Otherwise name-match with exactly-1 uniqueness guard (name is not\nguaranteed unique in OpenFGA; ambiguous results abort rather than guess).\nModel: if OPENFGA_MODEL_ID is set and present in the store, reuse;\notherwise append a new model version (models are append-only, tuples\nremain valid). Previously the script created a new store + model on every\ninvocation, producing ID churn + silent fail-open (\"disabled authz\" → all\nchecks return true).\n\n**doctor-infra L2b expansion (Codex PR #9 review)**\nL2 currently probes permission-service (:8090) for JWT enforcement.\nExpanded to 3 additional services that expose `/api/v1/authz/check`:\napi-gateway (:8080), user-service (:8089), core-data-service (:8092).\nScope deliberately excludes auth-service (:8088) and variant-service\n(:8091) — Codex verified they do not expose this endpoint; probing would\ngenerate 404 noise rather than drift signal.\n\nVerified on staging (2026-04-18):\n  [PASS] L2: Token''sız /authz/check → 401 (JWT zorunlu, permitAll kapalı)\n  [PASS] L2b-gateway: Token''sız /authz/check → 401 (JWT zorunlu)\n  [PASS] L2b-user-service: Token''sız /authz/check → 401 (JWT zorunlu)\n  [PASS] L2b-core-data-service: Token''sız /authz/check → 401 (JWT zorunlu)\n\nOut of scope (planned follow-ups):\n- Drift #1 (doc parity README 8082) → merged via PR #467\n- Drift #2 (render pre-deploy flip) → separate PR, operational-risk flip\n- Drift #4 (KV db/* + jwt/auth-service path check) → separate PR\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(contract,openfga): FEC contract coverage + tuple seed idempotency note (CI unblock + Codex PR #469 review)\n\n- FEC contract (`extensions/PRJ-PM-SUITE/contract/feature_execution_contract.v1.json`)\n  `delivery_scope.change_path_globs` did not include `backend/openfga/init.sh`\n  → enforcement-check blocking FAIL on scoped_changed_files_count=3 with\n  errors=1 (`delivery_scope:uncovered_change`). Added; local re-run OK.\n- `backend/openfga/init.sh` §5 tuple seed: Codex PR #469 review noted\n  store/model are idempotent but seed tuples re-write blindly. Added\n  explicit NOTE block explaining intentional seed-once semantics —\n  duplicate-write 4xx IS the correct drift signal (operator should use\n  `fga tuple write` CLI which short-circuits duplicates, or clear store).\n  No behavior change; documentation only (store/model reuse path remains\n  the safe re-entry).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp4y31CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsgAQAAeISYAhV9vT/51sd6froT5a\ng/g6ssKqhd54AklJFaAfLBg2KOWsFZrhlDjcCf4u33wzvDQxEGN81fWcpBugOZsn\ntK14lQWD79jAQHArGg9fbWR67lXfrUlqCcMy9vheZPuRXpqlcgMkLG8RHNfzTOmc\nwnM6RjQgDFx3JunMsPHjBiV4VSltZTSgvsdTIWG7S2VAaYdV6TTvVPYIBDf3TvmD\njZqzwOhLL3CuI60r35fbHKMK3jp9JcxY6ofP3WDXCzD4XOD7GhhnYiAA9+YKHcr5\n3tAwbKgPB2Ig6iV3t02QjWVrpoSPVtGsDTi5FbsaSDqDhcIo0QrkMNCF1StZKeD/\nLFSGOvAYnIsPN78xYy0uTosT4Xzvy+Hzx2QMsMeNdaMa5LjTZjh/gls3ETKGb1wc\nsioG7qOf2U6WjKcye6d/Xc/JJf0Q6lA9LX7IqnzG3ZUtJ0Y+pECY06M2o7sUwaBc\n15IqSmrf0ArSHQUOThiCubx+9uQB7JWgeA2+UNNFIhyXSF4Q6o4d3kJ2YZHTcl0F\ngfl4oRYiDkzZtvxB6yuMmFWgrJFZSau3i1x75R0GWto6GZYNgz8wwxMwYfjH69fQ\nsGVmfCOUZ6htGKToI1cFaxOFL5/LeLAXkBP0TCz30ickIsrw4xZlN3vTJ75cjpir\n8V7BXjuglW9ciN7djtlw\n=7+8+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-18T07:08:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commit/68c47f6ba3f736c0f1ba87590a2711a8884d3908","node_id":"C_kwDOQooUwNoAKDY4YzQ3ZjZiYTNmNzM2YzBmMWJhODc1OTBhMjcxMWE4ODg0ZDM5MDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commit/30b1973aeddf3819cdf252bfb150b930d567c886","sha":"30b1973aeddf3819cdf252bfb150b930d567c886","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/30b1973aeddf3819cdf252bfb150b930d567c886"}],"sha":"68c47f6ba3f736c0f1ba87590a2711a8884d3908","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/68c47f6ba3f736c0f1ba87590a2711a8884d3908"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186576227?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/30b1973aeddf3819cdf252bfb150b930d567c886/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-18T07:01:48Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"Halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-18T07:01:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(doctor-infra): Section M robustness refactor (Codex PR #466 review MAJOR) (#468)\n\n* fix(doctor-infra): Section M robustness refactor (Codex PR #466 review MAJOR)\n\nCodex post-merge review flagged three robustness gaps in PR #466 Section M.\nThis commit addresses all three per the review''s recommended approach:\n\nM1 (Docker port detection):\n- Before: `docker inspect --format ''{{range ...PortBindings...}}''` — fragile\n  Go template binding to an internal Docker API struct; format breaks on\n  Docker version bumps and mis-selects multi-bind (IPv4 + IPv6) cases.\n- After: `docker port CONTAINER 8080/tcp` — the official Docker CLI pattern,\n  parsed with awk to tolerate IPv4 `0.0.0.0:8080`, IPv6 `:::8080`, and\n  multi-bind output. Format-stable across Docker versions.\n\nM2 (nginx upstream parsing):\n- Before: file-based awk matching only `location /api/ { ... proxy_pass ... }`.\n  False-negatives on `location /api {` (no trailing slash), regex variants\n  `location ~* ^/api/`, envsubst/include-generated config, and refactors\n  that move the block.\n- After: primary path uses `docker exec platform-web-nginx nginx -T` which\n  renders the effective runtime config (what the server actually uses).\n  awk parser normalizes optional location modifiers (=, ~, ~*, ^~) and\n  trailing slashes, matching the canonical URI `/api`. Static-file fallback\n  (WARN-level) kept for when container/-T is unavailable.\n\nM3 (TLS verify posture):\n- Before: `curl -k ... https://ai.acik.com/...` — TLS verify disabled\n  unconditionally. Dangerous if script is reused in prod contexts where\n  cert guards matter.\n- After: default is verified TLS. Operator must explicitly opt in to\n  insecure mode via `DOCTOR_INFRA_INSECURE_LIVE_SMOKE=1` (stage self-signed\n  cert scenarios). Live smoke can also be fully skipped via\n  `DOCTOR_INFRA_SKIP_LIVE_SMOKE=1`. Error messaging guides operator to the\n  right flag when verified TLS fails.\n\nVerified on staging (2026-04-18, post-PR #466 deploy):\n  [PASS] M1: api-gateway host port binding → 8080 (stage compose reality)\n  [PASS] M2: nginx /api upstream → 127.0.0.1:8080 (matches gateway bind)\n  [PASS] M3: nginx /api/v1/authz/version → 401 (auth gate, route healthy)\n\nM3 passed with default (verified TLS) — staging has Let''s Encrypt cert.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(doctor-infra): M2 regex location anchor normalize (Codex PR #468 review PARTIAL)\n\nCodex post-impl review flagged M2 awk strip missed the regex-case anchor:\n`location ~* ^/api/ {` URI strip left `^/api`, which did not match the\ncanonical `/api`. After trailing-slash normalize, added leading `^` strip\nfor regex anchor. Covers 6 nginx location syntax variants now:\n\n- `location = /api {`         (exact)\n- `location /api {`           (prefix, no slash)\n- `location /api/ {`          (prefix with slash)\n- `location ^~ /api/ {`       (non-regex prefix priority)\n- `location ~ ^/api {`        (regex)\n- `location ~* ^/api/ {`      (regex case-insensitive)\n\nUnit tested locally with awk + fake nginx -T fixtures — all 6 variants\n[MATCHED] correctly.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6fb50315c3cf741f342d9d0565aa31d06696d7e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/trees/6fb50315c3cf741f342d9d0565aa31d06696d7e0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/commits/30b1973aeddf3819cdf252bfb150b930d567c886","verification":{"payload":"tree 6fb50315c3cf741f342d9d0565aa31d06696d7e0\nparent a4b3673b2823a1859695430fa9f80e297c7ab162\nauthor Halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1776495708 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1776495708 +0300\n\nfix(doctor-infra): Section M robustness refactor (Codex PR #466 review MAJOR) (#468)\n\n* fix(doctor-infra): Section M robustness refactor (Codex PR #466 review MAJOR)\n\nCodex post-merge review flagged three robustness gaps in PR #466 Section M.\nThis commit addresses all three per the review''s recommended approach:\n\nM1 (Docker port detection):\n- Before: `docker inspect --format ''{{range ...PortBindings...}}''` — fragile\n  Go template binding to an internal Docker API struct; format breaks on\n  Docker version bumps and mis-selects multi-bind (IPv4 + IPv6) cases.\n- After: `docker port CONTAINER 8080/tcp` — the official Docker CLI pattern,\n  parsed with awk to tolerate IPv4 `0.0.0.0:8080`, IPv6 `:::8080`, and\n  multi-bind output. Format-stable across Docker versions.\n\nM2 (nginx upstream parsing):\n- Before: file-based awk matching only `location /api/ { ... proxy_pass ... }`.\n  False-negatives on `location /api {` (no trailing slash), regex variants\n  `location ~* ^/api/`, envsubst/include-generated config, and refactors\n  that move the block.\n- After: primary path uses `docker exec platform-web-nginx nginx -T` which\n  renders the effective runtime config (what the server actually uses).\n  awk parser normalizes optional location modifiers (=, ~, ~*, ^~) and\n  trailing slashes, matching the canonical URI `/api`. Static-file fallback\n  (WARN-level) kept for when container/-T is unavailable.\n\nM3 (TLS verify posture):\n- Before: `curl -k ... https://ai.acik.com/...` — TLS verify disabled\n  unconditionally. Dangerous if script is reused in prod contexts where\n  cert guards matter.\n- After: default is verified TLS. Operator must explicitly opt in to\n  insecure mode via `DOCTOR_INFRA_INSECURE_LIVE_SMOKE=1` (stage self-signed\n  cert scenarios). Live smoke can also be fully skipped via\n  `DOCTOR_INFRA_SKIP_LIVE_SMOKE=1`. Error messaging guides operator to the\n  right flag when verified TLS fails.\n\nVerified on staging (2026-04-18, post-PR #466 deploy):\n  [PASS] M1: api-gateway host port binding → 8080 (stage compose reality)\n  [PASS] M2: nginx /api upstream → 127.0.0.1:8080 (matches gateway bind)\n  [PASS] M3: nginx /api/v1/authz/version → 401 (auth gate, route healthy)\n\nM3 passed with default (verified TLS) — staging has Let''s Encrypt cert.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(doctor-infra): M2 regex location anchor normalize (Codex PR #468 review PARTIAL)\n\nCodex post-impl review flagged M2 awk strip missed the regex-case anchor:\n`location ~* ^/api/ {` URI strip left `^/api`, which did not match the\ncanonical `/api`. After trailing-slash normalize, added leading `^` strip\nfor regex anchor. Covers 6 nginx location syntax variants now:\n\n- `location = /api {`         (exact)\n- `location /api {`           (prefix, no slash)\n- `location /api/ {`          (prefix with slash)\n- `location ^~ /api/ {`       (non-regex prefix priority)\n- `location ~ ^/api {`        (regex)\n- `location ~* ^/api/ {`      (regex case-insensitive)\n\nUnit tested locally with awk + fake nginx -T fixtures — all 6 variants\n[MATCHED] correctly.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp4yxcCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+KsQAGuaa7nvkhotv8h1Qd5EruBm\nUDGPjT/vUuOp1xTAlsXnHG2dTFwWxErznzhceQCog3xb7Bj1+H+Fmunp0CkmreSZ\niTDc+kxMZ7gxmA9CBb5OHDU08AUZAROlPhXun5XViSf1YH2t3EAtuESdxqTV51pj\no+1cS5WkkNC/4qEyPuYfSUPtQUx4FJ6KzkadvcQHMdNT43ktoDCcLyG+6lDNaPR4\nizP5S2bsbYGkCsz1G+sHIu7vBO0NLgD8FHqENLNFYasWPK2vi5JS1TxRaFw920ur\nLDlki6vLsyDpBvKnsiKs28r/iNFKTlrcBVGEDHyT9zJxK3JTizH2vadTob2qt/ik\nSN3jzj4/sWHAon2cO5InjUgKNoh5u1ZDtqVC09c32XaiLFfeJkFGBgFh89WFfvN7\nfPqrEEC2t88GniDV2pinWYGT/bqpE+pg5SRkA7ZPGidhbD+2f1KKlvWqb7dtcn7f\n/5kjmXokPONM1WmC7mLbn4wZjo3zBvAIA5b