u/platform-ssot/commit/a4b3673b2823a1859695430fa9f80e297c7ab162","node_id":"C_kwDOQooUwNoAKGE0YjM2NzNiMjgyM2ExODU5Njk1NDMwZmE5ZjgwZTI5N2M3YWIxNjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commit/3dcbf52605a6829112d8f2ee7819710af6b809f3","sha":"3dcbf52605a6829112d8f2ee7819710af6b809f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/3dcbf52605a6829112d8f2ee7819710af6b809f3"}],"sha":"a4b3673b2823a1859695430fa9f80e297c7ab162","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/a4b3673b2823a1859695430fa9f80e297c7ab162"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186576227?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/3dcbf52605a6829112d8f2ee7819710af6b809f3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-18T05:49:38Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"Halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-18T05:49:38Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(doctor-infra): Section M — stage port drift guard (2026-04-18 incident) (#466)\n\nAdds three fail-closed checks that catch the class of drift responsible\nfor the 2026-04-18 nginx 502 regression:\n\n- M1: api-gateway container host port binding must be 8080 on stage\n  compose (backend/docker-compose.yml hardcodes `8080:8080`).\n- M2: nginx `location /api/ { ... }` proxy_pass upstream port must\n  match M1''s gateway bind. Mismatch = WEB_GATEWAY_UPSTREAM GH env drift,\n  which produces silent 502 on all /api/* routes including /api/v1/authz.\n  awk regex anchored to exact `/api/` block (not /api/services/ etc).\n- M3: live smoke against https://ai.acik.com/api/v1/authz/version via\n  nginx — 401/403 = healthy (auth gate), 502/503/504 = fail-closed.\n\nTogether these prevent the drift from slipping past deploy into a\nproduction-visible regression; section runs in both --quick and full modes.\n\nIncident backstory: GH env (stage) `WEB_GATEWAY_UPSTREAM=http://127.0.0.1:8082`\ncopied from prod template, but stage compose binds api-gateway at 8080.\nNginx regenerated with 8082 upstream → connection refused → 502 on\nall /api/v1/authz/* routes. Post-deploy-validate also failed because\nBACKEND_HEALTH_URLS secret carried 8082 drift. Both fixed via\n`gh api PATCH` + redeploy; this commit adds the detection so recurrence\nis caught at doctor-infra time rather than in user-facing traffic.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7d4e0ec8074369a082d35ec3d058f386cf26412c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/trees/7d4e0ec8074369a082d35ec3d058f386cf26412c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/commits/3dcbf52605a6829112d8f2ee7819710af6b809f3","verification":{"payload":"tree 7d4e0ec8074369a082d35ec3d058f386cf26412c\nparent 3b91e44c58e99474882090f08b23ba419b653c06\nauthor Halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1776491378 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1776491378 +0300\n\nfeat(doctor-infra): Section M — stage port drift guard (2026-04-18 incident) (#466)\n\nAdds three fail-closed checks that catch the class of drift responsible\nfor the 2026-04-18 nginx 502 regression:\n\n- M1: api-gateway container host port binding must be 8080 on stage\n  compose (backend/docker-compose.yml hardcodes `8080:8080`).\n- M2: nginx `location /api/ { ... }` proxy_pass upstream port must\n  match M1''s gateway bind. Mismatch = WEB_GATEWAY_UPSTREAM GH env drift,\n  which produces silent 502 on all /api/* routes including /api/v1/authz.\n  awk regex anchored to exact `/api/` block (not /api/services/ etc).\n- M3: live smoke against https://ai.acik.com/api/v1/authz/version via\n  nginx — 401/403 = healthy (auth gate), 502/503/504 = fail-closed.\n\nTogether these prevent the drift from slipping past deploy into a\nproduction-visible regression; section runs in both --quick and full modes.\n\nIncident backstory: GH env (stage) `WEB_GATEWAY_UPSTREAM=http://127.0.0.1:8082`\ncopied from prod template, but stage compose binds api-gateway at 8080.\nNginx regenerated with 8082 upstream → connection refused → 502 on\nall /api/v1/authz/* routes. Post-deploy-validate also failed because\nBACKEND_HEALTH_URLS secret carried 8082 drift. Both fixed via\n`gh api PATCH` + redeploy; this commit adds the detection so recurrence\nis caught at doctor-infra time rather than in user-facing traffic.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp4xtyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALbcQAKeIMnW3NBkwfHfBXmTkjYoJ\n2j+KjkKorOQNd2V2SLDQAeCzbnHFmMFY3M51Yshz7jMov6iMknN2rg5Q1+Bng944\nm7wlwbMZb/IfqpVnHPFvDWvPGt6Ro2Fu83qnvxnxUdhhiYrvnaxfaYCqVd5yioSo\nyJ2jZcOkwVhcgYUdub93zdFRoUKA3VKsVXb25RBDl5dOaAp+hW+lSx9w4sXD0Fee\nyiou0PAWp0V8L/Ii3Y4Mzd9iU40ez07s4hyqsxN02RLNTJs4ZjNeNPai/lITCgKq\nbgT+q4CLO5vh/2wv6MqtvpitTpWYLJoaRw8M8ASPWeUl0e163VjvjMdltQiUYp/m\nXIzFoll8R6MxHyshqynVb0Lel7Yy4apCN61Pg4Z9FdRX5LWRpriFsiMmXowBghPs\nNxUqkc78oez3r8oAbMGF0h1tynnH9oHOgL8bFrv1ndeKw+1/94t2k/KHUcHUp7U0\nPataMwEg0b7CKrcFdSrDQJ5WzKs+KePJbSjKPEodqqA/X19tpxt9yI/lsJT4aA58\nt