/users/Halildeu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/3b91e44c58e99474882090f08b23ba419b653c06/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-18T01:37:19Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"Halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-18T01:37:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(vault): provider rehearsal matrix + escrow drill + break-glass decision tree (P1.10) (#465)\n\nRB-vault-kms-autounseal.md updates for Open Item OI-04 (prod cutover gate):\n\n- §3 provider rehearsal matrix — AWS KMS, GCP KMS, Azure Key Vault,\n  HashiCorp Transit (4-provider parity, dry-run compatible, scope\n  boundary documented).\n- §3 common dry-run checklist (Step A-F): provider key binding,\n  VAULT_SEAL_* env, fresh init with `-recovery-shares=5 -recovery-threshold=3`,\n  3× restart validation, CLI fallback path, fail classification.\n- §5.1 break-glass KMS access failure — 45-minute decision tree\n  (0-5 incident ack → 5-15 severity + restore path → 15-30 IAM restore\n  + key re-enable → 30-45 post-restore smoke → 45+ fresh-init contingency).\n  Decision authority matrix: Platform Eng Lead (commander) + Security Lead\n  (IAM witness). Communication templates included.\n- §5.5 recovery key escrow drill (quarterly cadence) — 5-of-3 recovery\n  share generation, dual escrow (1Password Team Platform + physical safe),\n  `vault operator generate-root -init` flow with OTP decode, root token\n  critical op validation, audit log target (`docs/04-operations/DRILLS/`).\n\nAC-0320 scenario corrections based on Vault 1.21 semantic audit:\n\n- Senaryo 5: \"5-of-3 unseal\" → \"5 recovery share / threshold 3\".\n  Recovery shares are NOT unseal shares under KMS seal (they only\n  authorize `generate-root`). Command syntax corrected:\n  `-key-shares=1 -key-threshold=1 -recovery-shares=5 -recovery-threshold=3`.\n- Senaryo 6: \"manual unseal with recovery keys\" corrected. Recovery\n  shares cannot manually unseal a KMS-sealed Vault. Primary recovery\n  path is IAM/key restore; fresh-init is a last-resort contingency\n  (data loss risk — existing seal inaccessible).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"71c4257f9c031e60a3bfe1fdae23059772be8ac5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/trees/71c4257f9c031e60a3bfe1fdae23059772be8ac5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/commits/3b91e44c58e99474882090f08b23ba419b653c06","verification":{"payload":"tree 71c4257f9c031e60a3bfe1fdae23059772be8ac5\nparent c8318e98ab2f0cb0e304d375fb55136e14698b74\nauthor Halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1776476239 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1776476239 +0300\n\ndocs(vault): provider rehearsal matrix + escrow drill + break-glass decision tree (P1.10) (#465)\n\nRB-vault-kms-autounseal.md updates for Open Item OI-04 (prod cutover gate):\n\n- §3 provider rehearsal matrix — AWS KMS, GCP KMS, Azure Key Vault,\n  HashiCorp Transit (4-provider parity, dry-run compatible, scope\n  boundary documented).\n- §3 common dry-run checklist (Step A-F): provider key binding,\n  VAULT_SEAL_* env, fresh init with `-recovery-shares=5 -recovery-threshold=3`,\n  3× restart validation, CLI fallback path, fail classification.\n- §5.1 break-glass KMS access failure — 45-minute decision tree\n  (0-5 incident ack → 5-15 severity + restore path → 15-30 IAM restore\n  + key re-enable → 30-45 post-restore smoke → 45+ fresh-init contingency).\n  Decision authority matrix: Platform Eng Lead (commander) + Security Lead\n  (IAM witness). Communication templates included.\n- §5.5 recovery key escrow drill (quarterly cadence) — 5-of-3 recovery\n  share generation, dual escrow (1Password Team Platform + physical safe),\n  `vault operator generate-root -init` flow with OTP decode, root token\n  critical op validation, audit log target (`docs/04-operations/DRILLS/`).\n\nAC-0320 scenario corrections based on Vault 1.21 semantic audit:\n\n- Senaryo 5: \"5-of-3 unseal\" → \"5 recovery share / threshold 3\".\n  Recovery shares are NOT unseal shares under KMS seal (they only\n  authorize `generate-root`). Command syntax corrected:\n  `-key-shares=1 -key-threshold=1 -recovery-shares=5 -recovery-threshold=3`.\n- Senaryo 6: \"manual unseal with recovery keys\" corrected. Recovery\n  shares cannot manually unseal a KMS-sealed Vault. Primary recovery\n  path is IAM/key restore; fresh-init is a last-resort contingency\n  (data loss risk — existing seal inaccessible).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp4uBPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3h0QACYb8FgpcGMPFVOwi3P/zMTA\nvegG7SSWREmKxM89rFf2XJ7yFlcQxUMd7ErqarRDlf4t6N630OY64KnQw0WQidxT\nMAg6Mntxp+FxmB5EM3xrqnqW6iPL2z6wCXBHBoc7a9HW9QGoOSkZQubcht8AzYU1\nWAb1ruatD5Py0KZgNzYSBSeqUYwPMgRbFuT/6U0XnyIyN1ExnXRjTPsUZTKDA5De\n9Go/fxCyn+tPGTymoJbo8HXJSVCpGyexOaThzg/gE2wSsEEtjWiOxg8AkpVP2F/3\naAVsNkzWigeGbmFuRQP+cffNSIqnh5qqVnDOVzmRymxYaQimlWHMujAubbwsBVKT\n1zzlH+gS4qK+nBx7ky3nLZr9XAnVm0/6b+fb0rI/Lckg4tQe2IuUtWU5OjNVUyKL\n6aHADA7S7qCKX6V/nX+9gvwsOYZ00UP2p8nv1b8S+vjxo5arn05OOEBfUXqlTj85\nyE0Y2CsnHpkS3gb+drza+nWA3g5YtJPMXtqK/skbweCO5Fh4b5S26LDoReQjDy3o\nrRL5D