rs/Halildeu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Halildeu","id":186576227,"login":"Halildeu","node_id":"U_kgDOCx7tYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Halildeu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/commits/c8318e98ab2f0cb0e304d375fb55136e14698b74/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-18T01:30:43Z","email":"halildeu@gmail.com","name":"Halildeu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-18T01:30:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(deploy): document stage WEB_GATEWAY_UPSTREAM → 8080 drift (nginx 502 incident) (#464)\n\nRoot cause: stage GH env `WEB_GATEWAY_UPSTREAM=http://127.0.0.1:8082` but\nstage compose hardcodes `api-gateway: 8080:8080`. Nginx regenerated with\n8082 upstream → connect refused → 502 on /api/v1/authz/*.\n\nLive fix applied via `gh api ... -X PATCH WEB_GATEWAY_UPSTREAM=8080` +\nworkflow re-run. This commit adds guardrail docs so the drift cannot\nsilently return:\n\n- `backend/docker-compose.yml`: comment clarifies stage vs prod semantics\n  (stage hardcoded 8080, prod uses `API_GATEWAY_PORT` via prod compose).\n- `backend/.env.prod.example`: STAGE NOTES block warns operators that\n  `API_GATEWAY_PORT=8082` is prod-only; copying as-is to stage canonical\n  env is inert but misleading.\n- `RB-staging-prod-profile.md` §5 nginx /api/* 502 runbook updated with\n  5-step resolution (Step A-E) based on 2026-04-18 incident playbook.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f27246ca58a187e9de21da9c83099d556015936e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/trees/f27246ca58a187e9de21da9c83099d556015936e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Halildeu/platform-ssot/git/commits/c8318e98ab2f0cb0e304d375fb55136e14698b74","verification":{"payload":"tree f27246ca58a187e9de21da9c83099d556015936e\nparent 64e1ddb79db968424424610e8db8f7973f44899a\nauthor Halildeu <halildeu@gmail.com> 1776475843 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1776475843 +0300\n\nfix(deploy): document stage WEB_GATEWAY_UPSTREAM → 8080 drift (nginx 502 incident) (#464)\n\nRoot cause: stage GH env `WEB_GATEWAY_UPSTREAM=http://127.0.0.1:8082` but\nstage compose hardcodes `api-gateway: 8080:8080`. Nginx regenerated with\n8082 upstream → connect refused → 502 on /api/v1/authz/*.\n\nLive fix applied via `gh api ... -X PATCH WEB_GATEWAY_UPSTREAM=8080` +\nworkflow re-run. This commit adds guardrail docs so the drift cannot\nsilently return:\n\n- `backend/docker-compose.yml`: comment clarifies stage vs prod semantics\n  (stage hardcoded 8080, prod uses `API_GATEWAY_PORT` via prod compose).\n- `backend/.env.prod.example`: STAGE NOTES block warns operators that\n  `API_GATEWAY_PORT=8082` is prod-only; copying as-is to stage canonical\n  env is inert but misleading.\n- `RB-staging-prod-profile.md` §5 nginx /api/* 502 runbook updated with\n  5-step resolution (Step A-E) based on 2026-04-18 incident playbook.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp4t7DCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAT6IQACJlOBTlZgduZ0bxC4qpLHPl\n29j56IawumGj9lIGYLFyEQZWTPeuQp0sWGSv/+QrsqtxrJ/H+Ft/3e9ZovRJsW5y\ncB7nyosJ0AoQqfbpKleNRSAJc2UbRMlbu42dNcK2eW6d+9g1jALjA9lLkRo+6fr0\n0hjWhlzIzQGp+wTxSCLIID/6AmVLywki2ihBg7CliHaWTgfcJ2HspGZJcRtS3MP4\nTPMEe0waIWCoHIri4IY6EcFgVBC2k0p817lq9nptZOALE00F+G1rX