he LMS because all other\n      services and MFE rely on oauth to authenticate with the LMS so we\n      just end up turning this on later in the settings stack.\n\n* We use it to only run certain oauth_dispatch tests in the LMS test\n  environment because the oauth_dispatch app is not installed in the\n  CMS.\n    * We use the `skip_unless_lms` decorator now instead to do this or\n      just run the tests in both suites because they are valid tests in\n      both contexts.","tree":{"sha":"9a832e7eb2a336d07a276d2af4c84a714072a3f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m3hrab/edx-platform/git/trees/9a832e7eb2a336d07a276d2af4c84a714072a3f6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m3hrab/edx-platform/git/commits/92a47097b7cd46e89d0b17f51e02a4bd069832c3","verification":{"payload":"tree 9a832e7eb2a336d07a276d2af4c84a714072a3f6\nparent 7cd4170ca7bfd29612fe4b8b469df539d64e327f\nauthor Feanil Patel <feanil@axim.org> 1761937371 -0400\ncommitter Feanil Patel <feanil@axim.org> 1762192446 -0500\n\nfeat: Drop the ENABLE_OAUTH2_PROVIDER flag.\n\nThis setting was not actually not changing installation behavior, that\nis being set by whether oauth_dispatch is in INSTALLED_APPS or not.\n\nThis flag was being used to:\n\n* Hide enable/disable certain URL paths.\n    * We need these paths on all the time in the LMS because all other\n      services and MFE rely on oauth to authenticate with the LMS so we\n      just end up turning this on later in the settings stack.\n\n* We use it to only run certain oauth_dispatch tests in the LMS test\n  environment because the oauth_dispatch app is not installed in the\n  CMS.\n    * We use the `skip_unless_lms` decorator now instead to do this or\n      just run the tests in both suites because they are valid tests in\n      both contexts.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgDFYRWaLkJgizbOvA88L1WtWKAr\nP17funxYmxKSkYVCkAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQN+