64e327f"}],"sha":"7f0375b6b9064adbe34f1641ba008518c25df971","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m3hrab/edx-platform/commits/7f0375b6b9064adbe34f1641ba008518c25df971"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/59769569?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Serj-N/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Serj-N/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Serj-N/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Serj-N/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Serj-N","id":59769569,"login":"Serj-N","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5NzY5NTY5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Serj-N/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Serj-N/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Serj-N/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Serj-N/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Serj-N/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Serj-N","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m3hrab/edx-platform/commits/7cd4170ca7bfd29612fe4b8b469df539d64e327f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-10-30T21:23:49Z","email":"59769569+Serj-N@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Serhiii Nanai"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-10-30T21:23:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: [FC-0092] Optimize Course Info Blocks API (#37122)\n\nThe Course Info Blocks API endpoint has been known to be rather slow\nto return the response. Previous investigation showed that the major\ntime sink was the get_course_blocks function, which is called three\ntimes in a single request. This commit aims to improve the response\ntimes by reducing the number of times that this function is called.\n\nSolution Summary\n\nThe first time the function get_course_blocks is called, the result\n(transformed course blocks) is stored in the current WSGI request\nobject. Later in the same request, before the second get_course_blocks\ncall is triggered, the already transformed course blocks are taken\nfrom the request object, and if they are available, get_course_blocks\nis not called (if not, it is called as a fallback). Later in the\nrequest, the function is called again as before (see Optimization\nStrategy and Difficulties).\n\nOptimization Strategy and Difficulties\n\nThe original idea was to fetch and transform the course blocks once\nand reuse them in all three cases, which would reduce get_course_blocks\ncall count to 1. However, this did not turn out to be a viable solution\nbecause of the arguments passed to get_course_blocks. Notably, the\nallow_start_dates_in_future boolean flag affects the behavior of\nStartDateTransformer, which is a filtering transformer modifying the\nblock structure returned.\n\nThe first two times allow_start_dates_in_future is False, the third\ntime it is True. Setting it to True in all three cases would mean that\nsome blocks would be incorrectly included in the response.\n\nThis left us with one option - optimize the first two calls. The\ndifference between the first two calls is the non-filtering\ntransformers, however the second call applies a subset of transformers\nfrom the first call, so it was safe to apply the superset of\ntransformers in both cases. This allowed to reduce the number of\nfunction calls to 2. However, the cached structure may be further\nmutated by filters downstream, which means we need to cache a copy of\nthe course structure (not the structure itself). The copy method itself\nis quite heavy (it calls deepcopy three times), making the benefits of\nthis solution much less tangible. In fact, another potential\noptimization that was considered was to reuse the collected block\nstructure (pre-transformation), but since calling copy on a collected\nstructure proved to be more time-consuming than calling get_collected,\nthis change was discarded, considering that the goal is to improve\nperformance.\n\nRevised Solution\n\nTo achieve a more tangible performance improvement, it was decided to\nmodify the previous strategy as follows:\n\n* Pass a for_blocks_view parameter to the get_blocks function to make\n  sure the new caching logic only affects the blocks view.\n* Collect and cache course blocks with future dates included.\n* Include start key in requested fields.\n* Reuse the cached blocks in the third call, which is in\n  get_course_assignments\n* Before returning the response, filter out any blocks with a future\n  start date, and also remove the start key if it was not in requested\n  fields","tree":{"sha":"7f5fa9b697c51a1e3b98d7531d38b682659492fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m3hrab/edx-platform/git/trees/7f5fa9b697c51a1e3b98d7531d38b682659492fb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m3hrab/edx-platform/git/commits/7cd4170ca7bfd29612fe4b8b469df539d64e327f","verification":{"payload":"tree 7f5fa9b697c51a1e3b98d7531d38b682659492fb\nparent ec1d9593d91ea147322561fd80e1e3844921da8f\nauthor Serhiii Nanai <59769569+Serj-N@users.noreply.github.com> 1761859429 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1761859429 -0400\n\nfeat: [FC-0092] Optimize Course Info Blocks API (#37122)\n\nThe Course Info Blocks API endpoint has been known to be rather slow\nto return the response. Previous investigation showed that the major\ntime sink was the get_course_blocks function, which is called three\ntimes in a single request. This commit aims to improve the response\ntimes by reducing the number of times that this function is called.\n\nSolution Summary\n\nThe first time the function get_course_blocks is called, the result\n(transformed course blocks) is stored in the current WSGI request\nobject. Later in the same request, before the second get_course_blocks\ncall is triggered, the already transformed course blocks are taken\nfrom the request object, and if they are available, get_course_blocks\nis not called (if not, it is called as a fallback). Later in the\nrequest, the function is called again as before (see Optimization\nStrategy and Difficulties).\n\nOptimization Strategy and Difficulties\n\nThe original idea was to fetch and transform the course blocks once\nand reuse them in all three cases, which would reduce get_course_blocks\ncall count to 1. However, this did not turn out to be a viable solution\nbecause of the arguments passed to get_course_blocks. Notably, the\nallow_start_dates_in_future boolean flag affects the behavior of\nStartDateTransformer, which is a filtering transformer modifying the\nblock structure returned.\n\nThe first two times allow_start_dates_in_future is False, the third\ntime it is True. Setting it to True in all three cases would mean that\nsome blocks would be incorrectly included in the response.\n\nThis left us with one option - optimize the first two calls. The\ndifference between the first two calls is the non-filtering\ntransformers, however the second call applies a subset of transformers\nfrom the first call, so it was safe to apply the superset of\ntransformers in both cases. This allowed to reduce the number of\nfunction calls to 2. However, the cached structure may be further\nmutated by filters downstream, which means we need to cache a copy of\nthe course structure (not the structure itself). The copy method itself\nis quite heavy (it calls deepcopy three times), making the benefits of\nthis solution much less tangible. In fact, another potential\noptimization that was considered was to reuse the collected block\nstructure (pre-transformation), but since calling copy on a collected\nstructure proved to be more time-consuming than calling get_collected,\nthis change was discarded, considering that the goal is to improve\nperformance.\n\nRevised Solution\n\nTo achieve a more tangible performance improvement, it was decided to\nmodify the previous strategy as follows:\n\n* Pass a for_blocks_view parameter to the get_blocks function to make\n  sure the new caching logic only affects the blocks view.\n* Collect and cache course blocks with future dates included.\n* Include start key in requested fields.\n* Reuse the cached blocks in the third call, which is in\n  get_course_assignments\n* Before returning the response, filter out any blocks with a future\n  start date, and also remove the start key if it was not in requested\n  fields","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpA9dlCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAySsQAABL2mQDpyWjXWLYCfdDJ931\nc8SC2y09EE7H3fpaF23VmyEBPuNuNM+08nAaDp+5MpdeRF7WfFpvBtRALXpNAyDp\nn7mG9udVUJbgTge9WtIKaOo1udr+2TUn5wEisZjpCFnLX8tw2yEqRmru53r7L8Z+\nvFqCvNWWrUc65BfwSR61PhjzG71OXK7IQEbPcrTweea3h5aPP4+FMo0Cy/Ky8oGS\nnW19lYAboSdx6IxP8o1gwXqTnZGQE8KfnIZTJQxI1Nd17QBrnrYRjAHoXVsE7Ybi\n2kH8BNBOoQdarqbHEdv5y4n1rBu5X9EMv08+1kQSvzo+lghLrwkxZDLdzb2zTbvr\nrU+NzLzMmbmV2KrvIeBhi3Ebp6ehgL32EdxdOFch8+SA67Hno7MGOslRTkHPG5Bz\nvdwruFHmRNrcRCm1EsJWaPnD6OJBUk4dE7I/mMQJ2eKWnMYMdQy2EyJpFuOKfHLo\ns2pZ2GDuFuecxBpz1PYlnTnCIc0qYH+I0FEXzfIv8afPZ3/XoDb5LoGhQ9cOFOLJ\nKB0EEwwnSZAC/rFq3LzBj9L5pWMHzcNOxfpgD/RjhHbdozyAA2M42IGnQA1D2q+H\nBObeQXDFeVoI5zOiQfXiyYYUTG9CRhBIHG8OaFsG8+qn+JkdnsF+z67x7H/g7UUU\nbw1iKUxv/SBv1CtgjmT5\n=1P6U\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2025-10-30T21:23:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/m3hrab/edx-platform/commit/7cd4170ca7bfd29612fe4b8b469df539d64e327f","node_id":"C_kwDOQotp2NoAKDdjZDQxNzBjYTdiZmQyOTYxMmZlNGI4YjQ2OWRmNTM5ZDY0ZTMyN2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/m3hrab/edx-platform/commit/ec1d9593d91ea147322561fd80e1e3844921da8f","sha":"ec1d9593d91ea147322561fd80e1e3844921da8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m3hrab/edx-platform/commits/ec1d9593d91ea147322561fd80e1e3844921da8f"}],"sha":"7cd4170ca7bfd29612fe4b8b469df539d64e327f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m3hrab/edx-platform/commits/7cd4170ca7bfd29612fe4b8b469df539d64e327f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/781561?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feanil/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feanil/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feanil/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feanil/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/feanil","id":781561,"login":"feanil","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4MTU2MQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feanil/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feanil/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feanil/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feanil/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feanil/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/feanil","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m3hrab/edx-platform/commits/af8c62684b6d7c5cbda7da710e1a4714fee44161/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-10-30T18:40:04Z","email":"feanil@axim.org","name":"Feanil Patel"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-10-30T18:40:04Z","email":"feanil@axim.org","name":"Feanil Patel"},"message":"build: Remove edx-name-affirmation from the exception list.\n\nThis should prevent it from accidentally getting added back to the\ndefault build.","tree":{"sha":"f8d68123473a319fe1884cd1c6d932faa014beef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m3hrab/edx-platform/git/trees/f8d68123473a319fe1884cd1c6d932faa014beef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m3hrab/edx-platform/git/commits/af8c62684b6d7c5cbda7da710e1a4714fee44161","verification":{"payload":"tree f8d68123473a319fe1884cd1c6d932faa014beef\nparent 86032c19a07b1be2d229704905f9b9d4535959de\nauthor Feanil Patel <feanil@axim.org> 1761849604 -0400\ncommitter Feanil Patel <feanil@axim.org> 1761849604 -0400\n\nbuild: Remove edx-name-affirmation from the exception list.\n\nThis should prevent it from accidentally getting added back to the\ndefault build.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgDFYRWaLkJgizbOvA88L1WtWKAr\nP17funxYmxKSkYVCkAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQN9I7uV07HBT50uZhA73KxRB8YOnHt0sM4zgI/ZfbBP3wHNVGbvEywhDVsaT8fgvQP\nqF1tFvCvaCrHHC/pwehQ4=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2025-10-30T18:40:38Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/781561?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feanil/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feanil/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feanil/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feanil/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/feanil","id":781561,"login":"feanil","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4MTU2MQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feanil/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feanil/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feanil/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feanil/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feanil/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/feanil","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/m3hrab/edx-platform/commit/af8c62684b6d7c5cbda7da710e1a4714fee44161","node_id":"C_kwDOQotp2NoAKGFmOGM2MjY4NGI2ZDdjNWNiZGE3ZGE3MTBlMWE0NzE0ZmVlNDQxNjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/m3hrab/edx-platform/commit/86032c19a07b1be2d229704905f9b9d4535959de","sha":"86032c19a07b1be2d229704905f9b9d4535959de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m3hrab/edx-platform/commits/86032c19a07b1be2d229704905f9b9d4535959de"}],"sha":"af8c62684b6d7c5cbda7da710e1a4714fee44161","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m3hrab/edx-platform/commits/af8c62684b6d7c5cbda7da710e1a4714fee44161"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/781561?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feanil/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feanil/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feanil/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feanil/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/feanil","id":781561,"login":"feanil","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4MTU2MQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feanil/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feanil/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feanil/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feanil/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feanil/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/feanil","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m3hrab/edx-platform/commits/86032c19a07b1be2d229704905f9b9d4535959de/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-10-30T18:31:06Z","email":"feanil@axim.org","name":"Feanil Patel"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-10-30T18:31:06Z","email":"feanil@axim.org","name":"Feanil Patel"},"message":"test: Remove tests that rely on edx-name-affirmation service being installed\n\nThe service is specific to 2U and should not be installed by default.  When we\ntry to patch objects from that library, that can only be done if the\noriginal object is importable.  So those tests don''t make sense to have\nin the base system which you should be able to run without the\nedx-name-affirmation library.","tree":{"sha":"0afd92ec9db936bfbf567336f055fb3e9928cf71","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m3hrab/edx-platform/git/trees/0afd92ec9db936bfbf567336f055fb3e9928cf71"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m3hrab/edx-platform/git/commits/86032c19a07b1be2d229704905f9b9d4535959de","verification":{"payload":"tree 0afd92ec9db936bfbf567336f055fb3e9928cf71\nparent c2df1500e9c41f6bb8bfc8f6329897a3221d7577\nauthor Feanil Patel <feanil@axim.org> 1761849066 -0400\ncommitter Feanil Patel <feanil@axim.org> 1761849066 -0400\n\ntest: Remove tests that rely on edx-name-affirmation service being installed\n\nThe service is specific to 2U and should not be installed by default.  When we\ntry to patch objects from that library, that can only be done if the\noriginal object is importable.  So those tests don''t make sense to have\nin the base system which you should be able to run without the\nedx-name-affirmation library.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgDFYRWaLkJgizbOvA88L1WtWKAr\nP17funxYmxKSkYVCkAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQPTG2i8SqmUXBkloNP3YAsLeSXj9P9Lr+XKTbbJrCH1k76NOY7dbFIPpsAPd2KaH8l\nAM23x2P/u4dXU54zADQgA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2025-10-30T18:32:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/781561?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feanil/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fe